[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677867 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e31c388-1806-57fb-9cd0-75424b113a0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=- 2 x \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} + \\frac{1}{2} + 2 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677847} {:answer/id #uuid "4349c545-a07e-5d8f-9156-933086c69328" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=x \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} - \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} + \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677853} {:answer/id #uuid "adde3500-6947-53ca-9352-6c57c450cb13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=- 3 x \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} + \\frac{1}{2} + 3 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677863} {:answer/id #uuid "e59cbc0f-3b81-50a2-925e-9c539c3c2cf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\frac{3 x \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}{2} - \\frac{3 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}{2} + \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677868} {:answer/id #uuid "feb78fa5-ffd7-5c5d-b7b7-bfc27f8775d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}{2} - \\frac{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}{2} + \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677871}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677863} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc1f4fe6-ae6e-56ce-84a4-a60a4cc57966" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677866}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e439dc93-b230-57f3-aee3-f899eec8ff28" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y={2}^{-6x+5}$ at the point where $x=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny={2}^{u},\\,u=-6x+5.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}u}={2}^{u}\\ln(2),\\,\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-6.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x} \\\\ & ={2}^{u}\\ln(2)\\cdot (-6) \\\\ & =(-6)\\cdot {2}^{u}\\ln(2) \\\\ & =-6\\cdot {2}^{-6x+5}\\ln(2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at $x=1$, we have to evaluate $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}$ at that point as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\big|_{x=1} & =(-6)\\cdot {2}^{-6(1)+5}\\ln(2) \\\\ & =-6\\cdot {2}^{-1}\\ln(2) \\\\ & =- 3 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $x=1$ is $- 3 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}.$\n\nAlso, the $y$-value of the point on the curve where $x=1$ is\n\n$$\ny_1={2}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we find the equation of the tangent at that point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-y_1&=m(x-x_1) \\\\ y-(\\frac{1}{2})&=(- 3 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)})\\left(x-(1)\\right) \\\\ y&=- 3 x \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} + \\frac{1}{2} + 3 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186678599 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2340bfbd-6513-5e5a-b825-ea1d0a903a8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\left(\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{x}{4} \\right)}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678620} {:answer/id #uuid "40e36773-b19c-53e4-8b18-e20e2eea849f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2\\left(\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{x}{4} \\right)}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678640} {:answer/id #uuid "5ad72e40-4fbc-5f3f-a0b9-6b1a48f7f191" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\left(\\arcsin{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678664} {:answer/id #uuid "6b976a27-703a-5c45-aee1-8e171a3a6108" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4\\left(\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{x}{4} \\right)}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678673} {:answer/id #uuid "da0a0217-3467-50ce-8d39-f984c8c3c4ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\left(\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678731}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186678620} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ac28db8-fac2-59f8-b62d-91aeb124a07e" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678614}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "040cf90f-e9fa-56a3-ad4c-f1af4cb4bd99" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{16 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nChoose the antiderivative. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{4}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{4})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{16 - x^{2}}=4\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{x}{4})^2}.\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=4\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4=2$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{16 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=2\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the supplied primitive:\n\n$$\n2\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=2\\left(\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}\\right)+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n2\\left(\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{x}{4} \\right)}\\right)+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186678633 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18c0ccdc-170c-54ad-a845-5dc98b396090" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\arcsin{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678611} {:answer/id #uuid "30c69d46-ccea-5283-825f-948729033a54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{