$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{4 x}{5}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{4}{5})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n16 x^{2} + 25=25\\left(1+(\\frac{4 x}{5})^2\\right).\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{5}{4}\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{3}{25}\\cdot \\frac{5}{4}=\\frac{3}{20}$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int \\frac{3}{16 x^{2} + 25}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{3}{20}\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the supplied primitive:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{20}\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=\\frac{3}{20}\\left(\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}\\right)+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{20}\\left(\\arctan{\\left(\\frac{4 x}{5} \\right)}\\right)+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186679113 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "974f4491-1b3e-5162-8762-b997c2ce7d0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679152}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186679152} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b20481d-efa0-5d19-bace-b463c668fb4a" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679143}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "2276b7cb-4dac-5fe2-bb8d-8f1bf4683a99" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{-2}^{2} \\frac{3}{x^{2} + 4}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arctan{\\left(-1 \\right)}=- \\frac{\\pi}{4},\\quad \\arctan{\\left(1 \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$.\n\n{{answer}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{2}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\nx^{2} + 4=4\\left(1+(\\frac{x}{2})^2\\right).\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=2\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot 2=\\frac{3}{2}$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=-2&\\Longrightarrow u=-1\\\\x=2&\\Longrightarrow u=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{-2}^{2} \\frac{3}{x^{2} + 4}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\int_{-1}^{1} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the supplied primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\left[\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{-1}^{1}\\right)=\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186679117 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19912f7a-c635-5395-99a4-013d98b0d958" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679111}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186679111} :answer-field/id #uuid "be16bb1a-f6f4-5233-8a1c-d8524f048c88" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679171}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "3de4a265-dec4-55ca-a9f1-ffb48c66ba45" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{-2}^{2} \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{16 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arcsin{\\left(- \\frac{1}{2} \\right)}=- \\frac{\\pi}{6},\\quad \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{1}{2} \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$.\n\n{{answer}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{4}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{4})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{16 - x^{2}}=4\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{x}{4})^2}.\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=4\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4=2$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=-2&\\Longrightarrow u=- \\frac{1}{2}\\\\x=2&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{-2}^{2} \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{16 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=2\\left(\\int_{- \\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the supplied primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n2\\left(\\left[\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{- \\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\right)=2\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186679120 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47cd604e-5003-5beb-a4a5-d9d85cb9390f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679123}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186679123} :answer-field/id #uuid "e94e8786-71eb-5b21-8a20-50168f744c66" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679194}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "45114a62-33d3-51ec-a7c8-28ce8b3500fa" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{-3}^{3} \\frac{3}{x^{2} + 9}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arctan{\\left(-1 \\right)}=- \\frac{\\pi}{4},\\quad \\arctan{\\left(1 \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$.\n\n{{answer}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{3}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{3})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\nx^{2} + 9=9\\left(1+(\\frac{x}{3})^2\\right).\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=3\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 3=1$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=-3&\\Longrightarrow u=-1\\\\x=3&\\Longrightarrow u=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{-3}^{3} \\frac{3}{x^{2} + 9}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\int_{-1}^{1} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the supplied primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{-1}^{1}=\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi}{2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186679127 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21197bf9-2b81-5ac7-8c46-599b9dd9fed0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679112}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186679112} :answer-field/id #uuid "c55102e2-8ac3-5c1e-9026-690c0be8c3ee" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679179}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5b0acf8e-9b1e-5ef1-915d-3d20f3467d5a" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{2} \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{16 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arcsin{\\left(0 \\right)}=0,\\quad \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{1}{2} \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$.\n\n{{answer}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{4}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{4})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{16 - x^{2}}=4\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{x}{4})^2}.\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=4\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $1\\cdot 4=4$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=0\\\\x=2&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{2} \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{16 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=4\\left(\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the supplied primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n4\\left(\\left[\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\right)=4\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186679136 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd50c84e-e76e-5b86-9c45-33afb043d39f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4 \\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679182}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186679182} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d7e8cf9-9c61-5b9f-a08a-ea419798d119" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679124}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "6dc4c518-ea77-5d68-9ae9-a019b2654d65" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{- \\frac{3}{2}}^{\\frac{3}{2}} \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{9 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arcsin{\\left(- \\frac{1}{2} \\right)}=- \\frac{\\pi}{6},\\quad \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{1}{2} \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$.\n\n{{answer}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{3}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{3})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{9 - x^{2}}=3\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{x}{3})^2}.\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=3\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot 3=4$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=- \\frac{3}{2}&\\Longrightarrow u=- \\frac{1}{2}\\\\x=\\frac{3}{2}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{- \\fr