$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arctan{\\left(-1 \\right)}=- \\frac{\\pi}{4},\\quad \\arctan{\\left(1 \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$.\n\n{{answer}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{4}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{4})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\nx^{2} + 16=16\\left(1+(\\frac{x}{4})^2\\right).\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=4\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{1}{16}\\cdot 4=\\frac{1}{4}$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=-4&\\Longrightarrow u=-1\\\\x=4&\\Longrightarrow u=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{-4}^{4} \\frac{1}{x^{2} + 16}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\int_{-1}^{1} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the supplied primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\left[\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{-1}^{1}\\right)=\\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi}{8}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186679198 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98984389-6c56-5627-9dcc-17a55eb70207" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679154}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186679154} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc25e429-ec91-5412-b340-a316818fb8a9" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679205}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f3812e4c-4072-5cbb-aae5-d8098598e7d2" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{3}{2}} \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{9 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arcsin{\\left(0 \\right)}=0,\\quad \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{1}{2} \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$.\n\n{{answer}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{3}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{3})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{9 - x^{2}}=3\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{x}{3})^2}.\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=3\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 3=2$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=0\\\\x=\\frac{3}{2}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{\\frac{3}{2}} \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{9 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=2\\left(\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the supplied primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n2\\left(\\left[\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\right)=2\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi}{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186679722 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b45d82d-d26e-5c68-a136-f5686a3380de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}\\left(\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{4 x}{3} \\right)}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679729} {:answer/id #uuid "1268b773-686b-5e87-a8e0-5956661826c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{4 x}{3} \\right)}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679736} {:answer/id #uuid "153207b8-967f-5f59-bd12-ae5e22b97cd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{4 x}{3} \\right)}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679740} {:answer/id #uuid "97886b89-c7e2-528a-abad-310da5f5c168" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac