:answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 6 x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681515} {:answer/id #uuid "b5552839-979c-52c7-b581-889fc622b022" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 3 x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681534}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186681476} :answer-field/id #uuid "beae62df-011f-5184-98d1-7e004e9cf11b" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681539}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "222d38f5-d071-5e10-b7d2-658568738b16" :question/problem "Suppose we would like to find an **integrating factor** to convert the differential equation\n\n$$\ny'=- 6 x y - 7 x\n$$\n\ninto an exact equation. Select the correct options in the reasoning below. Take $x$ to be real.\n\nFor a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nif\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}=g(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $g(x)$ is independent of $y$, an integrating factor is\n\n$$\nI(x)={{field-2}}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\exp(x)$ denotes $e^x$.\n\nFirst, rewrite our equation in differential form:\n\n$$\n{{field-3}}\n$$\n\nLet's denote\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=6 x y + 7 x,\\qquad Q(x,y)=1\n$$\n\nNow compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}={{field-4}}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}={{field-5}}\n$$\n\nSince\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})={{field-6}}\n$$\n\nis a function of $x$ only, an integrating factor is\n\n$$\nI(x)={{field-7}}\n$$\n\nand multiplication gives the exact equation\n\n$$\n{{field-8}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nif\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})=g(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $g(x)$ is independent of $y$, an integrating factor is\n\n$$\nI(x)=\\exp(\\int g(x)\\,\\text{d}x)\n$$.\n\nHere $\\exp(x)=e^x$.\n\nFirst, rewrite our equation in differential form:\n\n$$\n(6 x y + 7 x)\\,\\text{d}x+\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nLet's denote\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=6 x y + 7 x,\\qquad Q(x,y)=1\n$$\n\nCompute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}(6 x y + 7 x)=6 x \\\\ \\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}(1)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})&=\\frac{1}{1}(6 x-(0)) \\\\ &=6 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a function of $x$ only. Choose the multiplicative constant to be one. Thus\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x)&=\\exp(\\int (6 x)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\ &=\\exp(3 x^{2}) \\\\ &=e^{3 x^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiply the original differential equation by this integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x)((6 x y + 7 x)\\,\\text{d}x+\\,\\text{d}y)&=I(x)\\cdot 0 \\\\ e^{3 x^{2}}((6 x y + 7 x)\\,\\text{d}x+\\,\\text{d}y)&=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186681426 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6be44275-0574-58d0-a729-fc57fe9eb30a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}+\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681466} {:answer/id #uuid "89e5b595-924c-5cb3-a388-399e276667f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681491} {:answer/id #uuid "d94bafee-f6e4-59b3-a267-7a315b9ea010" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681563} {:answer/id #uuid "ef5d7c42-7a56-5cff-82c8-2d447ef49443" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}+\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})" :d