r-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681591} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1165f095-fd53-55b5-848b-aad688ce45bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{- 4 x}((2 y + 7)\\,\\text{d}x+\\,\\text{d}y)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681406} {:answer/id #uuid "7fdd0e05-bcab-5850-bcf6-9f340d4313a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{- 2 x}((2 y + 7)\\,\\text{d}x+\\,\\text{d}y)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681479} {:answer/id #uuid "d6b1827b-55b8-5130-81a8-9e1a5a160e6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{2 x}((2 y + 7)\\,\\text{d}x+\\,\\text{d}y)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681558} {:answer/id #uuid "eb70306e-87a2-5e2f-98f1-7ee062eb293b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{4 x}((2 y + 7)\\,\\text{d}x+\\,\\text{d}y)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681578}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186681558} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb379c9d-6ec6-51ce-909e-b28b54ef822f" :answer-field/key "field-8" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681593}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3388d415-d9f7-515a-acae-b8730ca8fd58" :question/problem "Suppose we would like to find an **integrating factor** to convert the differential equation\n\n$$\ny'=- 2 y - 7\n$$\n\ninto an exact equation. Select the correct options in the reasoning below. Take $x$ to be real.\n\nFor a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nif\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}=g(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $g(x)$ is independent of $y$, an integrating factor is\n\n$$\nI(x)={{field-2}}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\exp(x)$ denotes $e^x$.\n\nFirst, rewrite our equation in differential form:\n\n$$\n{{field-3}}\n$$\n\nLet's denote\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=2 y + 7,\\qquad Q(x,y)=1\n$$\n\nNow compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}={{field-4}}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}={{field-5}}\n$$\n\nSince\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})={{field-6}}\n$$\n\nis a function of $x$ only, an integrating factor is\n\n$$\nI(x)={{field-7}}\n$$\n\nand multiplication gives the exact equation\n\n$$\n{{field-8}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nif\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})=g(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $g(x)$ is independent of $y$, an integrating factor is\n\n$$\nI(x)=\\exp(\\int g(x)\\,\\text{d}x)\n$$.\n\nHere $\\exp(x)=e^x$.\n\nFirst, rewrite our equation in differential form:\n\n$$\n(2 y + 7)\\,\\text{d}x+\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nLet's denote\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=2 y + 7,\\qquad Q(x,y)=1\n$$\n\nCompute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}(2 y + 7)=2 \\\\ \\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}(1)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})&=\\frac{1}{1}(2-(0)) \\\\ &=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a function of $x$ only. Choose the multiplicative constant to be one. Thus\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x)&=\\exp(\\int (2)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\ &=\\exp(2 x) \\\\ &=e^{2 x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiply the original differential equation by this integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x)((2 y + 7)\\,\\text{d}x+\\,\\text{d}y)&=I(x)\\cdot 0 \\\\ e^{2 x}((2 y + 7)\\,\\text{d}x+\\,\\text{d}y)&=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:answer/id #uuid "43d0adbb-b4de-5cd0-bccf-8c9f902ca47e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681437} {:answer/id #uuid "449cecdb-4480-52d4-aba4-17c78b9e2a0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}+\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681438} {:answer/id #uuid "4cc949ce-4bdc-50db-b970-74f29a895251" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}+\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681442} {:answer/id #uuid "6be44275-0574-58d0-a729-fc57fe9eb30a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}+\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681466} {:answer/id #uuid "7e8c7c4e-4500-5cee-bf49-e86d9db15260" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681477} {:answer/id #uuid "805ae835-f697-59cc-868f-b3b9f0b79f55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}+\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681480} {:answer/id #uuid "89e5b595-924c-5cb3-a388-399e276667f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681491} {:answer/id #uuid "9230b092-a187-5bd5-b2a4-d0ae6cbb2091" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}+\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681495} {:answer/id #uuid "93514c91-aa22-515c-b766-be7590e7e81c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681498} {:answer/id #uuid "a8f69811-8338-57b3-817d-80565a8f975f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}+\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681519} {:answer/id #uuid "b7803323-aa3e-5bcb-962d-8fea7e9d80a5" :answer/typ