field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681574} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22233521-2e37-5e17-9592-4a156863e33d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\exp(\\int g(x)\\,\\text{d}x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681417} {:answer/id #uuid "299aac5c-32c6-5589-b557-0e94aa81bf1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\exp(g(x))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681424} {:answer/id #uuid "4ca9a064-4ed8-58e2-9714-95442b755d52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\exp(-g(x))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681441} {:answer/id #uuid "a91e6b06-f8a9-511d-80d9-b640f5435e2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\exp(-\\int g(x)\\,\\text{d}x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681520}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186681417} :answer-field/id #uuid "e98353f0-93a0-5f77-ba68-822093c8792c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681577} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9269f312-6c14-5dde-8173-768917589460" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681496} {:answer/id #uuid "a1766d18-5135-5a8e-bf4d-e2edbbcd0c1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681510} {:answer/id #uuid "a677c5d8-df00-556d-a3cd-fd5a87c9dec9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{15}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681513} {:answer/id #uuid "ee8c92ee-4def-5a03-b135-2441617a773b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681584}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186681510} :answer-field/id #uuid "f625bd36-c935-5d4e-a683-e611935762f9" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681590}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ff416bf9-988a-577d-90f2-5b5cdb25e21b" :question/problem "Suppose we would like to find an **integrating factor** to convert the differential equation\n\n$$\n5 xy'=- 7 x^{2} - 15 y\n$$\n\ninto an exact equation. Select the correct options in the reasoning below. Work on the interval $x>0$.\n\nFor a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nif\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}=g(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $g(x)$ is independent of $y$, an integrating factor is\n\n$$\nI(x)={{field-2}}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\exp(x)$ denotes $e^x$.\n\nFirst, rewrite our equation in differential form:\n\n$$\n{{field-3}}\n$$\n\nLet's denote\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=7 x^{2} + 15 y,\\qquad Q(x,y)=5 x\n$$\n\nNow compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}={{field-4}}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}={{field-5}}\n$$\n\nSince\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})={{field-6}}\n$$\n\nis a function of $x$ only, an integrating factor is\n\n$$\nI(x)={{field-7}}\n$$\n\nand multiplication gives the exact equation\n\n$$\n{{field-8}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nif\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})=g(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $g(x)$ is independent of $y$, an integrating factor is\n\n$$\nI(x)=\\exp(\\int g(x)\\,\\text{d}x)\n$$.\n\nHere $\\exp(x)=e^x$.\n\nFirst, rewrite our equation in differential form:\n\n$$\n(7 x^{2} + 15 y)\\,\\text{d}x+5 x\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nLet's denote\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=7 x^{2} + 15 y,\\qquad Q(x,y)=5 x\n$$\n\nCompute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}(7 x^{2} + 15 y)=15 \\\\ \\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}(5 x)=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})&=\\frac{1}{5 x}(15-(5)) \\\\ &=\\frac{2}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a function of $x$ only. Choose the multiplicative constant to be one. Thus\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x)&=\\exp(\\int \\left(\\frac{2}{x}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\ &=\\exp(2 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}) \\\\ &=x^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn $x>0$, the power rule for logarithms gives $\\exp(k\\ln x)=x^k$.\n\nMultiply the original differential equation by this integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x)((7 x^{2} + 15 y)\\,\\text{d}x+5 x\\,\\text{d}y)&=I(x)\\cdot 0 \\\\ x^{2}((7 x^{2} + 15 y)\\,\\text{d}x+5 x\\,\\text{d}y)&=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682691 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "054aa328-8f57-565a-a206-535421169ab4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682670} {:answer/id #uuid "2687513b-066f-55c8-8dda-f4b34f54727a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3\\left(\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682688} {:answer/id #uuid "76be5748-22da-5774-81d8-207bb26aaee4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\left(\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682718} {:answer/id #uuid "9cd447a8-7e98-5db6-8928-c7f3a26930f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\left(\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{x}{4} \\right)}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682736} {:answer/id #uuid "f20d841d-4f83-51c7-8173-489ea9367416" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\left(\\arcsin{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682774}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682718} :answer-field/id #uuid "dfaeeb09-b347-53b0-904a-10bd23843fbb" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682762}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3142b06d-bcb6-5c1e-8833-2865ec0d326e" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{4 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nChoose the antiderivative. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{2}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{4 - x^{2}}=2\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{x}{2})^2}.\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=2\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot 2=3$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{4 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=3\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\n$$\n3\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=3\\left(\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}\\right)+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n3\\left(\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}\\right)+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682705 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "073c2bd5-178d-5e5e-823d-2e38e6dd56a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{4 x}{5} \\right)}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682671} {:answer/id #uuid "36e3bc7e-3e6b-5063-8190-6803e2a8c0a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{8 x}{5} \\right)}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682692} {:answer/id #uuid "49b64ae9-2f05-59ec-8cd8-c6fc3fd6f7d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{4 x}{5} \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682699} {:answer/id #uuid "6aebfbc6-0dd0-5a4a-a307-07b5285bb523" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\arcsin{\\left(x \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682712} {:answer/id #uuid "b1fe77f6-d9ed-56e4-b6cb-4c46a8a859d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{8 x}{5} \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682742}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682671} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ac6138a-4c7e-5f02-8816-1b474bd6824d" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682681}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "5a421a58-948e-5542-a6c4-c105fa219eee" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{25 - 16 x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nChoose the antiderivative. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{4 x}{5}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{4}{5})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{25 - 16 x^{2}}=5\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{4 x}{5})^2}.\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{5}{4}\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot \\frac{5}{4}=\\frac{1}{2}$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{25 - 16 x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}\\right)+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{4 x}{5} \\right)}\\right)+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682711 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50e18cac-7a33-543e-95e3-3ea2eb889e61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1\\left(\\arcsin{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682701} {:answer/id #uuid "b92d90cc-a214-50e5-b54e-5caf1f7a0b02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{4 x}{3} \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682745} {:answer/id #uuid "c0061cb1-8680-52d6-9d21-78b4ec405974" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{2 x}{3} \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682752} {:answer/id #uuid "e2f48239-3241-574d-bd74-e7019be7d99c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{8 x}{3} \\right)}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682765} {:answer/id #uuid "e3ae4fea-f54e-5655-b37f-72e280bea302" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\left(\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{4 x}{3} \\right)}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682766}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682745} :answer-field/id #uuid "8091343a-bce8-5305-8188-2e61041cbb5a" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682724}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "6ab1dc30-1799-5701-87df-381e5894e2ee" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{9 - 16 x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nChoose the antiderivative. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{4 x}{3}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{4}{3})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{9 - 16 x^{2}}=3\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{4 x}{3})^2}.\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{3}{4}\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}=1$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{9 - 16 x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arcsin{\\left(