le:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=\\frac{2}{3}\\left(\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}\\right)+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}\\left(\\arctan{\\left(\\frac{x}{3} \\right)}\\right)+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682856 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2388702c-c709-5e71-b319-65f7c6725905" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}\\left(\\arctan{\\left(\\frac{x}{10} \\right)}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682799} {:answer/id #uuid "69891e05-07e1-518a-923a-cc87325147cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}\\left(\\arctan{\\left(\\frac{x}{5} \\right)}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682832} {:answer/id #uuid "9a831c8a-c3a0-5828-bcf8-9ef3cdd075b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}\\left(\\arctan{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682854} {:answer/id #uuid "9b8ebd34-531d-53f8-883f-3d6fffede3cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{5}\\left(\\arctan{\\left(\\frac{2 x}{5} \\right)}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682855} {:answer/id #uuid "b29d3634-66b8-50bb-ad32-18466174fbbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{5}\\left(\\arctan{\\left(\\frac{x}{5} \\right)}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682861}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682832} :answer-field/id #uuid "db45237c-e5c8-5a90-a84d-081bbfe6682c" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682879}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9fac851b-355b-5020-8f36-949a9a05aba7" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{4}{x^{2} + 25}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nChoose the antiderivative. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{5}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{5})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\nx^{2} + 25=25\\left(1+(\\frac{x}{5})^2\\right).\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=5\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{4}{25}\\cdot 5=\\frac{4}{5}$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int \\frac{4}{x^{2} + 25}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{4}{5}\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{5}\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=\\frac{4}{5}\\left(\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}\\right)+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{5}\\left(\\arctan{\\left(\\frac{x}{5} \\right)}\\right)+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682872 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0df5c099-d024-592c-9440-7598fa8d7d07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}\\left(\\arctan{\\left(\\frac{x}{6} \\right)}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682788} {:answer/id #uuid "5996abf7-3f2e-55ac-a363-c9ec97c766da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}\\left(\\arctan{\\left(\\frac{2 x}{3} \\right)}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682821} {:answer/id #uuid "6e4d58b0-4239-52fa-9c16-7c50b3af235f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}\\left(\\arctan{\\left(\\frac{x}{3} \\right)}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682833} {:answer/id #uuid "b2dd9e0d-b693-574e-90f2-9e533a86e9f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\left(\\arctan{\\left(\\frac{2 x}{3} \\right)}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682862} {:answer/id #uuid "d4e4c3ee-ca1c-5b3c-b345-772e9140b95e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}\\left(\\arctan{\\left(\\frac{x}{3} \\right)}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682878}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682878} :answer-field/id #uuid "66bcebd1-596c-5794-a036-d1136d473062" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682830}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "cb147313-6321-57c2-9e41-a59bfa74b9a7" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{4}{x^{2} + 9}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nChoose the antiderivative. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{3}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{3})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\nx^{2} + 9=9\\left(1+(\\frac{x}{3})^2\\right).\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=3\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{4}{9}\\cdot 3=\\frac{4}{3}$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int \\frac{4}{x^{2} + 9}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{4}{3}\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{3}\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=\\frac{4}{3}\\left(\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}\\right)+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{3}\\left(\\arctan{\\left(\\frac{x}{3} \\right)}\\right)+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682882 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ad483cf-21dd-5fc7-97c6-af7ecfac55ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{6}\\left(\\arctan{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682803} {:answer/id #uuid "550b3ae7-10e8-52e6-8435-be070591a897" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}\\left(\\arctan{\\left(\\frac{4 x}{3} \\right)}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682820} {:answer/id #uuid "95fd1368-e7a7-5a85-be27-78bfed1ec416" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}\\left(\\arctan{\\left(\\frac{2 x}{3} \\right)}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682853} {:answer/id #uuid "aba8c11c-58cd-5663-86be-0ac76c43092c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}\\left(\\arctan{\\left(\\frac{x}{3} \\right)}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682858} {:answer/id #uuid "ba57cb8e-468c-5c63-809e-ff6b41b46e38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}\\left(\\arctan{\\left(\\frac{2 x}{3} \\right)}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682866}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682866} :answer-field/id #uuid "785ed284-86a5-596d-a82c-36093cb94aa1" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682840}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "deff6d65-8112-5b95-a6ff-9646caad51ac" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{4 x^{2} + 9}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nChoose the antiderivative. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{2 x}{3}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{2}{3})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n4 x^{2} + 9=9\\left(1+(\\frac{2 x}{3})^2\\right).\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}=\\frac{1}{6}$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int \\frac{1}{4 x^{2} + 9}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{1}{6}\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{6}\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=\\frac{1}{6}\\left(\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}\\right)+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{6}\\left(\\arctan{\\left(\\frac{2 x}{3} \\right)}\\right)+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186683011 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "887f20d7-c3bb-5f93-b4e0-13c10c21e892" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186683033}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186683033} :answer-field/id #uuid "20aeb071-f38e-5388-a548-9dc76bbacdef" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186683015}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "13285ed5-a0db-5b3a-b640-d68de99074b7" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{4} \\frac{4}{x^{2} + 16}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{4}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{4})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\nx^{2} + 16=16\\left(1+(\\frac{x}{4})^2\\right).\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=4\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 4=1$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=0\\\\x=4&\\Longrightarrow u=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{4} \\frac{4}{x^{2} + 16}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arctan{\\left(0 \\right)}=0,\\quad \\arctan{\\left(1 \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$.\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{1}=\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)-\\left(0\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi}{4}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186683012 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8ec46ef-2302-5566-a10d-87d41945d32a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186683040}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186683040} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3a233d5-0ce0-5283-b70a-6b9c2aba4968" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186683044}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "16b53daa-14dc-5da8-8f94-7fbd5cede039" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{2} \\frac{2}{x^{2} + 4}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{2}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\nx^{2} + 4=4\\left(1+(\\frac{x}{2})^2\\right).\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=2\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2=1$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=0\\\\x=2&\\Longrightarrow u=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{2} \\frac{2}{x^{2} + 4}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arctan{\\left(0 \\right)}=0,\\quad \\arctan{\\left(1 \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$.\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{1}=\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)-\\left(0\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi}{4}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186683014 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce6ab13f-a216-56fc-a883-05600bc1089d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186683045}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186683045} :answer-field/id #uuid "e60662bb-f35d-56ab-b75e-dfe60a001cb1" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186683050}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "1d222a92-2853-555f-98ca-efa744b18673" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{-3}^{3} \\frac{3}{x^{2} + 9}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{3}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{3})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\nx^{2} + 9=9\\left(1+(\\frac{x}{3})^2\\right).\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=3\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 3=1$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=-3&\\Longrightarrow u=-1\\\\x=3&\\Longrightarrow u=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{-3}^{3} \\frac{3}{x^{2} + 9}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\int_{-1}^{1} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arctan{\\left(-1 \\right)}=- \\frac{\\pi}{4},\\quad \\arctan{\\left(1 \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$.\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{-1}^{1}=\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi}{2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186683019 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae5562fe-2a81-53c6-b681-260e6379d6d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186683041}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186683041} :answer-field/id #uuid "f32f759b-4ff7-503d-828c-ae04505e7fdc" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186683054}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2eaeaf04-a4a9-59d2-b4f7-87b6c47b8d9c" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{2} \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{16 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{4}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{4})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{16 - x^{2}}=4\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{x}{4})^2}.\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=4\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $1\\cdot 4=4$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=0\\\\x=2&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{2} \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{16 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=4\\left(\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arcsin{\\left(0 \\right)}=0,\\quad \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{1}{2} \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$.\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n4\\left(\\left[\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\right)=4\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186683020 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f931b18d-a427-5e6c-8717-6fc9f2a68ff2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186683056}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186683056} :answer-field/id #uuid "64fa45be-734f-5a53-a1f8-46b7f7ba30ca" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186683027}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "3475a31e-8811-5a04-8514-23df6335e8a7" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{-1}^{1} \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{4 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{2}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{4 - x^{2}}=2\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{x}{2})^2}.\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=2\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot 2=3$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=-1&\\Longrightarrow u=- \\frac{1}{2}\\\\x=1&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{-1}^{1} \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{4 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=3\\left(\\int_{- \\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arcsin{\\left(- \\frac{1}{2} \\right)}=- \\frac{\\pi}{6},\\quad \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{1}{2} \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$.\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n3\\left(\\left[\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{- \\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\right)=3\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\pi.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186683026 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "947dca03-c740-5bcf-8f6a-fdc569b5c107" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4 \\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186683034}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186683034} :answer-field/id #uuid "6814be85-0e4d-5841-8e09-d898afe2b5f8" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186683028}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "5a0117c4-51ef-54d2-8f11-754b90a9c632" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{- \\frac{3}{2}}^{\\frac{3}{2}} \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{9 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{3}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{3})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{9 - x^{2}}=3\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{x}{3})^2}.\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=3\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot 3=4$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=- \\frac{3}{2}&\\Longrightarrow u=- \\frac{1}{2}\\\\x=\\frac{3}{2}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{- \\frac{3}{2}}^{\\frac{3}{2}} \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{9 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=4\\left(\\int_{- \\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arcsin{\\left(- \\frac{1}{2} \\right)}=- \\frac{\\pi}{6},\\quad \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{1}{2} \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$.\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n4\\left(\\left[\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{- \\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\right)=4\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{4 \\pi}{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186683029 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a687e8fa-fa75-5745-809b-113d89674c35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186683039}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186683039} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d88223b-a299-5c5e-a521-c85f03765297" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186683022}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "6b8136e7-b7a6-53df-a