ion is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=5$ and $Q(x)=x{e}^{-5x}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int 5\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{5x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={e}^{5x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+5y) & ={e}^{5x}\\cdot x{e}^{-5x} \\\\ {e}^{5x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+5{e}^{5x}\\cdot y & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x))$ and carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{5x}) & =x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{5x})\\text{d}x & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{5x} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{{x}^{2}{e}^{-5x}}{2}+C{e}^{-5x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186686873 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e73fbce-e1e6-57c8-8925-6e9d97846f8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "C e^{2 x} + \\frac{x^{2} e^{2 x}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686842} {:answer/id #uuid "5fa95c42-6e2b-57c2-8dac-cefb3d4ec147" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "C e^{x} + \\frac{x^{2} e^{2 x}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686845} {:answer/id #uuid "65a5594e-4851-54cf-8c21-75f305e01082" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "C e^{x} + \\frac{x^{2} e^{2 x}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686847} {:answer/id #uuid "c780b6e2-f64b-5d75-90d1-1dc43b607bc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "C e^{2 x} + \\frac{x^{2} e^{2 x}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686874}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186686842} :answer-field/id #uuid "8aa8886f-46bd-5835-918e-30ee0f7ff5ef" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 