w, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={x}^{6}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{6}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{6}{x}y) & ={x}^{6}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}{{x}^{5}} \\\\ {x}^{6}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+6{x}^{5}y & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x))$ and carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{6}) & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{6})\\text{d}x & =\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this integral, we integrate by parts. \n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int {u}^{′}v\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nLet $u=x,{u}^{′}=1,{v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x,$ and $v=-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}{2}.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y{x}^{6} & =\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{6} & =x(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}{2})-\\int (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}{2})\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{6} & =x(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}{2})+\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{6} & =-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}{4}\\,+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}{{x}^{6}}}{4}-\\frac{\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}{{x}^{5}}}{2}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{6}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186686899 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f44c0f8-eda9-5e3a-9308-7411cb897eb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x^{2}} - \\frac{\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}}{x} + \\frac{\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}}{x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686894} {:answer/id #uuid "669df105-ee50-53a8-9f5c-7745ac2d7a7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x^{3}} + \\frac{\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}}{x} + \\frac{\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}}{x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 1