correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186691808} :answer-field/id #uuid "9077e362-5e58-5461-80f8-f1f36b833c72" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691839} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fe29d16-81aa-5669-9e51-04a0ece91e3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691812} {:answer/id #uuid "88a1133c-4754-53d8-9023-69103808838f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6 x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691831} {:answer/id #uuid "bf734055-c0b1-5bfa-aa52-e132129bd9e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691863} {:answer/id #uuid "dbd52e8b-f705-5c5d-81f5-f23573b5cee5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691877}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186691863} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9326610-28eb-57d5-8ec9-92a0e1e0fa23" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691873}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2131f3d4-6260-51c9-aa60-055aea78b619" :question/problem "Suppose we would like to find an **integrating factor** to convert the differential equation\n\n$$\n(6 x y)\\,\\text{d}x+\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\ninto an exact equation. Select the correct options in the reasoning below. Take $x$ to be real.\n\nFor a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nif\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}=g(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $g(x)$ is independent of $y$, an integrating factor is\n\n$$\nI(x)={{field-2}}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\exp(x)$ denotes $e^x$.\n\nLet's denote\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=6 x y,\\qquad Q(x,y)=1\n$$\n\nNow compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}={{field-3}}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}={{field-4}}\n$$\n\nSince\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})={{field-5}}\n$$\n\nis a function of $x$ only, an integrating factor is\n\n$$\nI(x)={{field-6}}\n$$\n\nand multiplication gives the exact equation\n\n$$\n{{field-7}}\n$$\n\nChoose the multiplicative constant to be one." :question/worked-solution "For a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nif\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})=g(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $g(x)$ is independent of $y$, an integrating factor is\n\n$$\nI(x)=\\exp(\\int g(x)\\,\\text{d}x)\n$$.\n\nHere $\\exp(x)=e^x$.\n\nLet's denote\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=6 x y,\\qquad Q(x,y)=1\n$$\n\nCompute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}(6 x y)=6 x \\\\ \\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}(1)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})&=\\frac{1}{1}(6 x-(0)) \\\\ &=6 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a function of $x$ only. Choose the multiplicative constant to be one. Thus\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x)&=\\exp(\\int (6 x)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\ &=\\exp(3 x^{2}) \\\\ &=e^{3 x^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiply the original differential equation by this integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x)((6 x y)\\,\\text{d}x+\\,\\text{d}y)&=I(x)\\cdot 0 \\\\ e^{3 x^{2}}((6 x y)\\,\\text{d}x+\\,\\text{d}y)&=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:answer/id #uuid "38a360e2-65f0-5433-acce-d0375bee2c6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}+\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691803} {:answer/id #uuid "39d81e15-fa53-5d33-8a74-acfe29bc85dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}+\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691804} {:answer/id #uuid "3d6ef659-63ea-5ce1-964d-e7023bf71e1d" :an