07} {:answer/id #uuid "57c18e05-fd5b-54f6-ae85-6bb07d037ec6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691910}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186691894} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad2785a0-19f0-5669-a4ab-3300635fb709" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691935}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "d4a0fb07-de45-5ff4-8196-467d2b3e5c33" :question/problem "Find an **integrating factor** depending on $x$ alone that makes the equation exact:\n\n$$\n4 xy'=5 x^{2}\n$$\n\nUse the differential form obtained by moving the right-hand side to the left and multiplying by $\\text{d}x$, without dividing by the coefficient of $y'$. In this form, $P$ is the coefficient of $\\text{d}x$ and $Q$ is the coefficient of $\\text{d}y$. Work on $x>0$ and choose $I(1)=1$.\n\nDifferential form:\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}\n$$\n\nCompute the quotient:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})={{field-2}}\n$$\n\nAn integrating factor is\n\n$$\nI(x)={{field-3}}\n$$\n\nand multiplication gives the exact equation\n\n$$\n{{field-4}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nif\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})=g(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $g(x)$ is independent of $y$, an integrating factor is\n\n$$\nI(x)=\\exp(\\int g(x)\\,\\text{d}x)\n$$.\n\nHere $\\exp(x)=e^x$.\n\nFirst, rewrite our equation in differential form:\n\n$$\n(- 5 x^{2})\\,\\text{d}x+4 x\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nLet's denote\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=- 5 x^{2},\\qquad Q(x,y)=4 x\n$$\n\nCompute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}(- 5 x^{2})=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}(4 x)=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})&=\\frac{1}{4 x}(0-(4)) \\\\ &=- \\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a function of $x$ only. Choose the multiplicative constant to be one. Thus\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x)&=\\exp(\\int \\left(- \\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\ &=\\exp(- \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}) \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn $x>0$, the power rule for logarithms gives $\\exp(k\\ln x)=x^k$.\n\nMultiply the original differential equation by this integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x)((- 5 x^{2})\\,\\text{d}x+4 x\\,\\text{d}y)&=I(x)\\cdot 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{x}((- 5 x^{2})\\,\\text{d}x+4 x\\,\\text{d}y)&=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186691975 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6044fae-fb77-53c8-9663-54dfce81b73c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{\\frac{\\left(x - 2\\right)^{2}}{2}}}{2} - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691982} {:answer/id #uuid "3c470bcb-44e9-4787-af29-c628c15d79da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac12e^{\\left(\\frac{x^2}{2}-2x+2\\right)}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186747956}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186691982} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9884a46-d929-5597-ad6e-6c857d5796ab" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691977}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "89df1509-cae7-5985-b0de-0050e1bd764c" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\cos(1y)\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}+\\left(2 - x\\right)\\sin(1y)=x - 2\n$$\n\nthat satisfies $y(2)=- \\frac{\\pi}{6}$. Work on the local branch $-\\frac{\\pi}{2}<y<\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ near $x=2$. Give the solution in implicit form by completing the right-hand side.\n\n$\\sin(1y)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Collect and factor the right-hand side, then separate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos(1y)y'&=\\left(2 - x\\right)\\left(-1-\\sin(1y)\\right)\\\\\n\\frac{\\cos(1y)}{-1-\\sin(1y)}\\,\\mathrm{d}y&=\\left(2 - x\\right)\\mathrm{d}x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the stated branch the denominator is nonzero. Set $v=-1-\\sin(1y)$, so $\\mathrm{d}v=-1\\cos(1y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y$. Integrating gives\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{1}\\ln|-1-\\sin(1y)|=- \\frac{\\left(x - 2\\right)^{2}}{2}+C.\n$$\n\nMultiplying by $-1$ and absorbing the constant gives\n\n$$\n\\ln|-1-\\sin(1y)|=\\frac{\\left(x - 2\\right)^{2}}{2}+K.\n$$\n\nAt the initial point, $\\sin(1\\cdot\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right))=- \\frac{1}{2}$. Thus $v(2)=- \\frac{1}{2}$ and\n\n$$\nK=\\ln\\left|- \\frac{1}{2}\\right|+0.\n$$\n\nExponentiate and retain the sign of $v$ at the initial point:\n\n$$\n-1-\\sin(1y)=\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right)e^{\\frac{\\left(x - 2\\right)^{2}}{2}}.\n$$\n\nRearranging yields\n\n$$\n\\sin(1y)=\\frac{e^{\\frac{\\left(x - 2\\right)^{2}}{2}}}{2} - 1.\n$$\n\nThe stated branch selects the local solution through the initial point; no inverse-sine conversion is required."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186691976 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8462f606-4b37-5c83-a6da-080ec772f42d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1 - \\frac{e^{- x^{2}}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691974}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186691974} :answer-field/id #uuid "da579351-2b3c-5d0e-977e-0fa68d0ccd4e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691981}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "b8fa6e11-e81e-5792-8252-0d9c4179e95b" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\cos(2y)\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}+\\left(x\\right)\\sin(2y)=x\n$$\n\nthat satisfies $y(0)=\\frac{\\pi}{12}$. Work on the local branch $-\\frac{\\pi}{4}<y<\\frac{\\pi}{4}$ near $x=0$. Give the solution in implicit form by completing the right-hand side.\n\n$\\sin(2y)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Collect and factor the right-hand side, then separate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos(2y)y'&=\\left(x\\right)\\left(1-\\sin(2y)\\right)\\\\\n\\frac{\\cos(2y)}{1-\\sin(2y)}\\,\\mathrm{d}y&=\\left(x\\right)\\mathrm{d}x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the stated branch the denominator is nonzero. Set $v=1-\\sin(2y)$, so $\\mathrm{d}v=-2\\cos(2y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y$. Integrating gives\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{2}\\ln|1-\\sin(2y)|=\\frac{x^{2}}{2}+C.\n$$\n\nMultiplying by $-2$ and absorbing the constant gives\n\n$$\n\\ln|1-\\sin(2y)|=- x^{2}+K.\n$$\n\nAt the initial point, $\\sin(2\\cdot\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{12}\\right))=\\frac{1}{2}$. Thus $v(0)=\\frac{1}{2}$ and\n\n$$\nK=\\ln\\left|\\frac{1}{2}\\right|+0.\n$$\n\nExponentiate and retain the sign of $v$ at the initial point:\n\n$$\n1-\\sin(2y)=\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)e^{- x^{2}}.\n$$\n\nRearranging yields\n\n$$\n\\sin(2y)=1 - \\frac{e^{- x^{2}}}{2}.\n$$\n\nThe stated branch selects the local solution through the initial point; no inverse-sine conversion is required."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186692555 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9262c632-6c4e-5d71-9b04-9d1ba3cca4ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{4 x}{5} \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692644} {:answer/id #uuid "a156e746-eb49-5159-aa2d-3012b770fc72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{4 x}{5} \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692653} {:answer/id #uuid "a6d4531f-2f7c-5ca4-8fd3-5889f5efe810" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{8 x}{5} \\right)}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692656} {:answer/id #uuid "e1e8ba2f-5410-5acf-ab41-65f478ab7ba4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{8 \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{4 x}{5} \\right)}}{25}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692698} {:answer/id #uuid "ecc72496-558b-50c6-9c34-8ca68c4aa700" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{4 x}{5} \\right)}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692703}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186692703} :answer-field/id #uuid "fcb13a7c-e75b-59cf-9225-a0c4343fca3e" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692712}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "09b53fce-7186-54fd-8edb-2f8c949bfa41" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{25 - 16 x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nChoose the antiderivative. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{4 x}{5}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{4}{5})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nNormalize the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{25 - 16 x^{2}}=5\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{4 x}{5})^2}.\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{5}{4}\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot \\frac{5}{4}=\\frac{1}{2}$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{25 - 16 x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}\\right)+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{4 x}{5} \\right)}}{2}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186692563 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5548f241-9fad-51a4-bc9d-41471a85181b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4 \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692611} {:answer/id #uuid "5c1ec6d9-1702-531b-a623-191b71ca6d5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692618} {:answer/id #uuid "5d658b5b-2328-506c-9d6a-a87751bb1c85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8 \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692620} {:answer/id #uuid "79d2d7c4-f466-5555-a50a-d30efd1830be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692633} {:answer/id #uuid "ae19402f-e1b9-5216-a19a-c543f44c6ebc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8 \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{x}{4} \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692663}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186692611} :answer-field/id #uuid "f057d5ef-5572-52d5-b185-4928b28e1ce5" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692707}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1325f05c-6254-5239-924a-ed17def24a85" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{4 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nChoose the antiderivative. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{2}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nNormalize the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{4 - x^{2}}=2\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{x}{2})^2}.\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=2\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $2\\cdot 2=4$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{4 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=4\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\n$$\n4\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=4\\left(\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}\\right)+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n4 \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186692574 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e8f5fe4-8b95-51ff-bf5b-34b2f15cde44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692558} {:answer/id #uuid "7cf7281e-fddd-526f-b891-8f4452470dd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\arcsin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692634} {:answer/id #uuid "b6855eac-0a08-5c55-8679-d167635075e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{x}{4} \\right)}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692673} {:answer/id #uuid "f2896158-da18-55a0-89f9-a96c115d29dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{x}{4} \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692708} {:answer/id #uuid "f7b1bf82-54bd-56f3-8ef6-a330319e1194" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692711}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186692558} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebf72a16-0cfd-542f-9be6-bfa2444a60bd" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692701}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "25e27582-f1e2-52a4-85d6-86949f5fcd7e" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nChoose the antiderivative. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{2}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nNormalize the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{4 - x^{2}}=2\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{x}{2})^2}.\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=2\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2=1$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186692575 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "028b8fbb-9720-5a96-ad53-72ddb6ffabf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{x}{3} \\right)}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692550} {:answer/id #uuid "1d552641-d51b-565a-88ea-dcd5b62e1990" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3 \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{x}{3} \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692571} {:answer/id #uuid "2e0182cc-43a0-5d5e-a19a-b5e256329f59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6 \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{x}{6} \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692578} {:answer/id #uuid "92595d66-3585-509e-9ef9-649f028f0b55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\arcsin{\\left(x \\right)}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692643} {:answer/id #uuid "e1cecded-7f7d-505c-aaff-48625280159a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\arcsin{\\left(3 x \\right)}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692697}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186692571} :answer-field/id #uuid "abfa6f16-fc35-529a-95a5-08ae3ba44114" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692660}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "297ac9e7-b8a9-5a3b-962d-5f582cebfb0f" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{9 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nChoose the antiderivative. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{3}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{3})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nNormalize the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{9 - x^{2}}=3\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{x}{3})^2}.\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=3\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $1\\cdot 3=3$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{9 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=3\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\n$$\n3\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=3\\left(\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}\\right)+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n3 \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{x}{3} \\right)}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186692583 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03d14ff4-f113-51c9-abfe-d2076a3ad44e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{3 x}{5} \\right)}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692551} {:answer/id #uuid "b0a6e156-572a-555f-af3d-e2f3f9dc20cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{5 x}{3} \\right)}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692667} {:answer/id #uuid "b1f527d6-c1c9-528e-9288-b7b6bf3e7df0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\arcsin{\\left(x \\right)}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692670} {:answer/id #uuid "c5979824-8a32-5cd1-8a20-6e722ff47288" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\arcsin{\\left(x \\right)}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692682} {:answer/id #uuid "de1b480e-9354-5135-b420-6d673b75dd2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{2 \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{3 x}{5} \\right)}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692696}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186692551} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec16cbb1-fac5-59a3-b869-1e6ddcd92e37" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692702}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "356c7dff-ab79-5eac-a915-a14f2d6e4065" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{25 - 9 x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nChoose the antiderivative. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{3 x}{5}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{3}{5})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nNormalize the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{25 - 9 x^{2}}=5\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{3 x}{5})^2}.\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{5}{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot \\frac{5}{3}=\\frac{2}{3}$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{25 - 9 x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{2}{3}\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=\\frac{2}{3}\\left(\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}\\right)+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2 \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{3 x}{5} \\right)}}{3}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186692612 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b44de39-c475-59cd-a417-8dab989e180b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{2 x}{5} \\right)}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692557} {:answer/id #uuid "2fdb1b6e-90b8-5805-9d20-127870971aad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{2 x}{5} \\right)}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692580} {:answer/id #uuid "3bc3833b-36ef-5491-872d-f6908fb06cf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{5 x}{2} \\right)}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592