frac{1}{2}\\left(\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}\\right)+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\arctan{\\left(\\frac{x}{4} \\right)}}{2}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186692870 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f671a3a-8e44-5f06-8a99-b2c74fca5bf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 \\arctan{\\left(x \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692728} {:answer/id #uuid "68b875d4-e332-57cb-94a6-bf899ba7719d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\arctan{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692790} {:answer/id #uuid "ae944cfa-97d3-5e99-a921-63853e56ad8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4 \\arctan{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692827} {:answer/id #uuid "bab6948b-1da8-5d2c-b414-6a11cf39ea91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4 \\arctan{\\left(x \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692834} {:answer/id #uuid "d57a354d-392c-54a0-b47b-8e069281a968" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 \\arctan{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692856}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186692856} :answer-field/id #uuid "4fdc3313-e82f-5314-a725-4ffa5fbda3ad" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692773}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e67daad2-4eb1-599e-ad0c-33dc5036337d" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{4}{x^{2} + 4}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nChoose the antiderivative. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{2}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nNormalize the denominator:\n\n$$\nx^{2} + 4=4\\left(1+(\\frac{x}{2})^2\\right).\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=2\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $1\\cdot 2=2$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int \\frac{4}{x^{2} + 4}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=2\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\n$$\n2\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=2\\left(\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}\\right)+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n2 \\arctan{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186692873 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2811fee6-38df-5d3d-827f-e13fcd4cf85e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\arctan{\\left(\\frac{5 x}{2} \\right)}}{20}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692744} {:answer/id #uuid "67e54f61-4761-549e-9cf5-a94fc4569487" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\arctan{\\left(5 x \\right)}}{10}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692788} {:answer/id #uuid "bada49f7-fc83-5613-85ee-8f1ee0f97528" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5 \\arctan{\\left(\\frac{5 x}{2} \\right)}}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692835} {:answer/id #uuid "bdd0330e-09b2-5a37-975d-0a0acd570e38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\arctan{\\left(\\frac{5 x}{2} \\right)}}{10}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692839} {:answer/id #uuid "df7f6d49-2d58-55b1-a31d-6d2e213302a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\arctan{\\left(\\frac{5 x}{4} \\right)}}{20}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692863}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186692839} :answer-field/id #uuid "75b82ac8-5759-500e-aa6a-2ba7a9c52492" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692797}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "ed1aad87-6f1b-5e6d-85d3-7199d0489c00" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{25 x^{2} + 4}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nChoose the antiderivative. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{5 x}{2}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{5}{2})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nNormalize the denominator:\n\n$$\n25 x^{2} + 4=4\\left(1+(\\frac{5 x}{2})^2\\right).\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{2}{5}\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{2}{5}=\\frac{1}{10}$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int \\frac{1}{25 x^{2} + 4}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{1}{10}\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{10}\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=\\frac{1}{10}\\left(\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}\\right)+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\arctan{\\left(\\frac{5 x}{2} \\right)}}{10}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186692874 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34669325-72a9-55c2-a60b-1bab25d3c3bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\arctan{\\left(\\frac{x}{4} \\right)}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692756} {:answer/id #uuid "4e529a9d-5bcc-5ebc-bc1f-40a1892e3cf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\arctan{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692770} {:answer/id #uuid "78895b18-b0e0-5f95-8a9f-5906aedfeb9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\arctan{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692798} {:answer/id #uuid "80cf0563-4aef-5be0-854e-eaa56fd79add" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\arctan{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692803} {:answer/id #uuid "9ea2934f-4944-58a1-b578-5639f0236b00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\arctan{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692817}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186692770} :answer-field/id #uuid "095565ed-6d46-5a8f-8b00-08b88320aee8" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186692723}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ee8614b1-724a-5ab7-bc81-4b936c05df1a" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{2}{x^{2} + 4}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nChoose the antiderivative. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{2}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nNormalize the denominator:\n\n$$\nx^{2} + 4=4\\left(1+(\\frac{x}{2})^2\\right).\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=2\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2=1$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int \\frac{2}{x^{2} + 4}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n\\arctan{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693059 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b6d82fcd-f8e6-5c42-9362-e0c21d7f479f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693124}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693124} :answer-field/id #uuid "5071aab3-0b63-575b-8580-6b3743d0842b" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693085}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0ee19251-9ec3-50f8-afac-37a3b36232b0" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{- \\frac{3}{2}}^{\\frac{3}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{9 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{3}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{3})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nNormalize the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{9 - x^{2}}=3\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{x}{3})^2}.\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=3\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 3=1$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=- \\frac{3}{2}&\\Longrightarrow u=- \\frac{1}{2}\\\\x=\\frac{3}{2}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{- \\frac{3}{2}}^{\\frac{3}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{9 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\int_{- \\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arcsin{\\left(- \\frac{1}{2} \\right)}=- \\frac{\\pi}{6},\\quad \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{1}{2} \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$.\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{- \\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{1}{2}}=\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi}{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693060 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04595e05-af1c-50aa-a0de-42138b20dda7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693055}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693055} :answer-field/id #uuid "45409891-4b88-5e6c-8425-841fb8302e5a" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693079}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "0f7e23d7-f594-5f67-b9ed-c802d03ed782" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{-1}^{1} \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{2 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{\\sqrt{2} x}{2}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nNormalize the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{2 - x^{2}}=\\sqrt{2}\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{\\sqrt{2} x}{2})^2}.\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=\\sqrt{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $2 \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}=4$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=-1&\\Longrightarrow u=- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\\\x=1&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{-1}^{1} \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{2 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=4\\left(\\int_{- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}}^{\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arcsin{\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\right)}=- \\frac{\\pi}{4},\\quad \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$.\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n4\\left(\\left[\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}}^{\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}}\\right)=4\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n2 \\pi.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693062 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a97417d9-94a6-5980-8d46-a467807fab3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693117}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693117} :answer-field/id #uuid "59b750ac-74c2-5c4b-b6bb-f67db8dbc51d" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693091}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "1371c8ad-ea4c-52bc-a8be-cbd7cd21bedd" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{\\sqrt{2}}^{2} \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{8 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{\\sqrt{2} x}{4}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nNormalize the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{8 - x^{2}}=2 \\sqrt{2}\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{\\sqrt{2} x}{4})^2}.\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=2 \\sqrt{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 2 \\sqrt{2}=4$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\sqrt{2}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{1}{2}\\\\x=2&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{\\sqrt{2}}^{2} \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{8 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=4\\left(\\int_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{1}{2} \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{6},\\quad \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$.\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n4\\left(\\left[\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}}\\right)=4\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi}{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693065 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7644753-abd6-5ed7-a994-0f807b480077" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3} \\pi}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693132}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693132} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3b1e437-277c-50aa-93b5-e24edf0fcc97" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693151}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "1a481085-117b-5999-ad76-8e19a57728c7" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{-2}^{2} \\frac{2}{x^{2} + 12}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{\\sqrt{3} x}{6}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{6})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nNormalize the denominator:\n\n$$\nx^{2} + 12=12\\left(1+(\\frac{\\sqrt{3} x}{6})^2\\right).\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=2 \\sqrt{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 2 \\sqrt{3}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=-2&\\Longrightarrow u=- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\\\x=2&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{-2}^{2} \\frac{2}{x^{2} + 12}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\left(\\int_{- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}}^{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arctan{\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\right)}=- \\frac{\\pi}{6},\\quad \\arctan{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$.\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\left(\\left[\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}}^{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}}\\right)=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\sqrt{3} \\pi}{9}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693071 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd2d16ed-0a22-517d-aff0-2fc17e5cbd6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693136}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693136} :answer-field/id #uuid "1749ef1b-b7dd-5332-b751-7e02c047f761" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693063}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "29922848-0161-5ee9-b650-fe402a88aa8f" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{5 \\sqrt{3}}{3}} \\frac{2}{x^{2} + 25}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{5}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{5})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nNormalize the denominator:\n\n$$\nx^{2} + 25=25\\left(1+(\\frac{x}{5})^2\\right).\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=5\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{2}{25}\\cdot 5=\\frac{2}{5}$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=0\\\\x=\\frac{5 \\sqrt{3}}{3}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{\\frac{5 \\sqrt{3}}{3}} \\frac{2}{x^{2} + 25}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{2}{5}\\left(\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}} \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arctan{\\left(0 \\right)}=0,\\quad \\arctan{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$.\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{5}\\left(\\left[\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}}\\right)=\\frac{2}{5}\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi}{15}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693081 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4efd285-7561-56f4-bccc-435c7e27f225" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693122}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693122} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2c51ac5-8776-5b03-b151-314d5edb2a90" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693127}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 175921