domain unchanged. The symbols $\\mathbf i,\\mathbf j$ are the planar unit vectors.\n\n- **I.** $D(x,y)=\\langle\\frac{1}{x-2},\\sqrt{y-2}\\rangle$ on $\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x-2\\ne0,\\ y-2\\geq0\\}$.\n\n- **II.** $F(x,y)=\\ln(x-2)\\,\\mathbf i$ on $\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x-2\\geq0\\}$.\n\n- **III.** $N(x,y)=\\langle\\sqrt{x-y},\\ln(x+y-4)\\rangle$ on $\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x-y\\geq0,\\ x+y-4>0\\}$." :question/worked-solution "Check planar inputs and outputs, then test whether the formula is real and defined at every point of the stated domain.\n\n- **I.** $D$ The components require $x-2\\ne0,\\ y-2\\geq0$. Every point in the stated domain satisfies these conditions. The square-root boundary $y-2=0$ is allowed when $x-2\\ne0$.  The inputs and outputs are planar, so select this function.\n\n- **II.** $F$ The components require $x-2>0$. The point $(2,2)$ lies in the stated domain, but gives $\\ln(0)$; the logarithm is undefined. The omitted planar component is zero: $\\ln(x-2)\\,\\mathbf i+0\\,\\mathbf j=\\langle\\ln(x-2),0\\rangle$. Its output is still planar. The formula therefore fails on the entire stated domain. Do not select this function; shrinking the domain is not allowed in this question.\n\n- **III.** $N$ The components require $x-y\\geq0,\\ x+y-4>0$. Every point in the stated domain satisfies these conditions. The boundary $x-2=y-2>0$ is allowed. The inputs and outputs are planar, so select this function.\n\nSelect I, III only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707518 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7edbcea0-a4e4-5b9a-abe8-777381fee67c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707493} {:answer/id #uuid "90f22b0e-9022-5c4f-a39b-9b18e0faa36e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707499}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707493} :answer-field/id #uuid "36da47c7-ffe9-5eb7-b362-ed0c024c8839" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707482} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "792d1e27-8754-5c3a-8747-d3c67c4332a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707492} {:answer/id #uuid "e627cd83-a906-5088-8bc6-405c4580471f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707521}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707521} :answer-field/id #uuid "98802511-c89a-574f-80a4-e3056aa37bbd" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707502} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31a36004-19dd-5401-a5d6-027446d61149" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707479} {:answer/id #uuid "3551ec68-1e94-5f4c-8d4a-c69b00acc9e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707481}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707479} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9007f92-b835-5a1c-8ccc-48bcef6f7aae" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707504}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e0e3935c-9b67-5c67-b0f0-72f2ff2fe2ee" :question/problem "Which formulas define vector fields on $\\mathbb R^2$ on their **entire stated domains**? Select all that apply. Keep every stated domain unchanged. The symbols $\\mathbf i,\\mathbf j$ are the planar unit vectors.\n\n- **I.** $T(x,y)=\\langle\\sqrt{x-y+6},\\ln(x+y)\\rangle$ on $\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x-y+6\\geq0,\\ x+y>0\\}$.\n\n- **II.** $M(x,y)=\\ln(x+3)\\,\\mathbf i$ on $\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x+3>0\\}$.\n\n- **III.** $J(x,y)=\\langle\\frac{1}{x+3},\\sqrt{y-3}\\rangle$ on $\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x+3\\geq0,\\ y-3\\geq0\\}$." :question/worked-solution "Check planar inputs and outputs, then test whether the formula is real and defined at every point of the stated domain.\n\n- **I.** $T$ The components require $x-y+6\\geq0,\\ x+y>0$. Every point in the stated domain satisfies these conditions. The boundary $x+3=y-3>0$ is allowed. The inputs and outputs are planar, so select this function.\n\n- **II.** $M$ The components require $x+3>0$. Every point in the stated domain satisfies these conditions. The omitted planar component is zero: $\\ln(x+3)\\,\\mathbf i+0\\,\\mathbf j=\\langle\\ln(x+3),0\\rangle$. Its output is still planar. The inputs and outputs are planar, so select this function.\n\n- **III.** $J$ The components require $x+3\\ne0,\\ y-3\\geq0$. The point $(-3,4)$ lies in the stated domain, but gives $1/0$; the reciprocal is undefined. The formula therefore fails on the entire stated domain. Do not select this function; shrinking the domain is not allowed in this question.\n\nSelect I, II only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707533 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d472eed-f8d5-5ee1-9db7-ccd243145067" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707527} {:answer/id #uuid "14f49d01-9486-5e0b-8026-e0a57a22b0fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707530}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707530} :answer-field/id #uuid "5cc538ee-e54b-52e6-bbbe-e548ffff4ef2" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707541} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22201626-0d65-5fb0-8e7f-a5c6db38b7c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707532} {:answer/id #uuid "ee630744-08fb-5098-b051-3d0c2d1b3a4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707563}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707532} :answer-field/id #uuid "9390f336-9f3b-5b94-a124-ab73085df8f7" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707548} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5048a3e8-9a7c-531d-8409-ee8d0b2b37e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707539} {:answer/id #uuid "7627e420-8cf7-5cc7-a547-e2aa1271d5fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707544}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707539} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3df1e7e-d2ef-5e0c-9b14-53cd99b9c8be" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707561}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "26d1b88a-fd6c-549a-8858-e6e5e3ae5994" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on $\\mathbb R^2$? Select all that apply. Use each function's declared input coordinates and its natural real domain.\n\n- **I.** $Z(x,y)=(\\frac{1}{(x+2)})\\,\\mathbf i+(0)\\,\\mathbf j$\n\n- **II.** $S(x,y)=\\frac{1}{(x+2)}+\\frac{1}{(x+2)}$\n\n- **III.** $A(x,y)=\\langle (x+2)^2,(x+2)^2\\rangle$" :question/worked-solution "Check the input dimension and output dimension.\n\n- **I.** $Z$ takes 2 input coordinates and returns a vector with 2 components. The declared input list determines the input dimension, even when a coordinate is unused; a zero output coordinate still counts. Its natural real domain is $\\{(x,y)\\in \\mathbb R^2:(x+2)\\ne 0\\}$, which is nonempty. A restricted natural domain is allowed. Both dimensions are two, so select this function.\n\n- **II.** $S$ takes 2 input coordinates and returns a scalar. The declared input list determines the input dimension, even when a coordinate is unused; a zero output coordinate still counts. Its natural real domain is $\\{(x,y)\\in \\mathbb R^2:(x+2)\\ne 0\\}$, which is nonempty. A restricted natural domain is allowed. The input and output are not both two-dimensional, so do not select this function.\n\n- **III.** $A$ takes 2 input coordinates and returns a vector with 2 components. The declared input list determines the input dimension, even when a coordinate is unused; a zero output coordinate still counts. All components are real on $\\mathbb R^2$. Both dimensions are two, so select this function.\n\nSelect I, III only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707666 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f5cca12-3b19-5421-9d88-790702b6a221" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2 \\\\ z &=- 8 y - 5 + 2 \\pi\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707656} {:answer/id #uuid "289becc4-b8e1-50ae-843f-bb6ae0483f2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2 \\\\ z &=- 4 y - 5 + 2 \\pi\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707657} {:answer/id #uuid "2fd46d57-fdf0-5d81-8ca8-450d6df4db6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2 \\\\ z &=4 y - 5\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707660} {:answer/id #uuid "820bd526-f1f7-5fde-927e-d6bc4cebd402" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2 \\\\ z &=- 8 y - 1 + \\pi\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707673} {:answer/id #uuid "9f962802-d8e3-5e87-8294-7cefdb4cc77e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2 \\\\ z &=- 4 y - 1 + \\pi\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707676}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707676} :answer-field/id #uuid "b539ee71-d8cf-5fca-ba72-135b35d3b904" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707679}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3ce8fb9a-d09b-5a3e-b572-a68774df28ef" :question/problem "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $x=2$. The point $P(2,-1 + \\frac{\\pi}{4},3)$ lies on $C$, and\n\n$$\nf_y(x,y)=-\\left(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x\\left(y + 1\\right))\\right)\n$$\n\nFind the equations of the tangent line to $C$ at $P$." :question/worked-solution "The plane fixes $x$, so $y$ varies along the section. Evaluate the supplied partial:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m&=f_y(2,-1 + \\frac{\\pi}{4}) \\\\ &=-\\left(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\left(2\\right)\\left(\\left(-1 + \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) + 1\\right))\\right) \\\\ &=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse point-slope form at $(y_0,z_0)=(-1 + \\frac{\\pi}{4},3)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-(3)&=(-4)(y-(-1 + \\frac{\\pi}{4})) \\\\ z&=- 4 y - 1 + \\pi\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe tangent retains the fixed-coordinate plane:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2 \\\\ z &=- 4 y - 1 + \\pi\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n"} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4400488d-7de3-5836-8aa3-f80469fc33c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707695} {:answer/id #uuid "9fa166de-ecc3-5678-9e26-51f94e8b2ec7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707709}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707709} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5e47416-93f8-5630-b413-35dea96203bf" :answer-field/key "$K(x,y,z)=\\langle0,\\frac{1}{x-y},0\\rangle$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707711} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707763 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17e7c8fb-8a83-5ac4-8abb-13d97f116b6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\langle 3,0,\\frac{18}{13}\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707765} {:answer/id #uuid "3d30d925-d58a-528f-9959-d24a423a2aaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\langle -2,0,\\frac{6}{13}\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707771} {:answer/id #uuid "67075c53-7e42-56b5-8fdc-4b9877040650" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\langle -3,0,- \\frac{9}{13}\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707781} {:answer/id #uuid "b19d4e69-bbe9-5beb-a844-710b86a74171" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\langle -1,0,0\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707787} {:answer/id #uuid "ff34cb4a-4d73-5d88-8d1b-42dfc8a3c78b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\langle -1,0,4\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707796}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707781} :answer-field/id #uuid "339702a9-dd54-5e7b-9497-6975c31fcbac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707769}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "074fb8c2-fd96-5d84-90e7-baf7c5d8a421" :question/problem "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $y=5$. The point $P(-4,5,3)$ lies on $C$. The partial derivative is supplied:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f_x(x,y) & =-\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}}{2x-y}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is a tangent vector to $C$ at $P$?" :question/worked-solution "Holding $y$ fixed means that $x$ varies, so the slice slope is $f_x(-4,5)$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m=f_x(-4,5) & =-\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{{\\left(5\\right)}^{2}-{\\left(-4\\right)}^{2}}}{2\\left(-4\\right)-\\left(5\\right)}\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{3}{13}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe displayed quotient is evaluated at the supplied point; its denominator is nonzero. Simplifying the numerator and denominator gives the exact slope above.\n\nA change of $1$ in $x$ along the tangent gives a change of $\\frac{3}{13}$ in $z$, with no change in $y$. A tangent direction is $\\langle 1,0,\\frac{3}{13}\\rangle$.\n\nThe tangent line through $P(-4,5,3)$ is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y&=5 \\\\ z-(3)&=\\left(\\frac{3}{13}\\right)(x-(-4))\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe second plane is equivalently $\\frac{3 x}{13} - z + \\frac{51}{13}=0$. Normal vectors are $\\mathbf n_1=\\langle 0,1,0\\rangle$ and $\\mathbf n_2=\\langle - \\frac{3}{13},0,1\\rangle$. Their cross product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf n_1\\times\\mathbf n_2 & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i&\\mathbf j&\\mathbf k \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ - \\frac{3}{13} & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ & =\\langle 1,0,\\frac{3}{13}\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAny nonzero scalar multiple is valid. The listed answer is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3\\left(\\langle 1,0,\\frac{3}{13}\\rangle\\right) & =\\langle -3,0,- \\frac{9}{13}\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIt has the required component ratio $v_z/v_x=\\frac{3}{13}$."} {:answer/id #uuid "17e7c8fb-8a83-5ac4-8abb-13d97f116b6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\langle 3,0,\\frac{18}{13}\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707765} {:answer/id #uuid "3d30d925-d58a-528f-9959-d24a423a2aaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\langle -2,0,\\frac{6}{13}\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707771} {:answer/id #uuid "5bfa23c1-10d5-575f-adca-735373bba2a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\langle 0,-1,- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707777} {:answer/id #uuid "67075c53-7e42-56b5-8fdc-4b9877040650" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\langle -3,0,- \\frac{9}{13}\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707781} {:answer/id #uuid "72d7e9e6-68c2-5963-8013-322172f953fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\langle -1,0,\\frac{1}{3}\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707784} {:answer/id #uuid "bd4723ab-3930-555a-a78d-9c773f2639d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\langle -3,0,\\frac{9}{2}\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707788} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707790 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "140a0c9c-5ddf-5e97-9cf2-08623d2f49dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\langle 0,2,-4\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707764} {:answer/id #uuid "307e35f4-f814-5485-92bc-037dc17d6b7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\langle 0,-2,- 3 \\sqrt{2}\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707767} {:answer/id #uuid "5bfa23c1-10d5-575f-adca-735373bba2a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\langle 0,-1,- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707777} {:answer/id #uuid "d6925a9c-c6c6-5fc0-bd0e-1d2a87ec6ad1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\langle 0,3,- \\frac{15 \\sqrt{2}}{4}\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707791} {:answer/id #uuid "e0f260a4-c909-52d8-94e8-0df98a901873" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\langle 0,-2,-2\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707792}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707767} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0aa99c9-526a-58f9-82de-9c41e9ec77ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707794}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "cba914e7-7c8a-5902-80e2-2c2c483b8c05" :question/problem "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $x=-2$. The point $P(-2,1,-2)$ lies on $C$. The partial derivative is supplied:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f_y(x,y) & =\\frac{y-x}{\\sqrt{x(y+x)}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is a tangent vector to $C$ at $P$?" :question/worked-solution "Holding $x$ fixed means that $y$ varies, so the slice slope is $f_y(-2,1)$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m=f_y(-2,1) & =\\frac{\\left(1\\right)-\\left(-2\\right)}{\\sqrt{\\left(-2\\right)(\\left(1\\right)+\\left(-2\\right))}} \\\\ & =\\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe displayed quotient is evaluated at the supplied point; its denominator is nonzero. Simplifying the numerator and denominator gives the exact slope above.\n\nA change of $1$ in $y$ along the tangent gives a change of $\\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2}$ in $z$, with no change in $x$. A tangent direction is $\\langle 0,1,\\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2}\\rangle$.\n\nThe tangent line through $P(-2,1,-2)$ is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x&=-2 \\\\ z-(-2)&=\\left(\\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)(y-(1))\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe second plane is equivalently $\\frac{3 \\sqrt{2} y}{2} - z - \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2} - 2=0$. Normal vectors are $\\mathbf n_1=\\langle 1,0,0\\rangle$ and $\\mathbf n_2=\\langle 0,- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2},1\\rangle$. Their cross product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf n_1\\times\\mathbf n_2 & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i&\\mathbf j&\\mathbf k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & - \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2} & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ & =\\langle 0,-1,- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2}\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNegating this cross product gives $\\langle 0,1,\\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2}\\rangle$.\n\nAny nonzero scalar multiple is valid. The listed answer is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2\\left(\\langle 0,1,\\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2}\\rangle\\right) & =\\langle 0,-2,- 3 \\sqrt{2}\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIt has the required component ratio $v_z/v_y=\\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2}$."} {:answer/id #uuid "d6925a9c-c6c6-5fc0-bd0e-1d2a87ec6ad1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\langle 0,3,- \\frac{15 \\sqrt{2}}{4}\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707791} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "894b045c-1e31-59b1-ba1a-98a949ad987c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708022} {:answer/id #uuid "b5b1ca1b-c0c1-5a3d-87a2-37e36ba91230" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708034}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708034} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a0b8510-9892-556a-8e03-1b3fa0fe4537" :answer-field/key "$H(x,y)=\\langle \\frac{1}{x+1}, y^2\\rangle$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708003} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a225254-d2c6-5337-a636-e35c15a56a3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707999} {:answer/id #uuid "a26eb61a-d4b2-5866-a966-e0ec2bb41eca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708027}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707999} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b6be1fd-8a2c-5e3a-ad0b-7a15b9190b67" :answer-field/key "$Q(x,y)=\\langle \\frac{1}{x}, y^2\\rangle$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708004} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708014 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29420350-aa17-584d-a333-52a7c7d9d286" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708006} {:answer/id #uuid "82c903e6-70fb-51d6-b590-a59f3c55eeab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708021}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708006} :answer-field/id #uuid "39c0cd14-a81f-539f-8daf-b152867e3005" :answer-field/key "$U(x,y,z)=\\left(\\frac{1}{x+1}\\right)\\,\\mathbf i+(y^2)\\,\\mathbf j+\\left(\\frac{z}{y+1}\\right)\\,\\mathbf k$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708007} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "806c210a-2def-5c1b-8a03-96a12517eb5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708017} {:answer/id #uuid "fd804ac1-54b8-5e42-80db-b60141b8d3ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708047}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708017} :answer-field/id #uuid "3eb69669-b272-5476-bb7d-80afd7340fe4" :answer-field/key "$M(x,y,z)=\\langle x+2, y^2, z+x\\rangle$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708008} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82c0ebbc-4a48-5528-916c-34a97eb60772" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708020} {:answer/id #uuid "98bac681-7763-5876-adbd-dfbbff33fd58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708024}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708024} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e9038ec-5b24-5a1e-9878-eba5450bfb16" :answer-field/key "$S(x,y)=\\langle \\ln(y-1), \\sqrt{x-1}\\rangle$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708025}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6f871634-2896-5f28-a432-eb07d2e8419b" :question/problem "A vector field on $\\mathbb R^3$ assigns a vector in $\\mathbb R^3$ to each point of a subset of $\\mathbb R^3$.\n\nWhich of the following are vector fields on $\\mathbb R^3$? Use each function's natural real domain. Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A vector field on $\\mathbb R^3$ assigns a vector in $\\mathbb R^3$ to each point of a subset of $\\mathbb R^3$.\n\nCheck each function's declared inputs and output vectors.\n\n- **M.** $M(x,y,z)$ takes points in $\\mathbb R^3$. Its output has $3$ coordinates and is a vector in $\\mathbb R^3$. All components are defined on $\\mathbb R^3$. It maps its nonempty domain in $\\mathbb R^3$ to vectors in $\\mathbb R^3$, so it **is** a vector field on $\\mathbb R^3$.\n\n- **S.** $S(x,y)$ takes points in $\\mathbb R^2$. Its output has $2$ coordinates and is a vector in $\\mathbb R^2$. A logarithm needs a positive argument. A square root allows a zero radicand. Its natural domain is\n$$\nS_{S}=\\{(x,y)\\in \\mathbb R^2\\mid y-1>0,\\quad x-1\\ge0\\}.\n$$\nIt **is not** a vector field on $\\mathbb R^3$ because its declared inputs are not points of $\\mathbb R^3$ and its outputs are not vectors in $\\mathbb R^3$.\n\n- **U.** $U(x,y,z)$ takes points in $\\mathbb R^3$. Its three standard-basis coefficients give \n$$\nU(x,y,z)=\\langle \\frac{1}{x+1}, y^2, \\frac{z}{y+1}\\rangle.\n$$\nA denominator must be nonzero. Its natural domain is\n$$\nS_{U}=\\{(x,y,z)\\in \\mathbb R^3\\mid x+1\\ne0,\\quad y+1\\ne0\\}.\n$$\nIt maps its nonempty domain in $\\mathbb R^3$ to vectors in $\\mathbb R^3$, so it **is** a vector field on $\\mathbb R^3$.\n\nSelect $M$ and $U$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709444 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d0e7796-fae7-5497-aedb-d0234c9ab560" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709434} {:answer/id #uuid "588ec05c-c000-52f5-be4a-fe39041454fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709437} {:answer/id #uuid "665afda9-523d-54a1-ad10-655ecabcd496" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709439} {:answer/id #uuid "a8982c6d-922f-50c8-b237-3dd60353d270" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709443} {:answer/id #uuid "f3cd4a4e-6896-5e99-8bb5-f03d48c0a9b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709448}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709434} :answer-field/id #uuid "cdbc0289-fe2e-5a39-836e-578941851a82" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709445}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c565ef1b-4265-5336-8e9a-9ceec999ae7e" :question/problem "What is the amplitude of $f(x)=\\frac{7}{4}\\sin x$?" :question/worked-solution "To plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=\\sin x$.\n- Then, stretch it parallel to the $y$-axis by a stretch factor of $\\frac{7}{4}$.\n\nThe resulting graph is shown below.\n\n![](images/ed/edee0b0ce281e5e6579dfc8e833d095efa3fbc70fe61708c245a3ca778c62165.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the maximum value is $y_{\\max}=\\frac{7}{4}$ and the minimum value is $y_{\\min}=-\\frac{7}{4}$. Therefore, the amplitude is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{Amplitude} &= \\frac{y_{\\max}-y_{\\min}}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\frac{7}{4}-(-\\frac{7}{4})}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\frac{7}{4}+\\frac{7}{4}}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\frac{7}{2}}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{7}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709446 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "953b739f-a0d9-5b07-9d01-00692649b5d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709441}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709441} :answer-field/id #uuid "53ad02cc-4d5e-59d5-804e-4fb1f6599d52" :answer-field/key "amplitude" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709436}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "d57bf29f-23bb-5404-b7dd-508d2f703902" :question/problem "What is the amplitude of the function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{\\cos x}{\\frac{2}{3}}?\n$$\n\nAmplitude: {{amplitude}}" :question/worked-solution "Dividing by $\\frac{2}{3}$ is the same as multiplying by $\\frac{3}{2}$:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{\\cos x}{\\frac{2}{3}}=\\frac{3}{2}\\cos x.\n$$\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=\\cos x$.\n- Then, stretch it parallel to the $y$-axis by a stretch factor of $\\frac{3}{2}$.\n\nThe resulting graph is shown below.\n\n![](images/9c/9ca2b4f0f8ccdd98ebb462a2af2972dc08ae95af9a530436c19f37a6ac5d26ba.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the maximum value is $y_{\\max}=\\frac{3}{2}$ and the minimum value is $y_{\\min}=-\\frac{3}{2}$. Therefore, the amplitude is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{Amplitude} &= \\frac{y_{\\max}-y_{\\min}}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\frac{3}{2}-(-\\frac{3}{2})}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{3}{2}}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709603 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b6959aa-b411-50c1-b88c-13bf0143c11d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709596}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709596} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f3f40e2-0578-5bfa-9121-fec57649062b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709597}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7fff4698-89f1-5753-bfed-0ac0ac3ca5be" :question/problem "Given that the area spanned by the vectors $\\mathbf{u}=\\langle \\frac{3}{2},-4\\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{v}=\\langle a,6\\rangle$ equals zero, what is the value of $a$?\n\n$a=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Place the vectors in the columns of a matrix:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{2} & a \\\\ -4 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\det(M)=\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot6-a(-4)=9+4a.\n$$\n\nThe area is $|\\det(M)|$. It is zero exactly when the determinant is zero, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n9+4a&=0\\\\\n4a&=-9\\\\\na&=-\\frac{9}{4}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a check, the second components give the scale factor $6/(-4)=-3/2$. Multiplying the first component $3/2$ by this factor gives $-9/4$, so the completed vectors are parallel and span zero area."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709727 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c36968e-cc80-5c88-abd9-7cdf5ecbadf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$y=\\tan x-2$; its minimum value is $-1$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709725} {:answer/id #uuid "561c27d1-5951-514c-ae8e-498019cce232" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$y=\\tan x-1$; it has no minimum value." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709728} {:answer/id #uuid "743c883f-44cf-591d-927e-57e3376336d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$y=\\tan x-2$; it has no minimum value." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709731} {:answer/id #uuid "8f14ac0a-a66e-52b5-9099-a0b0bbc62e42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$y=\\tan x+2$; it has no minimum value." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709734} {:answer/id #uuid "97f8c226-ab19-5b3f-bd9c-2419d4ea1fe1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$y=\\tan x-2$; its minimum value is $-2$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709735}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709731} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab318bf7-b4d6-5e5c-a793-f51cd19098aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709738}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "50182077-23bf-59c9-aac0-f4b42aef17fb" :question/problem "![A portion of a translated tangent curve with the exact point P marked.](images/cc/cc5bced3bf4c0545426d56fe3c9cba8f181565bb1b454206ad9677331be1514b.png)\n\nThe graph shows a portion of $y=\\tan x+D$ and contains the exact point $P=(\\frac{\\pi}{4},-1)$. Recall that $\\tan\\frac{\\pi}{4}=1$.\n\nWhich statement gives **both** the equation of the curve and whether the full function has a minimum value? Consider all real $x$ for which the function is defined." :question/worked-solution "Use the point $P$ to compare the translated graph with $y=\\tan x$ at the **same** horizontal coordinate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-1&=\\tan\\frac{\\pi}{4}+D\\\\\n-1&=1+D\\\\\nD&=-2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, start with $y=\\tan x$ and shift it by $2$ units **down**. The equation is $y=\\tan x-2$.\n\n![The full tangent graph shifted two units down.](images/b9/b9d101d16896a81064c1d7406fbbea2b0529fc6a08aceb7a7614f40ce9af38c2.png)\n\nThe small portion in the question does not show the full range. On every full branch, tangent takes arbitrarily negative values. A vertical shift preserves this property, so the function **has no minimum value**. Neither the marked height $-1$ nor the vertical intercept $-2$ is a minimum.\n\nTherefore, the correct statement is: $y=\\tan x-2$; it has no minimum value."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709902 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c3da79d-ebb2-5e99-8771-89b84bb9d048" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{6 \\left(-2 + \\sqrt{2}\\right)}{\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709897} {:answer/id #uuid "48feb464-f6de-5ff9-8070-a789ae952e60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{6 \\sqrt{2}}{\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709900} {:answer/id #uuid "6151ba92-2d71-5adb-90c7-3db071fda483" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{18 \\left(-2 + \\sqrt{2}\\right)}{\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709901} {:answer/id #uuid "6cdcf3f3-b29b-53c6-b5a0-8785e288c1cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{6 \\left(2 - \\sqrt{2}\\right)}{\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709903} {:answer/id #uuid "e83340aa-9966-58b1-9ad8-b5c416594c8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\sqrt{5} \\left(2 - \\sqrt{2}\\right)}{\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709916}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709897} :answer-field/id #uuid "b23e5cae-7780-5b6b-ae9f-52dc1dffcdc6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709909}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "65076c36-16b6-5b2b-890e-1f4a785e7c2b" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{C}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}(x+z))\\,\\text{d}s$ along the line segment from $(-2,4,-4)$ to $(-3,6,-2).$" :question/worked-solution "For scalar arc length, use\n\n$$\n\\int_C f\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_0^1 f(\\mathbf r(t))\\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t\n$$\n\nParametrize the segment and check its endpoints:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r(t)&=A+t(B-A) \\\\  &=\\left(- t - 2,2 t + 4,2 t - 4\\right) \\\\  \\mathbf r(0)&=\\left(-2,4,-4\\right) \\\\  \\mathbf r(1)&=\\left(-3,6,-2\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $0\\le t\\le1$, the velocity and speed are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)&=\\left(-1,2,2\\right) \\\\  \\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(-1)^2+(2)^2+(2)^2} \\\\  &=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute all three coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf r(t))&=\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}((- t - 2)+(2 t - 4))\\right) \\\\  &=\\cos{\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{4} - \\frac{3 \\pi}{2} \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equivalent definite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f\\,\\mathrm{d}s&=3{\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\cos{\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{4} - \\frac{3 \\pi}{2} \\right)})\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse $u=\\frac{\\pi t}{4} - \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}$ and $\\mathrm{d}u=\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t$. The new bounds are $u(0)=- \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}$ and $u(1)=- \\frac{5 \\pi}{4}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I&=\\frac{12}{\\pi}\\int_{- \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{- \\frac{5 \\pi}{4}}\\cos u\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &=\\frac{12}{\\pi}\\left[\\sin u\\right]_{- \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{- \\frac{5 \\pi}{4}} \\\\  &=\\frac{12}{\\pi}\\left(\\sin\\left(- \\frac{5 \\pi}{4}\\right)-\\sin\\left(- \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}\\right)\\right) \\\\  &=\\frac{12}{\\pi}\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)-(1)\\right) \\\\  &=\\frac{6 \\left(-2 + \\sqrt{2}\\right)}{\\pi}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:answer/id #uuid "2160a09e-87e7-5413-8148-a60fb3c8c78e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\log_{3}(\\frac{1}{3}) \\approx 1.442" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710244} {:answer/id #uuid "3ed19971-577b-5083-a4b2-7adcc0264721" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\log_{1.442}(\\frac{1}{3}) \\approx 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710248} {:answer/id #uuid "598bd888-6b8a-532f-864d-5d2d9431faf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\log_{2.080}(\\frac{1}{3}) \\approx 9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710252} {:answer/id #uuid "5e34e244-4264-5365-9f48-966681239816" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\log_{10}(\\frac{1}{3}) \\approx 2.154" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710253} {:answer/id #uuid "ca86f322-1281-51ba-abd6-300ef5f4f7c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\log_{29}(\\frac{1}{4}) \\approx 2.321" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710259} {:answer/id #uuid "e7d306de-200a-5749-beb3-04289a5bcd21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\log_{9}(\\frac{1}{3}) \\approx 2.080" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710261} {:answer/id #uuid "87b5de75-8e2f-5de4-9775-3da8f6159aa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{1}{2},0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710712} {:answer/id #uuid "b8fcd68a-1072-5461-9d6d-caf71bc3239a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{3}{2},0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710716} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711017 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30d42a46-199b-5876-a577-02df07046c81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711021}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711021} :answer-field/id #uuid "30e85019-16b8-5fbd-a30d-c444bad2494a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711022} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41f7b3c9-a556-53a6-8f1b-8f8cff7c381e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711024}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711024} :answer-field/id #uuid "3bc3f86c-4516-5f01-9ec9-8dff4027c465" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711023}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "18e6fb5a-75af-5a6c-97e9-934ada084867" :question/problem "Find where the normal line to the curve $y=\\frac{1}{x}-1$ at the point $(2,- \\frac{1}{2})$ intersects the $x$-axis.\n\nThe intersection is $(${{field-1}}$,$ {{field-2}}$)$. Give exact values." :question/worked-solution "Rewrite the radical or reciprocal using powers, then differentiate.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x)&=-1 + \\frac{1}{x}, \\\\f'(x)&=- \\frac{1}{x^{2}}=- \\frac{1}{x^{2}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluate the tangent slope and take its negative reciprocal to find the normal slope.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm_t=f'(2)&=- \\frac{1}{(2)^{2}}=- \\frac{1}{4}, \\\\m_n=-\\frac{1}{m_t}&=-\\frac{1}{\\left(- \\frac{1}{4}\\right)}=4.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse point-slope form through $(2,- \\frac{1}{2})$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny-\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right)&=4(x-(2)), \\\\y&=4 x - \\frac{17}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the $x$-axis, $y=0$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n0&=4x+\\left(- \\frac{17}{2}\\right), \\\\x&=\\frac{17}{8}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe intersection is $(\\frac{17}{8},0)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711025 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ad1639f-b64a-5769-82ed-02e05839f62c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711027}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711027} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdee68f2-72fc-5bc7-985f-5b0ac15788eb" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711034} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a95b0ec-864a-50e4-94a8-d87a628dd52c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711020}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711020} :answer-field/id #uuid "f06268c3-24a7-51e0-9689-f128fcc12de6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711038}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "61986396-db29-5c50-b599-1e03204a89b9" :question/problem "Find where the normal line to the curve $y=\\sqrt{x^{3}}-3$ at the point $(4,5)$ intersects the $y$-axis.\n\nThe intersection is $(${{field-1}}$,$ {{field-2}}$)$. Give exact values." :question/worked-solution "Rewrite the radical or reciprocal using powers, then differentiate.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x)&=x^{\\frac{3}{2}} - 3, \\\\f'(x)&=\\frac{3 x^{\\frac{1}{2}}}{2}=\\frac{3 \\sqrt{x}}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluate the tangent slope and take its negative reciprocal to find the normal slope.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm_t=f'(4)&=\\frac{3 \\sqrt{(4)}}{2}=3, \\\\m_n=-\\frac{1}{m_t}&=-\\frac{1}{(3)}=- \\frac{1}{3}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse point-slope form through $(4,5)$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny-(5)&=- \\frac{1}{3}(x-(4)), \\\\y&=- \\frac{x}{3} + \\frac{19}{3}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the $y$-axis, $x=0$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny&=- \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 0+\\left(\\frac{19}{3}\\right), \\\\y&=\\frac{19}{3}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe intersection is $(0,\\frac{19}{3})$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711030 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20edf35f-4a33-5ca6-bc4a-5f935bb93ca9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{265}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711019}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711019} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc22fe5f-5f84-55fc-ad97-6ac8556ab4e4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711033} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c60c85ea-4339-511d-9c52-5fc38cb0d52b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711036}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711036} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4308f6f-eda3-5d2f-ade2-9a50a4b130dc" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711040}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a97a2962-6ba1-5604-abc4-227d138bb2de" :question/problem "Find where the normal line to the curve $y=-3\\sqrt[4]{x}$ at the point $(16,-6)$ intersects the $x$-axis.\n\nThe intersection is $(${{field-1}}$,$ {{field-2}}$)$. Give exact values." :question/worked-solution "Rewrite the radical or reciprocal using powers, then differentiate.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x)&=- 3 x^{\\frac{1}{4}}, \\\\f'(x)&=- \\frac{3}{4 x^{\\frac{3}{4}}}=- \\frac{3}{4 x^{\\frac{3}{4}}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluate the tangent slope and take its negative reciprocal to find the normal slope.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm_t=f'(16)&=- \\frac{3}{4 (16)^{\\frac{3}{4}}}=- \\frac{3}{32}, \\\\m_n=-\\frac{1}{m_t}&=-\\frac{1}{\\left(- \\frac{3}{32}\\right)}=\\frac{32}{3}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse point-slope form through $(16,-6)$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny-(-6)&=\\frac{32}{3}(x-(16)), \\\\y&=\\frac{32 x}{3} - \\frac{530}{3}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the $x$-axis, $y=0$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n0&=\\frac{32}{3}x+\\left(- \\frac{530}{3}\\right), \\\\x&=\\frac{265}{16}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe intersection is $(\\frac{265}{16},0)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711039 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9fe8278c-d0df-516b-99d2-a2a722f9b277" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711028}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711028} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac75c705-8a67-5f78-88e8-7c0b3efa2b72" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711031} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7bbb8880-c729-504e-8d3e-58488413cb12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711026}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711026} :answer-field/id #uuid "cddebd60-d727-5248-b03f-c0f5755c0555" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711037}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f0c2287a-fb5a-504a-9902-8dd3de3bd720" :question/problem "Find where the normal line to the curve $y=3\\sqrt[3]{x^{2}}-1$ at the point $(1,2)$ intersects the $y$-axis.\n\nThe intersection is $(${{field-1}}$,$ {{field-2}}$)$. Give exact values." :question/worked-solution "Rewrite the radical or reciprocal using powers, then differentiate.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x)&=3 x^{\\frac{2}{3}} - 1, \\\\f'(x)&=\\frac{2}{x^{\\frac{1}{3}}}=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{x}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluate the tangent slope and take its negative reciprocal to find the normal slope.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm_t=f'(1)&=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{(1)}}=2, \\\\m_n=-\\frac{1}{m_t}&=-\\frac{1}{(2)}=- \\frac{1}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse point-slope form through $(1,2)$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny-(2)&=- \\frac{1}{2}(x-(1)), \\\\y&=- \\frac{x}{2} + \\frac{5}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the $y$-axis, $x=0$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny&=- \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 0+\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right), \\\\y&=\\frac{5}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe intersection is $(0,\\frac{5}{2})$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711056 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "672a3e83-d2f3-516d-ad05-e4955657a2d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711055}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711055} :answer-field/id #uuid "97e0f03e-c086-5b58-9ad3-8e7be34173cb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711058} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5731d32f-6d9c-5e8d-8dea-fd32ad0d1d2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{46}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711051}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711051} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5b31739-414a-50c0-93d4-b88fd0185e61" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711059}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "6ffc271a-c092-532f-b23f-0664c0e4304c" :question/problem "Find where the normal line to the curve $y=4\\sqrt{x}+3x+2$ at the point with $x$-coordinate $1$ intersects the $y$-axis.\n\nThe intersection is $(${{field-1}}$,$ {{field-2}}$)$. Give exact values." :question/worked-solution "First find the point on the curve.\n\n$$\nf(1)=4\\sqrt{(1)}+3(1)+2=9.\n$$\n\nThe normal passes through $(1,9)$.\n\nRewrite the radical or reciprocal using powers, then differentiate.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x)&=4 x^{\\frac{1}{2}} + 3 x + 2, \\\\f'(x)&=3 + \\frac{2}{x^{\\frac{1}{2}}}=3 + \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluate the tangent slope and take its negative reciprocal to find the normal slope.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm_t=f'(1)&=3 + \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{(1)}}=5, \\\\m_n=-\\frac{1}{m_t}&=-\\frac{1}{(5)}=- \\frac{1}{5}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse point-slope form through $(1,9)$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny-(9)&=- \\frac{1}{5}(x-(1)), \\\\y&=- \\frac{x}{5} + \\frac{46}{5}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the $y$-axis, $x=0$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny&=- \\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 0+\\left(\\frac{46}{5}\\right), \\\\y&=\\frac{46}{5}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe intersection is $(0,\\frac{46}{5})$."} {:answer/id #uuid "170025e4-1ff1-5339-aaff-2ca308d2dcf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(0,-\\frac{25}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711065} {:answer/id #uuid "449ae0dc-5697-5716-84ec-8b78d5783865" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{13}{3},0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711069} {:answer/id #uuid "6848d39a-e195-50e7-9d30-692e28d6ba01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(0,\\frac{25}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711071} {:answer/id #uuid "7233556c-6227-5f02-9efa-f76bc8c1dbf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{17}{3},0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711073} {:answer/id #uuid "96627440-41aa-59a9-8975-f9d4692df309" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(0,\\frac{7}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711076} {:answer/id #uuid "9cef1c15-052b-5ccb-850b-59d512ca7d22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{1}{3},0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711077} {:answer/id #uuid "a0b80f5d-d877-5d89-b2bc-4d457114223e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(0,\\frac{25}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711078} {:answer/id #uuid "ef8b7ca0-1eb6-5f5e-a4cd-22a986a653df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{3}{2},0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711081} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711326 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a73a181-a848-569c-a622-74cdad86fad0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711321} {:answer/id #uuid "afaff60d-0c88-58d0-90d2-f96b5c4da5ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711335} {:answer/id #uuid "ead10aa1-0e06-5bfc-82de-1f57e77729f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711340} {:answer/id #uuid "eb27843d-1eff-5a8e-a353-18caab0c17c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711341} {:answer/id #uuid "fd2107fb-8e2c-532b-9d6e-53cbf53d05f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711342}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711341} :answer-field/id #uuid "2fca0757-d32b-51fb-967f-c1396cb9c016" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711325}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "325ff2e4-ed82-59d7-8afd-e09d94d4b8e3" :question/problem "Find the slope of the tangent at the point $(- \\frac{\\pi}{6},1)$ for the curve $y \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$." :question/worked-solution "Treat $y$ as a function of $x$. Use the product rule on the cosine product; the derivative of $\\cos(x)$ is $-\\sin(x)$.\n\nDifferentiate both sides with respect to $x$, then collect the derivative terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)&=\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)\\\\\n\\frac{dy}{dx} \\cos{\\left(x \\right)} - y \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}&=0\\\\\n\\left(\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\\left(- y \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)\\\\\n\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\\frac{- y \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}}{\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $(- \\frac{\\pi}{6},1)$, the coefficient of $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$ is $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\ne 0$. Substitute the point to obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm&=\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{(- \\frac{\\pi}{6},1)}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}}{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}}\\\\\n&=- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712077 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47fa0ad3-a5e1-5948-b2cf-73943046a869" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 2 \\pi \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} + 2 \\pi \\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712066} {:answer/id #uuid "6b8b2f75-5c95-55eb-a761-bcfd4b57c9ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 4 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} + 4 \\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712071} {:answer/id #uuid "7d790571-c97a-5ed7-befc-1cf32f325ef0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 2 \\pi \\ln{\\left(4 \\right)} + 2 \\pi \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712073} {:answer/id #uuid "956eebc3-9ebb-5d3a-ac09-c4abee8d7c36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 \\pi \\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712075} {:answer/id #uuid "b1d687fe-932a-56e8-a2b9-b082c728cfc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712080}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712066} :answer-field/id #uuid "2bccab4f-7b27-525e-ab51-3552a1e92d8f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712060}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9d75ee31-a69f-5deb-847b-a58db14e4d91" :question/problem "Evaluate\n\n$$\n\\iint_R\\left(\\frac{2 y \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + 2}{y}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nHere $R=[- \\frac{\\pi}{2},\\frac{\\pi}{2}]\\times[2,4]$." :question/worked-solution "The region is $R=[- \\frac{\\pi}{2},\\frac{\\pi}{2}]\\times[2,4]$. Its interval lengths are $L_x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}-\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)=\\pi$ and $L_y=4-(2)=2$.\n\nDivide term by term and collect the single-variable terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\frac{2 y \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + 2}{y}\\\\\n&=2 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + \\frac{2}{y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy linearity, evaluate each signed single-variable contribution using the interval length of the absent variable.\n\nThe term in $y$ uses the $x$-interval length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\iint_R\\left(\\frac{2}{y}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}A\\\\\n&=\\pi\\int_{2}^{4}\\frac{2}{y}\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\\n&=\\pi\\left[2 \\ln{\\left(y \\right)}\\right]_{2}^{4}\\\\\n&=\\pi\\left(\\left(2 \\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}\\right)-\\left(2 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}\\right)\\right)\\\\\n&=- 2 \\pi \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} + 2 \\pi \\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe term in $x$ uses the $y$-interval length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\iint_R\\left(2 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}A\\\\\n&=2\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}2 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\\n&=2\\left[- 2 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right]_{- \\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\\\\n&=2\\left(\\left(0\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\right)\\\\\n&=0.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining the signed contributions gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I&=\\left(- 2 \\pi \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} + 2 \\pi \\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}\\right) + \\left(0\\right)\\\\\n&=\\boxed{- 2 \\pi \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} + 2 \\pi \\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712085 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "164d21aa-23d4-5962-8304-4e4b6551a2b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\pi + 2 + \\pi \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712059} {:answer/id #uuid "5ddca6b2-3839-548e-9dbb-b82cf600ddd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\pi - 2 \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)} + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712069} {:answer/id #uuid "9d2afddb-ec04-5dfb-a529-ef1a6743a51a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\pi \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)} - \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712076} {:answer/id #uuid "a1f269e7-e13f-567c-b63b-c67a1da1065f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 4 \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)} - \\pi + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712079} {:answer/id #uuid "dee2fda3-3f58-51dd-ad15-12515497b030" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\pi \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)} - \\pi + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712088}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712088} :answer-field/id #uuid "a088df9c-0ed9-5c91-8c4f-c5e24de7118e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712078}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "cad63c03-1a5e-5446-8b72-d688660a9494" :question/problem "Evaluate\n\n$$\n\\iint_R\\left(\\frac{y \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} - y - 2}{y}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nHere $R=[\\frac{\\pi}{2},\\pi]\\times[1,3]$." :question/worked-solution "The region is $R=[\\frac{\\pi}{2},\\pi]\\times[1,3]$. Its interval lengths are $L_x=\\pi-\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ and $L_y=3-(1)=2$.\n\nDivide term by term and collect the single-variable terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\frac{y \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} - y - 2}{y}\\\\\n&=\\sin{\\left(x \\right)} - 1 - \\frac{2}{y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy linearity, evaluate each signed single-variable contribution using the interval length of the absent variable.\n\nThe term in $y$ uses the $x$-interval length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\iint_R\\left(- \\frac{2}{y}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}A\\\\\n&=\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\int_{1}^{3}- \\frac{2}{y}\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\\n&=\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\left[- 2 \\ln{\\left(y \\right)}\\right]_{1}^{3}\\\\\n&=\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\left(\\left(- 2 \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\right)\\\\\n&=- \\pi \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe term in $x$ uses the $y$-interval length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\iint_R\\left(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}A\\\\\n&=2\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\\n&=2\\left[- \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}\\\\\n&=2\\left(\\left(1\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\right)\\\\\n&=2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe constant contributes its value times the full rectangle area:\n\n$$\n-1\\cdot\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)\\cdot(2)=- \\pi.\n$$\n\nCombining the signed contributions gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I&=\\left(- \\pi \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}\\right) + \\left(2\\right) + \\left(- \\pi\\right)\\\\\n&=\\boxed{- \\pi \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)} - \\pi + 2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712144 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f864bf7-59e7-5a5b-b0c4-4f728d17f4b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\pi - \\frac{\\pi \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}{2} + \\frac{\\pi \\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712121} {:answer/id #uuid "1e589833-726d-5e0d-9d89-423eb3b3bd26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4 - \\pi + \\frac{\\pi \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}{2} + \\frac{\\pi \\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712123} {:answer/id #uuid "2de4608a-eec1-5e31-bf82-88c423c1f450" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4 - \\pi + \\frac{\\pi \\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712124} {:answer/id #uuid "6fa8c7d9-9b07-5ddf-af9d-515dbc58597d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4 - \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712129} {:answer/id #uuid "e538399b-3c9c-5a9c-9671-d8616a82d372" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4 - \\pi - \\frac{\\pi \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}{2} + \\frac{\\pi \\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712143}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712143} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbf1f2c4-3678-508f-8900-2c899f9a1a39" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712142}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e6f0cd3b-3675-5561-93e8-838db9662fe0" :question/problem "Evaluate\n\n$$\n\\iint_R\\left(\\frac{1 + y\\left(- 3 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} - 1\\right) + y \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}}{y}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nHere $R=\\{(x,y):\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\le x\\le \\pi,\\ 2\\le y\\le 4\\}$." :question/worked-solution "The region is $R=[\\frac{\\pi}{2},\\pi]\\times[2,4]$. Its interval lengths are $L_x=\\pi-\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ and $L_y=4-(2)=2$.\n\nDivide term by term and collect the single-variable terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\frac{1 + y\\left(- 3 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} - 1\\right) + y \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}}{y}\\\\\n&=- 2 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} - 1 + \\frac{1}{y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy linearity, evaluate each signed single-variable contribution using the interval length of the absent variable.\n\nThe term in $y$ uses the $x$-interval length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\iint_R\\left(\\frac{1}{y}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}A\\\\\n&=\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\int_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{y}\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\\n&=\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\left[\\ln{\\left(y \\right)}\\right]_{2}^{4}\\\\\n&=\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\left(\\left(\\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}\\right)-\\left(\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}\\right)\\right)\\\\\n&=- \\frac{\\pi \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}{2} + \\frac{\\pi \\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe term in $x$ uses the $y$-interval length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\iint_R\\left(- 2 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}A\\\\\n&=2\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}- 2 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\\n&=2\\left[2 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}\\\\\n&=2\\left(\\left(-2\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\right)\\\\\n&=-4.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe constant contributes its value times the full rectangle area:\n\n$$\n-1\\cdot\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)\\cdot(2)=- \\pi.\n$$\n\nCombining the signed contributions gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I&=\\left(- \\frac{\\pi \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}{2} + \\frac{\\pi \\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}}{2}\\right) + \\left(-4\\right) + \\left(- \\pi\\right)\\\\\n&=\\boxed{-4 - \\pi - \\frac{\\pi \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}{2} + \\frac{\\pi \\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}}{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712262 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b5aa8fb-501b-5ebb-93ed-bb1a55860549" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712240} {:answer/id #uuid "78aca233-6440-5117-aa4d-10cf74faed97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712256} {:answer/id #uuid "ac3babac-b68d-5192-81ff-c4c74771cd6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712258} {:answer/id #uuid "c8b98947-eec5-58f3-8259-6f5fa48a8467" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{11}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712264} {:answer/id #uuid "fb26bd62-ca00-5372-aa3e-eb6d775c96cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712273}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712264} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b506039-078c-5852-9485-349cec765732" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712245}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "bc4624ca-e670-5dc7-84f5-78bb4bd61e93" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\iint_R f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}A$, where $R$ is the union of the following rectangles and\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\begin{cases}3 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}&\\frac{\\pi}{2}<x<\\pi,\\ -2<y<0\\\\y \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}&\\frac{\\pi}{2}<x<\\pi,\\ 0<y<1.\\end{cases}\n$$\n\nSet $f=0$ on the region boundaries." :question/worked-solution "Match each formula to its coordinate rectangle:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R_1&=(\\frac{\\pi}{2},\\pi)\\times(-2,0)\\\\R_2&=(\\frac{\\pi}{2},\\pi)\\times(0,1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe interiors do not overlap, and the boundaries have area zero. Apply additivity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iint_R f\\,\\mathrm{d}A&=\\sum_{j=1}^{2} I_j,\\\\I_j&=\\iint_{R_j}f\\,\\mathrm{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn $R_1$, separate the coordinate factors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\iint_{R_1}(3 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)})\\,\\mathrm{d}A\\\\&=\\left(\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}(\\cos{\\left(x \\right)})\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\right)\\left(\\int_{-2}^{0}(3)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\right)\\\\&=\\left[\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}\\left[3 y\\right]_{-2}^{0}\\\\&=\\left(\\sin{\\left(\\left(\\pi\\right) \\right)}-(\\sin{\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) \\right)})\\right)\\left(3 \\left(0\\right)-(3 \\left(-2\\right))\\right)\\\\&=\\left(-1\\right)\\left(6\\right)=-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn $R_2$, separate the coordinate factors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\iint_{R_2}(y \\sin{\\left(x \\right)})\\,\\mathrm{d}A\\\\&=\\left(\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)})\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\right)\\left(\\int_{0}^{1}(y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\right)\\\\&=\\left[- \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}\\left[\\frac{y^{2}}{2}\\right]_{0}^{1}\\\\&=\\left(- \\cos{\\left(\\left(\\pi\\right) \\right)}-(- \\cos{\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) \\right)})\\right)\\left(\\frac{\\left(1\\right)^{2}}{2}-\\left(\\frac{\\left(0\\right)^{2}}{2}\\right)\\right)\\\\&=\\left(1\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the signed contributions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iint_R f\\,\\mathrm{d}A&=\\left(-6\\right)\\\\&\\quad+\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\\\&=\\boxed{- \\frac{11}{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712367 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30173ae3-8e67-51ee-8f89-6d95e51d48f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712371} {:answer/id #uuid "4a8af6c3-3974-551e-86c5-54fae030a860" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{39}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712375} {:answer/id #uuid "6a176c1e-75bb-5e7b-9fc7-a3eff06746aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712379} {:answer/id #uuid "786bf17a-0e1a-5dcd-9358-c27d37d5dae7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{23}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712382} {:answer/id #uuid "d9ebf3b9-f2c5-5fbf-a6bb-dcc503a0fa0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712398}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712382} :answer-field/id #uuid "b77e2fca-86f8-5a8b-908f-6953377a408c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712391}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0d7a881e-8d60-5bd0-b8bc-99254fd65d35" :question/problem "Evaluate\n\n$$\n{\\int}_{C}F\\cdot\\text{d}r\n$$ given that $F(x,y)=(2 y - 1)\\,i+(2 x - y + 1)\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=(- 2 t - 2)\\,i+(- t - 1)\\,j$ for $t\\in[0,1].$\n\n*Hint:* Use\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm d r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt\n$$." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=- 2 t - 2,\\quad y=- t - 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t)) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=(2 y - 1)\\,i+(2 x - y + 1)\\,j \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left(2 \\left(- t - 1\\right) - 1\\right)\\,i \\\\ &{} +\\left(2 \\left(- 2 t - 2\\right) - \\left(- t - 1\\right) + 1\\right)\\,j\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=(- 2 t - 3)\\,i+(- 3 t - 2)\\,j\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- 2 t - 2)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- t - 1)\\,j \\\\  & =(-2)\\,i+(-1)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left({(- 2 t - 3)\\,i+(- 3 t - 2)\\,j}\\right) \\\\ &{} \\cdot\\left({(-2)\\,i+(-1)\\,j}\\right)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(- 2 t - 3)\\cdot(-2)+(- 3 t - 2) \\\\ &{} \\cdot(-1)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\left({4 t + 6}\\right)+\\left({3 t + 2}\\right) \\\\ &=7 t + 8\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\int_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{1}\\left({7 t + 8}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[{\\frac{7 t^{2}}{2} + 8 t}\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ &=((8)+\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right))-((0)+(0)) \\\\ &=\\left(\\frac{23}{2}\\right)-(0) \\\\ &=\\frac{23}{2}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712424 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29477c51-cc0e-56ca-9e44-6a38ea99d817" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712407} {:answer/id #uuid "29a3b855-7222-5e9a-a7b7-ebd50cb832c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{4} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712408} {:answer/id #uuid "7a139725-ead0-51d8-beda-22a1c85ff1fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712418} {:answer/id #uuid "819b664c-c934-5e80-8ece-fdb3bc7de37b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{\\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712420} {:answer/id #uuid "f6994e0e-9339-5b85-818f-d35db94e46c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712437}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712418} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b226c18-9361-5cb6-947b-2898d0f31d57" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712413}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9792dbb8-f58a-58d7-804e-352aa1151b07" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral\n$$\n\\iint_R \\frac{\\sin x}{y^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}A\n$$\nover the rectangle $R=[0,\\frac{\\pi}{2}]\\times[0,1].$" :question/worked-solution "The continuous integrand separates on the rectangle:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x,y)&=\\frac{\\sin x}{y^{2} + 1},\\\\\n&=\\left(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{y^{2} + 1}\\right).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$Apply the multiplicative property:\n$$\nI=\\left(\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\right)\\left(\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{1}{y^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\right).\n$$$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x&=- \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}+C_1,\\\\\n\\int \\frac{1}{y^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}y&=\\arctan{\\left(y \\right)}+C_2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$Evaluate upper minus lower in each factor, then multiply:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left[- \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\left[\\arctan{\\left(y \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{1}\\\\\n&=\\left(0-\\left(-1\\right)\\right)\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}-\\left(0\\right)\\right)\\\\\n&=\\left(1\\right)\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{\\pi}{4}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712431 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23379dcf-6c14-5233-94aa-201087fbfb37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712406} {:answer/id #uuid "498ec02d-74f0-5f6a-9c1d-328db98d774b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1 + e^{-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712412} {:answer/id #uuid "5eeba84f-ce3d-51ef-b31f-289237f32b63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712416} {:answer/id #uuid "b659317d-6fd6-5ea4-b7d1-a3546f29e3e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1 + e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712428} {:answer/id #uuid "e082293f-e7d2-554b-884b-26392d5817aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712432}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712432} :answer-field/id #uuid "89900d96-5b6a-5100-b13d-d6dff2b24389" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712421}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "def3a09b-5917-5e5a-9c1b-b923589ac7b1" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral\n$$\n\\iint_R \\frac{\\cos x}{y}\\,\\mathrm{d}A\n$$\nover the rectangle $R=[0,\\frac{\\pi}{2}]\\times[1,e^{2}].$" :question/worked-solution "The continuous integrand separates on the rectangle:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x,y)&=\\frac{\\cos x}{y},\\\\\n&=\\left(\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{y}\\right).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$Apply the multiplicative property:\n$$\nI=\\left(\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\right)\\left(\\int_{1}^{e^{2}} \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\right).\n$$$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x&=\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}+C_1,\\\\\n\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\mathrm{d}y&=\\ln{\\left(y \\right)}+C_2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$Evaluate upper minus lower in each factor, then multiply:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left[\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\left[\\ln{\\left(y \\right)}\\right]_{1}^{e^{2}}\\\\\n&=\\left(1-\\left(0\\right)\\right)\\left(2-\\left(0\\right)\\right)\\\\\n&=\\left(1\\right)\\left(2\\right)\\\\\n&=2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712453 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d48242b-6023-5db7-8d3a-eeecb6026126" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi \\left(4 + 5 \\pi\\right)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712442} {:answer/id #uuid "6e88f163-54a1-5d50-9758-c76af130019a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\pi \\left(\\pi + 4\\right)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712451} {:answer/id #uuid "d3bb970f-214a-5e0c-9e0d-2f2a0c88e94d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 + 6 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712461} {:answer/id #uuid "e2037cf7-ebea-5360-9d1d-cb3ea7e9f088" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712464} {:answer/id #uuid "f5f9a9b7-eb83-56cd-b7b6-22fbbf7aac3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi \\left(- 5 \\pi - 4\\right)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712466}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712451} :answer-field/id #uuid "0cce83b1-f5e4-552f-8181-ec9a1b346cf5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712439}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "83d3c56a-8bde-57d4-8339-cfbeec8ae536" :question/problem "Evaluate\n\n$$\n{\\int}_{C}F\\cdot\\text{d}r\n$$ given that $F(x,y)=(x + 1)\\,i+(y + 2)\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j$ for $t\\in[\\pi,2 \\pi].$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)},\\quad y=t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t)) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=(x + 1)\\,i+(y + 2)\\,j \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left(\\left(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) + 1\\right)\\,i \\\\ &{} +\\left(\\left(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) + 2\\right)\\,j\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 1)\\,i \\\\ &{} +(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2)\\,j\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}r^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i \\\\ &{} +\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i \\\\ &{} +(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left({\\begin{aligned}&(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 1)\\,i \\\\ &{} +(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2)\\,j\\end{aligned}}\\right) \\\\ &{} \\cdot\\left({\\begin{aligned}&(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i \\\\ &{} +(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,j\\end{aligned}}\\right)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 1) \\\\ &{} \\cdot(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}) \\\\ &{} +(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2) \\\\ &{} \\cdot(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left({\\begin{aligned}&t^{2} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + t \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}  \\\\ &{} + t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}}\\right) \\\\ &{} +\\left({\\begin{aligned}&- t^{2} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}  \\\\ &{} + t \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}}\\right)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&- 2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + t  \\\\ &{} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\int_{\\pi}^{2 \\pi}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{\\pi}^{2 \\pi}\\left({\\begin{aligned}&- 2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + t  \\\\ &{} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[{\\frac{t^{2}}{2} + t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}}\\right]_{\\pi}^{2 \\pi} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&((2 \\pi^{2})+(0)+(4 \\pi)) \\\\ &{} -(\\left(\\frac{\\pi^{2}}{2}\\right)+(0)+(- 2 \\pi))\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=(4 \\pi + 2 \\pi^{2})-(- 2 \\pi + \\frac{\\pi^{2}}{2}) \\\\ &=\\frac{3 \\pi \\left(\\pi + 4\\right)}{2}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nThe offset terms integrate by the reverse product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(\\frac{t^{2}}{2} + t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\begin{aligned}&- 2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + t  \\\\ &{} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713413 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "147cffcc-6699-58d3-9025-8721ab76d5a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\quad x\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713412} {:answer/id #uuid "280df5a3-19d1-5562-bea4-3c6e693e0985" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\quad x\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713417} {:answer/id #uuid "33677cfe-bdbe-5319-ba76-ebc6dc147973" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\quad y\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713419} {:answer/id #uuid "5032cc5e-2fd2-54de-9ef1-b8522865e44d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{No solution}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713426} {:answer/id #uuid "88169f54-cace-5a9b-9b6b-5027930f9473" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\quad y\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713432}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713412} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4b32cf7-163f-5023-bced-ecd53180d3ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713438}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "1961d6a3-1508-5420-8c4c-782e89040b3e" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}0 & -2 & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 3 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nUse Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "The first coefficient column is zero. The leading coefficient is in the $y$-column. Scale the entire first row using $R_1\\leftarrow (-\\frac{1}{2})R_1$:\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}0 & 1 & -\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 0 & 3 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThen use $R_2\\leftarrow R_2-(3)R_1$. The augmented entry becomes $-2-(3)(-\\frac{2}{3})=0$:\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}0 & 1 & -\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe last row says $0x+0y=0$, so it imposes no restriction. The remaining equation is $y=-\\frac{2}{3}$. Here $y$ is basic and $x$ is free: there is no pivot in the $x$-column. The general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\quad x\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)\n$$\n\nwhere $x$ is any real number."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713414 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f7798a1-c279-5611-a2e7-2d4b7a9f3477" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\quad x\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713423} {:answer/id #uuid "45d6df5f-553a-5b04-87ca-58f233263fe4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\quad y\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713424} {:answer/id #uuid "7b8e4452-2f91-5836-ac6f-35058a5b155f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{6} \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\quad y\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713430} {:answer/id #uuid "8933e10b-e07a-5610-9576-849f1a792c66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\quad x\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713433} {:answer/id #uuid "b1fe6c34-0868-58d7-9b8f-b535ff1dff48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{No solution}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713436}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713423} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb357fc6-2813-5aa6-8b7d-6d93d4c319f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713439}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "1b4af735-71b0-5e17-ae5e-e3fa9322a8bb" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}0 & 2 & \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 0 & -3 & -1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nUse Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "The first coefficient column is zero. The leading coefficient is in the $y$-column. Scale the entire first row using $R_1\\leftarrow (\\frac{1}{2})R_1$:\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & -3 & -1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThen use $R_2\\leftarrow R_2-(-3)R_1$. The augmented entry becomes $-1-(-3)(\\frac{1}{3})=0$:\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe last row says $0x+0y=0$, so it imposes no restriction. The remaining equation is $y=\\frac{1}{3}$. Here $y$ is basic and $x$ is free: there is no pivot in the $x$-column. The general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\quad x\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)\n$$\n\nwhere $x$ is any real number."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713418 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b66fb6d-dcc3-5774-af64-e711c2d2ce0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\quad y\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713410} {:answer/id #uuid "21dfb21f-ad01-5bea-9fc9-ee494f95f003" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{No solution}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713415} {:answer/id #uuid "24bea508-418e-5b40-884d-e980c83f327e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}\\end{bmatrix},\\quad x\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713416} {:answer/id #uuid "57c7254f-a0ec-5c35-8635-9224db7b610b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ \\frac{4}{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\quad x\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713427} {:answer/id #uuid "8c4b55f3-f8f9-57f7-8692-67465e70ef2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{8}{3} \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\quad y\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713434}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713427} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1f0576e-21c1-551f-9de6-9fc36eefee68" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713441}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "2ebf271b-f3b2-5c96-a703-65ec8994af19" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}0 & -2 & -\\frac{8}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{4}{3}\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nUse Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "The first coefficient column is zero. The leading coefficient is in the $y$-column. Scale the entire first row using $R_1\\leftarrow (-\\frac{1}{2})R_1$:\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}0 & 1 & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{4}{3}\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThen use $R_2\\leftarrow R_2-(1)R_1$. The augmented entry becomes $\\frac{4}{3}-(1)(\\frac{4}{3})=0$:\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}0 & 1 & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe last row says $0x+0y=0$, so it imposes no restriction. The remaining equation is $y=\\frac{4}{3}$. Here $y$ is basic and $x$ is free: there is no pivot in the $x$-column. The general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ \\frac{4}{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\quad x\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)\n$$\n\nwhere $x$ is any real number."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713420 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e7e79c3-b935-5dd2-832b-005a8b710448" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad x\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713428} {:answer/id #uuid "6fbb62e7-76fe-5721-879c-06d6a8f82982" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\quad y\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713429} {:answer/id #uuid "aebe3f63-5ddf-5bc0-b1b1-95781595d31b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{No solution}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713435} {:answer/id #uuid "bf6532ff-5f97-58fb-91f4-d0cc7e37ca71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad x\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713437} {:answer/id #uuid "f3a40f3c-a800-5ce5-83b8-de77199a0552" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\quad y\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713443}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713437} :answer-field/id #uuid "fed17810-b4c8-5f6f-9e9e-18e1d22929dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713444}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "340f4875-5286-5019-b0b3-61956884d9f8" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nUse Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "The first coefficient column is zero. The leading coefficient is in the $y$-column. Scale the entire first row using $R_1\\leftarrow (\\frac{1}{2})R_1$:\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThen use $R_2\\leftarrow R_2-(-2)R_1$. The augmented entry becomes $2-(-2)(-1)=0$:\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe last row says $0x+0y=0$, so it imposes no restriction. The remaining equation is $y=-1$. Here $y$ is basic and $x$ is free: there is no pivot in the $x$-column. The general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad x\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)\n$$\n\nwhere $x$ is any real number."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713421 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12be47be-4d59-5b33-a0f1-0eb6616a3c28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\quad y\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713411} {:answer/id #uuid "4ffb4b77-ef0c-506a-9081-19714d07aae2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad x\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713425} {:answer/id #uuid "81a97227-dc0c-504e-bc6d-93b275746a0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\quad x\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713431} {:answer/id #uuid "ea878b8c-eb4b-5b62-81de-120d7ab38ee7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{No solution}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713440} {:answer/id #uuid "f3501ee2-6eb1-5a9f-ab66-af2e56845344" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\quad y\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713442}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713440} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ec6a98e-0a97-5d4e-9198-c107cd0e9008" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713422}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "3a0eee65-36cf-51e9-aa99-c16bad62f331" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nUse Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "The first coefficient column is zero. The leading coefficient is in the $y$-column. Scale the entire first row using $R_1\\leftarrow (-\\frac{1}{2})R_1$:\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThen use $R_2\\leftarrow R_2-(3)R_1$. The augmented entry becomes $-2-(3)(-1)=1$:\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe last row says $0x+0y=1$, which is false. Hence the system has **no solution**."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713537 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0072c4ef-264a-5b06-89fb-6abeb107f83f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713531} {:answer/id #uuid "4edaf581-8338-5b38-acae-308800d0ddd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad y\\in\\mathbb{R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713534} {:answer/id #uuid "8748dc7e-e310-58c6-8ce8-ebf190b1874e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad y\\in\\mathbb{R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713538} {:answer/id #uuid "8ccbda55-4ce3-5687-9e25-45ec79b6d1d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad y\\in\\mathbb{R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713539} {:answer/id #uuid "c19bdce3-2fd5-5261-b54b-f7909920c29a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad y\\in\\mathbb{R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713547}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713547} :answer-field/id #uuid "a534ba62-c19b-5141-b98a-a82f7197a239" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713543}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "8723f61f-b51e-51c5-a3d2-ddd28bd50e68" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+3y &=5 \\\\ -3x-\\frac{9}{2}y &=-\\frac{15}{2}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse Gaussian elimination to reduce its augmented matrix to row echelon form, then select its complete general solution in vector form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 3 & 5 \\\\ -3 & -\\frac{9}{2} & -\\frac{15}{2}\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_1\\leftarrow\\frac{1}{2}R_1$:\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ -3 & -\\frac{9}{2} & -\\frac{15}{2}\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nNext apply $R_2\\leftarrow R_2+3R_1$. Both the coefficient entries and the augmented entry cancel:\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe corresponding equations are\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+\\frac{3}{2}y &=\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe last equation imposes no restriction. The variable $x$ is basic and $y$ is free, so\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{3}{2}y.\n$$\n\nSeparate the constant part from the coefficient of the free variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad y\\in\\mathbb{R}\n$$\n\nThe base vector gives a particular solution. The direction vector has second coordinate $1$ because $y$ itself varies freely. For a check, substituting into the first equation gives $2(\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{3}{2}y)+3y=5$. The second equation is $-\\frac{3}{2}$ times the first, so every vector in this family satisfies both equations."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713599 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2357388b-1c0a-5418-8583-7690efc9203e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713578} {:answer/id #uuid "350cab05-11d6-5690-b2e1-999dd505e7b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713583} {:answer/id #uuid "397aa157-380f-5e68-a2e8-50e0c3f46dbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713586} {:answer/id #uuid "b9a28110-035a-5e87-80ab-5e6d8984abad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713597} {:answer/id #uuid "e2ac340a-9749-5ef5-8f72-aff73eb50f9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713602}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713597} :answer-field/id #uuid "267809e4-876e-5a5a-8c1e-e415b4743636" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713579}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c9edc195-823a-5c2e-ac4b-ba7ca607ff90" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=4 y^{2} \\sqrt{x}+\\frac{x}{y}$, evaluate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}$ at the point $(1,1)$." :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4 y^{2} \\sqrt{x}+\\frac{x}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4 y^{2} \\sqrt{x}+x{y}^{-1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4 y^{2} \\sqrt{x})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{y}^{-1}) \\\\  & =4 \\sqrt{x}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y^{2})+x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{-1}) \\\\  & =4 \\sqrt{x}\\cdot (2 y)+x\\cdot (-{y}^{-2}) \\\\  & =8 y \\sqrt{x}-x{y}^{-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y}{|}_{(1,1)} & =8 (1) \\sqrt{(1)}-(1){(1)}^{-2} \\\\  & =8-(1) \\\\  & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713607 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26fdd424-f0d6-5c5a-875e-ec5e83e5cc69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{3 \\pi}{2} + \\frac{6}{\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713580} {:answer/id #uuid "286eb541-0a80-5a89-abdf-e55cf252483e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{6}{\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713582} {:answer/id #uuid "490d67da-3cf7-5576-83a1-7a72b81fe931" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{3 \\pi}{2} - \\frac{6}{\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713591} {:answer/id #uuid "5e33bb59-29f4-5885-abf1-74c34d98c754" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{3 \\pi}{2} - 2 \\ln{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3} \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713594} {:answer/id #uuid "ee36c59a-85cb-516f-836c-3411fbc55ae2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{6}{\\pi} + \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713604}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713591} :answer-field/id #uuid "e93aa025-9f60-584a-82b4-f55ed4aa2d66" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713603}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "fff0c50f-8039-5b75-8c50-72eec2dabcc5" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=2 \\ln{(x )} \\cos{(y )}-3 y \\sin{(x )}$, evaluate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$ at the point $(\\frac{\\pi}{3},\\pi)$." :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2 \\ln{(x )} \\cos{(y )}-3 y \\sin{(x )}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2 \\ln{(x )} \\cos{(y )})-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3 y \\sin{(x )}) \\\\  & =2 \\cos{(y )}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\ln{(x )})-3 y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sin{(x )}) \\\\  & =2 \\cos{(y )}\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)-3 y\\cdot (\\cos{(x )}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2 \\cos{(y )}}{x}-3 y \\cos{(x )}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(\\frac{\\pi}{3},\\pi):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(\\frac{\\pi}{3},\\pi)} & =\\frac{2 \\cos{(\\pi)}}{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right)}-3 (\\pi) \\cos{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right)} \\\\  & =- \\frac{6}{\\pi}-\\left(\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =- \\frac{3 \\pi}{2} - \\frac{6}{\\pi}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715069 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "276bfcdc-0d11-576a-b74e-90b33fb29538" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715072} {:answer/id #uuid "603ef468-cd80-495a-8e57-e741ff951e1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719529}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715072} :answer-field/id #uuid "96c98337-6f65-5c84-beb7-007655b99307" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715086} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e9240e1-2c75-5ea2-b492-e3150a4441f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715071} {:answer/id #uuid "a794ce98-3061-4681-b2ae-1b325035a636" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719530}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715071} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb43df56-4b29-5381-9a44-01ea28b6dd50" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715092}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "05c68c51-a7eb-5d8e-a440-2e04a301664e" :question/problem "![Circle with labeled points and marked center.](images/4b/4b7752efdfef70be07f71a8c6e66d2f1b228ae08c24c66d6d1480673ebd126c1.png)\n\nThe endpoints of a diameter of a circle are $A(-3,8)$ and $B(-2,-5)$. Find the coordinates $(h,k)$ of its center.\n\n$(h,k)=(${{field-1}}$,${{field-2}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "The center of a circle is the midpoint of any diameter. Average corresponding coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(h,k)&=\\left(\\frac{x_1+x_2}{2},\\frac{y_1+y_2}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\left(\\frac{(-3)+(-2)}{2},\\frac{(8)+(-5)}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\left(\\frac{-5}{2},\\frac{3}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=(- \\frac{5}{2},\\frac{3}{2}).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:answer/id #uuid "30e70fb7-f566-5f7b-b7ed-87637a01a634" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-3,\\frac{15}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715074} {:answer/id #uuid "3e4294a2-9c7e-5b97-88b8-984afae084b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(3,- \\frac{7}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715075} {:answer/id #uuid "4eb87c2e-ac13-524a-8d1c-b20207c483ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(- \\frac{1}{2},0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715078} {:answer/id #uuid "599a6902-97c7-509b-87fb-0c2ee90c4cc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(5,- \\frac{11}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715079} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715084 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e4294a2-9c7e-5b97-88b8-984afae084b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(3,- \\frac{7}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715075} {:answer/id #uuid "aebdfc91-d59e-5468-853d-be1f9a4ff691" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-5,\\frac{5}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715089} {:answer/id #uuid "b38a7c86-cfd8-54b6-ac5b-dd093c6b6ca9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(- \\frac{9}{2},2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715091} {:answer/id #uuid "df86cd6c-efb9-56e3-a0da-57b9a2abefe5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-8,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715095} {:answer/id #uuid "eac70afd-4667-5f9a-b6b4-f671e801d901" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{5}{2},-5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715097}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715089} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecec3526-4193-5a0a-9ff4-66394771d752" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715098}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8552ddf0-8aa8-54ff-9bdc-93fcede16502" :question/problem "![Circle with labeled points and marked center.](images/48/48f575c293699ded7de226fec06f7d5332f1f063d61535874015e68ca0b9e171.png)\n\nThe endpoints of a diameter of a circle are $A(-8,6)$ and $B(-2,-1)$. Find the coordinates $(h,k)$ of its center." :question/worked-solution "The center of a circle is the midpoint of any diameter. Average corresponding coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(h,k)&=\\left(\\frac{x_1+x_2}{2},\\frac{y_1+y_2}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\left(\\frac{(-8)+(-2)}{2},\\frac{(6)+(-1)}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\left(\\frac{-10}{2},\\frac{5}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=(-5,\\frac{5}{2}).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:answer/id #uuid "aa0da74e-261c-5a07-8605-39a6b71fccdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(0,- \\frac{1}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715087} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715088 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d5d5531-1a27-5839-a05b-914d1e017752" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(3,-8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715073} {:answer/id #uuid "30e70fb7-f566-5f7b-b7ed-87637a01a634" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-3,\\frac{15}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715074} {:answer/id #uuid "4eb87c2e-ac13-524a-8d1c-b20207c483ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(- \\frac{1}{2},0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715078} {:answer/id #uuid "599a6902-97c7-509b-87fb-0c2ee90c4cc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(5,- \\frac{11}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715079} {:answer/id #uuid "aa0da74e-261c-5a07-8605-39a6b71fccdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(0,- \\frac{1}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715087}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715087} :answer-field/id #uuid "486be1dd-1746-55c0-b5e6-c1d372aa646d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715076}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ae3685c8-b262-5240-b208-72ac454600d2" :question/problem "![Circle with labeled points and marked center.](images/88/88fabbaf20320a639853a13834d5f4f2b8c15c3e930e8c1b8f4d3304fa897fcd.png)\n\nThe endpoints of a diameter of a circle are $A(3,-8)$ and $B(-3,7)$. Find the coordinates $(h,k)$ of its center." :question/worked-solution "The center of a circle is the midpoint of any diameter. Average corresponding coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(h,k)&=\\left(\\frac{x_1+x_2}{2},\\frac{y_1+y_2}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\left(\\frac{(3)+(-3)}{2},\\frac{(-8)+(7)}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\left(\\frac{0}{2},\\frac{-1}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=(0,- \\frac{1}{2}).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:answer/id #uuid "aebdfc91-d59e-5468-853d-be1f9a4ff691" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-5,\\frac{5}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715089} {:answer/id #uuid "b38a7c86-cfd8-54b6-ac5b-dd093c6b6ca9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(- \\frac{9}{2},2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715091} {:answer/id #uuid "eac70afd-4667-5f9a-b6b4-f671e801d901" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{5}{2},-5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715097} {:answer/id #uuid "02137bb5-f64e-5275-9b8c-0fb3fea4ed0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$(\\frac{1}{2},1)$ and $(\\frac{3}{2},1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715101} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715104 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1651a2b6-adec-51c6-98be-91f7069d26fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{3}{4},-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715108} {:answer/id #uuid "2c8267f8-9df6-5a66-956d-3004bef9599c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{3}{4},3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715111} {:answer/id #uuid "58393c80-720a-521c-adc7-ac65dbbded12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{3}{2},-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715114} {:answer/id #uuid "817be77c-1959-505d-9d41-7b5dcb888086" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{3}{2},-6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715123} {:answer/id #uuid "b5bd02c6-d5db-5488-a294-6e77b74e0622" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{3}{8},-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715129}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715108} :answer-field/id #uuid "0491cbeb-7434-5942-ba96-f39d523106f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715103}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "06cde7b6-bdbd-5aad-9bad-8fe8e922719e" :question/problem "Given $f(x,y)=2 x^{2} - 3 x + 2 \\left(y + 3\\right)^{2}$, find the points $(x,y)$ where $\\nabla f=\\mathbf 0$." :question/worked-solution "A gradient vanishes exactly when every component vanishes. Differentiate with respect to each variable, holding the others constant.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f_{x}&=4 x - 3 \\\\ f_{y}&=4 y + 12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSet all components equal to zero:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4 x - 3&=0 \\\\ 4 y + 12&=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo write the simultaneous equations compactly, let $u=x,\\ v=y + 3$. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 u&=3 \\\\ u&=\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ v&=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n Recover the original coordinates using $x=u,\\ y=v - 3$.\n\nTherefore, the complete set of points in the domain is $(\\frac{3}{4},-3)$. Each satisfies every component equation."} {:answer/id #uuid "1651a2b6-adec-51c6-98be-91f7069d26fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{3}{4},-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715108} {:answer/id #uuid "2c8267f8-9df6-5a66-956d-3004bef9599c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{3}{4},3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715111} {:answer/id #uuid "58393c80-720a-521c-adc7-ac65dbbded12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{3}{2},-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715114} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b51f4e8-0208-5589-ae97-68b24880e5d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715105} {:answer/id #uuid "be5c4c4b-9920-5c8a-b25e-ca791a89fc66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715131}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715105} :answer-field/id #uuid 