 points lie on the same circle, so $B$ has radius $3$. Along the marked arc, moving from $A$ to $B$ is counterclockwise; add the marked angle.\n\n$$\n\\theta_B=135^\\circ+15^\\circ=150^\\circ.\n$$\n\nThus $B$ has polar coordinates $(3,150^\\circ)$. Using $x=r\\cos\\theta$ and $y=r\\sin\\theta$,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx &=3\\cos\\left(150^\\circ\\right)=3\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)=- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{3}}{2},\\\\y &=3\\sin\\left(150^\\circ\\right)=3\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)=\\frac{3}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian coordinates of $B$ are $(- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{3}}{2},\\frac{3}{2})$."} {:answer/id #uuid "5fc9e14a-8a9d-5bc9-8e6c-144ed352ec8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{9}{2},- \\frac{9 \\sqrt{3}}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722428} {:answer/id #uuid "6076a588-142a-591a-b42c-10d78df7f968" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{9 \\sqrt{3}}{2},- \\frac{9}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722429} {:answer/id #uuid "67c4fd59-cd31-598e-9258-a76fedf95461" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722430} {:answer/id #uuid "6e9c0687-7ebd-5b6c-9f83-a81c77957e2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{3}}{2},\\frac{3}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722432} {:answer/id #uuid "7d4e37b2-b891-54ca-977a-f2a9fbe5981b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2},\\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722435} {:answer/id #uuid "a546f1fd-fceb-5859-8449-e6ae430bf7f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{9 \\sqrt{2}}{2},- \\frac{9 \\sqrt{2}}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722437} {:answer/id #uuid "a9841cd1-b86d-556d-967b-e6be2652a05c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(- \\frac{9}{2},\\frac{9 \\sqrt{3}}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722438} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722