 remain $x=0$ and $y=0$, and the branches lie in quadrants I and III. The required graph is shown below.\n\n![](images/0f/0f76443dc9c8b90addbcd745237506c716f7b72699c63738ccf2aff1d9f046ca.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186737221 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f5560d0-76c2-5231-8865-c057b4f85426" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/0f/0f76443dc9c8b90addbcd745237506c716f7b72699c63738ccf2aff1d9f046ca.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737201} {:answer/id #uuid "5d01e69a-466b-5f51-ad44-02543d148fcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/e8/e879c6d57bfa5a99c09e0218bdb78e12c11ceb25e65e77acda500d091e7ee522.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737212} {:answer/id #uuid "6ab7479c-cf3f-5a78-930c-9c2b81afde0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/eb/ebbe5f934b3c27a1b5c010585d874af1c1d6cbfde35209a97a2c4398fdf6dd1b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737214} {:answer/id #uuid "729b362f-9ebf-50f5-99f9-ad7426a3eda1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/96/96a18dfedff32d5bc2ca66ffcf12760beb3e90f4072a152c23b359b5a0ad2006.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737215} {:answer/id #uuid "e1aab5d0-0699-56b7-a639-e592d169f054" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/b6/b62f11a76da14b9f41bc4accae83652a1923b51092818f4b7853f13b68e3cd83.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737225}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186737225} :answer-field/id #uuid "d934ef41-04c9-55a7-9adc-8d7d815191e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737224}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "d4498c2b-653d-5fa6-8983-9bb43d61f0fc" :question/problem "Which of the following is the graph of $y=\\frac{2}{5x}?$" :question/worked-solution "To plot $y=\\frac{2}{5x},$ start with the curve $y=\\frac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](images/49/49973aaa1c2e9a5347b92577c7ec5ea7a8e7937e9aa8984e1d1e1df82ce0c683.png)\n\nMultiply every $y$-coordinate by $\\frac{2}{5}$, keeping the $x$-coordinate fixed. This is a stretch by a scale factor of $\\frac{2}{5}$ parallel to the $y$-axis.\n\nAt $x=2$, the original height is $\\frac{1}{2}$. The new height is\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1}{5}.\n$$\n\nThus $(2, \\frac{1}{2})$ maps to $(2, \\frac{1}{5})$, and $(-2, -\\frac{1}{2})$ maps to $(-2, -\\frac{1}{5})$. The asymptotes remain $x=0$ and $y=0$, and the branches lie in quadrants I and III. The required graph is shown below.\n\n![](images/b6/b62f11a76da14b9f41bc4accae83652a1923b51092818f4b7853f13b68e3cd83.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186737330 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18173acb-583e-5ad0-8dbc-005cda540021" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737317} {:answer/id #uuid "7420ae78-59d5-5334-af3c-0df0d2c05ad8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737323} {:answer/id #uuid "7724e391-1008-5437-b33a-4d31dfe33f24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737324} {:answer/id #uuid "cbd86bfe-5d7e-5ece-b054-42765161b1ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737333} {:answer/id #uuid "f06b00b9-b14e-52c9-9532-4ddd82440486" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737335}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186737324} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ec95114-9596-50aa-af61-033200776115" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737319}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b357e87a-6338-5273-b0ca-140ce2e19212" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $(-2,-\\frac{3}{2})$ and the line $y=3$." :question/worked-solution "Let's sketch the given situation.\n\n![](images/74/746fcd7b375c2f06119f598e6b8a4f523c4bb750a838e98ac797b757ba671484.png)\n\nSince the line $y=3$ is horizontal, the shortest segment from $(-2,-\\frac{3}{2})$ to the line is vertical and perpendicular to the line. Its length is the absolute value of the difference between the point’s $y$-coordinate and $3$.\n\nSo, the shortest distance is\n\n$$\nd=\\left|-\\frac{3}{2}-3\\right|=\\left|-\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{6}{2}\\right|=\\left|-\\frac{9}{2}\\right|=\\frac{9}{2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186737332 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d781197-d8cb-5713-b4d6-524ae2d99f35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737321} {:answer/id #uuid "7def6f16-63f5-54c4-86cc-4f6e94f45e29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737325} {:answer/id #uuid "7e20d812-f6d7-5c40-8a3a-3c35ea278a06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737326} {:answer/id #uuid "936010d6-8591-5424-ad86-d5ab0af6e3a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{29}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737327} {:answer/id #uuid "9400d6fa-2d07-58d4-8ddb-c95379bb04bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737328}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186737326} :answer-field/id #uuid "b37ab2c7-f803-5ebe-b8e2-91b226c08fe2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737331}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "b6cd7c84-2308-590f-aaa1-b86dbba3f624" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $(-\\frac{5}{3},2)$ and the line $x=-\\frac{3}{4}$." :question/worked-solution "Let's sketch the given situation.\n\n![](images/28/28983a8df9aa1b44b6082c9c676e0d1f7e9740c4d7d1ce085feb8ea63bed6999.png)\n\nSince the line $x=-\\frac{3}{4}$ is vertical, the shortest segment from $(-\\frac{5}{3},2)$ to the line is horizontal and perpendicular to the line. Its length is the absolute value of the difference between the point’s $x$-coordinate and $-\\frac{3}{4}$.\n\nSo, the shortest distance is\n\n$$\nd=\\left|-\\frac{5}{3}-\\left(-\\frac{3}{4}\\right)\\right|=\\left|-\\frac{20}{12}+\\frac{9}{12}\\right|=\\left|-\\frac{11}{12}\\right|=\\frac{11}{12}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186737433 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41878c5c-f822-50b2-817e-24d65c72d093" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737426} {:answer/id #uuid "6036e67f-a132-5949-8ba6-76895cf7d19d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737428} {:answer/id #uuid "6bb1a00b-49e5-5867-ad4c-c7c0430c4b91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737429} {:answer/id #uuid "76f227ec-8955-574b-be24-48c12062e537" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737431} {:answer/id #uuid "88375a44-5999-5852-b1db-9ce2ea6e8250" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737432}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186737429} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf2dfc17-373a-5b31-8448-5921e099c3bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737437}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "8c749989-9a67-521d-9249-e63a6dcb9aae" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $(2,-\\frac{3}{2})$ and the line $2y-3x=4$." :question/worked-solution "Rewrite the line in slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2y-3x&=4\\\\2y&=3x+4\\\\y&=\\frac{3}{2}x+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe shortest segment to the line is perpendicular to it.\n\n![](images/30/308b254d7e4e0e3c03be88fca9aac2ba2452dc838d48706991fa1c0cd80fc30b.png)\n\nThe given line has slope $\\frac{3}{2}$, so the perpendicular slope is $-\\frac{2}{3}$. The perpendicular line through $(2,-\\frac{3}{2})$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-y_1&=m(x-x_1)\\\\y+\\frac{3}{2}&=-\\frac{2}{3}(x-2)\\\\y&=-\\frac{2}{3}x+\\frac{4}{3}-\\frac{3}{2}\\\\y&=-\\frac{2}{3}x-\\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the foot of the perpendicular by solving\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=\\frac{3}{2}x+2 \\\\ y &=-\\frac{2}{3}x-\\frac{1}{6}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nEquating the expressions for $y$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}x+2&=-\\frac{2}{3}x-\\frac{1}{6}\\\\\\frac{13}{6}x&=-\\frac{13}{6}\\\\x&=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen $y=\\frac{3}{2}(-1)+2=\\frac{1}{2}$, so the foot is $H=(-1,\\frac{1}{2})$. The distance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d&=\\sqrt{(x_2-x_1)^2+(y_2-y_1)^2}\\\\&=\\sqrt{(-1-2)^2+\\left(\\frac{1}{2}-\\left(-\\frac{3}{2}\\right)\\right)^2}\\\\&=\\sqrt{9+4}\\\\&=\\sqrt{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe shortest distance is $\\sqrt{13}$."} {:answer/id #uuid "1e90b189-07a5-5c7d-944c-d1198c55ccf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{9}{2},-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737499} {:answer/id #uuid "4708b346-d581-5b83-8774-5a590e18b693" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\frac{17}{13},-\\frac{7}{13})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737500} {:answer/id #uuid "4ed5e6db-cce8-5665-8b36-336b67ca620c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{9}{4},\\frac{1}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737502} {:answer/id #uuid "5e0be78a-d8a9-5b9e-9f7e-ac4ea4484c04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\frac{23}{13},-\\frac{11}{13})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737505} {:answer/id #uuid "682b084c-638a-5dc9-a269-e08e7d7e3d6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\frac{11}{13},-\\frac{3}{13})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737507} {:answer/id #uuid "8682029c-fb7b-53c6-93cf-8a056472172c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\frac{14}{13},-\\frac{5}{13})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737511} {:answer/id #uuid "9aeaf95e-d587-5f3f-b31d-401d457d23f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{3}{2},1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737513} {:answer/id #uuid "d95c362c-deee-5bf6-88c5-6dc2413fc224" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\frac{20}{13},-\\frac{9}{13})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737515} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186737648 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "181cf6a1-e44b-5af8-9111-3fdfac4366b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1 - \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737637} {:answer/id #uuid "60201a83-b849-538c-bc1c-b15fb4696792" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1 + \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737647} {:answer/id #uuid "b998e470-f3bb-504d-9939-5b7d42203776" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737652} {:answer/id #uuid "c0902d60-dd8d-5bd3-9fa0-b6415ceceb2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737653} {:answer/id #uuid "fecc146d-49cd-5c00-9b83-0eef0f978ff8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737660}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186737653} :answer-field/id #uuid "533a9da7-563a-575b-9a03-c7646cec9285" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737644}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "733b6379-1441-568d-905e-c7a39a576e2d" :question/problem "$$\n\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{12}}^{0} \\cos(2 x)\\tan(2 x)\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Use the identity $\\tan(2 x)=\\frac{\\sin(2 x)}{\\cos(2 x)}$ and simplify.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{12}}^{0} \\cos(2 x)\\tan(2 x)\\,\\text{d}x &=\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{12}}^{0} (\\cos(2 x)\\cdot \\frac{\\sin(2 x)}{\\cos(2 x)})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ &=\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{12}}^{0} (\\sin(2 x))\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $u=2 x$. Then $\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\mathrm{d}u$.\n\n| $x$ | $- \\frac{\\pi}{12}$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $- \\frac{\\pi}{6}$ | $0$ |\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{12}}^{0} (\\sin(2 x))\\,\\text{d}x &=\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{0} (\\sin(u))\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate and subtract the endpoint values.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{12}}^{0} (\\sin(2 x))\\,\\text{d}x &=\\left[- \\frac{\\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{2}\\right]_{- \\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{0} \\\\ &=\\left(- \\frac{\\cos{\\left((0) \\right)}}{2}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{\\cos{\\left(\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right) \\right)}}{2}\\right) \\\\ &=\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\right) \\\\ &=- \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186737649 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3618d6dd-b30d-5288-b5c3-84f169a27080" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737640}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186737640} :answer-field/id #uuid "f856be51-9c3c-5f50-be3e-f4355700ebfe" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737659}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7430cea2-7e06-542f-b991-4f4f1f712bf0" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}} \\frac{1}{\\sec(x)}(1+\\tan(x))\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Use the identity $\\frac{1}{\\sec(x)}=\\cos(x),\\quad \\tan(x)=\\frac{\\sin(x)}{\\cos(x)}$ and simplify.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}} \\frac{1}{\\sec(x)}(1+\\tan(x))\\,\\text{d}x &=\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}} (\\cos(x)(1+\\frac{\\sin(x)}{\\cos(x)}))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ &=\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}} (\\cos(x)+\\sin(x))\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate and subtract the endpoint values.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}} (\\cos(x)+\\sin(x))\\,\\text{d}x &=\\left[\\sin{\\left(x \\right)} - \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}} \\\\ &=(\\sin{\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right) \\right)} - \\cos{\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right) \\right)})-(\\sin{\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) \\right)} - \\cos{\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) \\right)}) \\\\ &=(- \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})-(0) \\\\ &=- \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186737651 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "126fa213-8c86-5e72-91f0-7f15c6cc158e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1 - \\frac{2 \\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737636} {:answer/id #uuid "2af3a61d-f6b4-5038-a7b6-140cc3b7225c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737639} {:answer/id #uuid "5f61aaef-29c5-5280-8227-361b384af4a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1 + \\frac{2 \\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737646} {:answer/id #uuid "8118c957-d252-5ba1-8a33-c2c7038e5d02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{2 \\sqrt{3}}{3} - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737650} {:answer/id #uuid "c22d186b-df02-5ddb-b52e-4892c010d06a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1 + \\frac{2 \\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737654}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186737636} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee040467-41b2-5bf9-9e05-6b4cfa40d60f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737657}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b72563e0-0946-55fa-b7d7-1c0d8c2dfecd" :question/problem "$$\n\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{0} \\frac{1}{\\cos(x)}\\cdot \\tan(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Use the identity $\\frac{1}{\\cos(x)}=\\sec(x)$ and simplify.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{0} \\frac{1}{\\cos(x)}\\cdot \\tan(x)\\,\\text{d}x &=\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{0} (\\sec(x)\\tan(x))\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate and subtract the endpoint values.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{0} (\\sec(x)\\tan(x))\\,\\text{d}x &=\\left[\\sec{\\left(x \\right)}\\right]_{- \\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{0} \\\\ &=(\\sec{\\left((0) \\right)})-(\\sec{\\left(\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right) \\right)}) \\\\ &=(1)-\\left(\\frac{2 \\sqrt{3}}{3}\\right) \\\\ &=1 - \\frac{2 \\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186737655 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51fcb07f-1391-5087-9a6b-d59ec1ff5720" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} + \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737643}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186737643} :answer-field/id #uuid "00ea9e14-e751-5176-b0ea-978e565e548f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737634}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d8126a61-68f9-5f61-9b64-a34c0fb03614" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}} \\cos(x)\\tan(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Use the identity $\\tan(x)=\\frac{\\sin(x)}{\\cos(x)}$ and simplify.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}} \\cos(x)\\tan(x)\\,\\text{d}x &=\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}} (\\cos(x)\\cdot \\frac{\\sin(x)}{\\cos(x)})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ &=\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}} (\\sin(x))\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate and subtract the endpoint values.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}} (\\sin(x))\\,\\text{d}x &=\\left[- \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right]_{- \\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}} \\\\ &=(- \\cos{\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) \\right)})-(- \\cos{\\left(\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right) \\right)}) \\\\ &=\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right) \\\\ &=- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} + \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186737658 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c651c85-9233-5a08-a874-f0c805b073a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737635} {:answer/id #uuid "1b38baf7-eef1-58de-9139-c5632cac48d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737638} {:answer/id #uuid "4300bd64-fe1e-5b4d-bac2-a157a1143573" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737641} {:answer/id #uuid "449442bb-4bd1-5c23-8111-915ac9590c3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737642} {:answer/id #uuid "547b6a9e-9f6e-5d00-8c2d-df7f64c87704" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737645}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186737642} :answer-field/id #uuid "dde5818f-f87a-506a-996d-97e4df80cdb5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737656}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f849a2bc-1692-5935-8f03-2b077881f981" :question/problem "$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}} \\cos(x)\\tan(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Use the identity $\\tan(x)=\\frac{\\sin(x)}{\\cos(x)}$ and simplify.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}} \\cos(x)\\tan(x)\\,\\text{d}x &=\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}} (\\cos(x)\\cdot \\frac{\\sin(x)}{\\cos(x)})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}} (\\sin(x))\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate and subtract the endpoint values.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}} (\\sin(x))\\,\\text{d}x &=\\left[- \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}} \\\\ &=(- \\cos{\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right) \\right)})-(- \\cos{\\left((0) \\right)}) \\\\ &=\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right)-(-1) \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186737686 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb706b8e-2d7e-5a66-baa2-ef8c93a081c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1 + \\frac{2 \\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737690}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186737690} :answer-field/id #uuid "86781813-0ed4-5eb7-b77a-a409f8f75f44" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737689}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "3da0d8fb-03df-5793-9409-cc6145399faf" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{12}} 2\\,\\sec(2 x)(\\tan(2 x)+4\\,\\cos^{2}(2 x))\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Use the identity $\\sec(2 x)=\\frac{1}{\\cos(2 x)}$ and simplify.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{12}} 2\\,\\sec(2 x)(\\tan(2 x)+4\\,\\cos^{2}(2 x))\\,\\text{d}x &=\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{12}} (2\\,\\sec(2 x)\\tan(2 x)+8\\,\\frac{\\cos^{2}(2 x)}{\\cos(2 x)})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{12}} (2\\,\\sec(2 x)\\tan(2 x)+8\\,\\cos(2 x))\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $u=2 x$. Then $\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\mathrm{d}u$.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi}{12}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi}{6}$ |\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{12}} (2\\,\\sec(2 x)\\tan(2 x)+8\\,\\cos(2 x))\\,\\text{d}x &=\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} (2\\,\\sec(u)\\tan(u)+8\\,\\cos(u))\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate and subtract the endpoint values.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{12}} (2\\,\\sec(2 x)\\tan(2 x)+8\\,\\cos(2 x))\\,\\text{d}x &=\\left[4 \\sin{\\left(u \\right)} + \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} \\\\ &=(4 \\sin{\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right) \\right)} + \\sec{\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right) \\right)})-(4 \\sin{\\left((0) \\right)} + \\sec{\\left((0) \\right)}) \\\\ &=(\\frac{2 \\sqrt{3}}{3} + 2)-(1) \\\\ &=1 + \\frac{2 \\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186737688 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6825372d-315c-5cf2-bf50-af646afd3960" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737687}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186737687} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a4d9446-3d6c-536a-b07d-1510a1162840" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737685}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "71d5a912-7d2e-5e07-97ee-8739c781b50a" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{16}}^{- \\frac{\\pi}{24}} \\frac{2}{\\cos^{2}(4 x)}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Use the identity $\\frac{1}{\\cos(4 x)}=\\sec(4 x)$ and simplify.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{16}}^{- \\frac{\\pi}{24}} \\frac{2}{\\cos^{2}(4 x)}\\,\\text{d}x &=\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{16}}^{- \\frac{\\pi}{24}} (2\\,\\left(\\frac{1}{\\cos(4 x)}\\right)^2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ &=\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{16}}^{- \\frac{\\pi}{24}} (2\\,\\sec^{2}(4 x))\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $u=4 x$. Then $\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{1}{4}\\mathrm{d}u$.\n\n| $x$ | $- \\frac{\\pi}{16}$ | $- \\frac{\\pi}{24}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $- \\frac{\\pi}{4}$ | $- \\frac{\\pi}{6}$ |\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{16}}^{- \\frac{\\pi}{24}} (2\\,\\sec^{2}(4 x))\\,\\text{d}x &=\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{- \\frac{\\pi}{6}} (2\\,\\sec^{2}(u))\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate and subtract the endpoint values.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{16}}^{- \\frac{\\pi}{24}} (2\\,\\sec^{2}(4 x))\\,\\text{d}x &=\\left[\\frac{\\tan{\\left(u \\right)}}{2}\\right]_{- \\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{- \\frac{\\pi}{6}} \\\\ &=\\left(\\frac{\\tan{\\left(\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right) \\right)}}{2}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{\\tan{\\left(\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) \\right)}}{2}\\right) \\\\ &=\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{6}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186737793 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76a3e586-92cb-5c6c-b961-d90c01f93ee2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737788} {:answer/id #uuid "955338ca-81d7-5079-bab5-9f1f78db9a45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737792} {:answer/id #uuid "ce36ae7c-f16a-58d9-a2be-91f6af553c3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737794} {:answer/id #uuid "d9c19b3e-382e-5cc1-95d6-f0bf2bc9e858" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737798} {:answer/id #uuid "f023b413-2fe9-5259-8683-8600ac3e957f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737800}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186737798} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6f262e0-edb2-5d5d-b8d6-c19a05247a58" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186737795}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9bb4591f-ee86-5810-af02-ac52f158e2ff" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $(\\frac{1}{2},8)$ and the line $x=5$." :question/worked-solution "Let's sketch the given situation.\n\n![](images/37/37186da62afac49f254e5fc5424a44499707146c4e06af64ce5a997c7ab0f6c8.png)\n\nSince the line $x=5$ is vertical, the shortest segment to it is horizontal and perpendicular to the line. Its length is the absolute value of the difference between the point’s $x$-coordinate and $5$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nd &= \\left|\\frac{1}{2}-5\\right| \\\\ &= \\left|\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{10}{2}\\right| \\\\ &= \\left|-\\frac{9}{2}\\right| \\\\ &= \\frac{9}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:answer/id #uuid "017e0edf-1be4-5390-8759-43a3bfcda9ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{8}{5},\\frac{1}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738120} {:answer/id #uuid "213c21e1-a661-59f9-abb3-b4704da95320" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{9}{5},-\\frac{8}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738121} {:answer/id #uuid "2a7361d1-2a7a-55c9-92b2-2efa5e9b503b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{143}{25},\\frac{101}{25})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738122} {:answer/id #uuid "2e3c06a1-e495-5fcf-975e-072e68c5cfd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\frac{41}{25},-\\frac{37}{25})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738124} {:answer/id #uuid "3453812c-334a-54dd-a9c1-4a3546c519b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{11}{5},-\\frac{7}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738125} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186738126 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e94aa99-6932-59c5-b797-6c046cb0edc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\frac{7}{13},-\\frac{30}{13})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738128} {:answer/id #uuid "9019faff-01f6-52f6-aebe-13cb687cdef5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{45}{13},\\frac{48}{13})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738132} {:answer/id #uuid "ae4e8e02-6073-5d38-a023-db597fb25384" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{19}{13},\\frac{9}{13})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738135} {:answer/id #uuid "bb6bdb16-c692-529c-8e4c-9f585ebbe9ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\frac{41}{13},-\\frac{81}{13})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738138} {:answer/id #uuid "d27eff77-6b07-5f4b-95c6-a16244a1800f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{21}{13},\\frac{12}{13})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738141}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186738138} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef3866e6-cefc-56d5-8b4d-8205054fed5d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738144}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "390c5193-fe7d-5708-b902-daf6d7cee9cb" :question/problem "![](images/a5/a52e96d3bff37df6d352648a27461614ab3ac6aa6e5896e7daa569b7b36d0e31.png)\n\nFind the point on the line $2y-3x=-3$ that is closest to the point $(-5,-5)$." :question/worked-solution "The closest point is where the given line meets the perpendicular line through $(-5,-5)$.\n\nFirst, rewrite the given line in slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2y-3x&=-3 \\\\ 2y&=3x-3 \\\\ y&=\\frac{3}{2}x-\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe given line has slope $\\frac{3}{2}$, so the perpendicular slope is $-\\frac{2}{3}$, its negative reciprocal. Using point-slope form,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-y_1&=m(x-x_1) \\\\ y-(-5)&=-\\frac{2}{3}\\left(x-(-5)\\right) \\\\ y&=-\\frac{2}{3}x-\\frac{10}{3}+(-5) \\\\ y&=-\\frac{2}{3}x-\\frac{25}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=\\frac{3}{2}x-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ y &=-\\frac{2}{3}x-\\frac{25}{3}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nby setting the expressions for $y$ equal and collecting terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}x-\\frac{3}{2}&=-\\frac{2}{3}x-\\frac{25}{3} \\\\ \\left(\\frac{3}{2}-\\left(-\\frac{2}{3}\\right)\\right)x&=-\\frac{25}{3}-\\left(-\\frac{3}{2}\\right) \\\\ \\frac{13}{6}x&=-\\frac{41}{6} \\\\ x&=-\\frac{41}{13}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute into the given line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y&=\\frac{3}{2}\\left(-\\frac{41}{13}\\right)+\\left(-\\frac{3}{2}\\right) \\\\ y&=-\\frac{123}{26}+\\left(-\\frac{3}{2}\\right) \\\\ y&=-\\frac{81}{13}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point on the line $2y-3x=-3$ closest to $(-5,-5)$ is $(-\\frac{41}{13},-\\frac{81}{13})$."} {:answer/id #uuid "5c612e15-d8d5-56a1-98fa-682da32d346d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{11}{25},\\frac{2}{25})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738127} {:answer/id #uuid "5e94aa99-6932-59c5-b797-6c046cb0edc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\frac{7}{13},-\\frac{30}{13})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738128} {:answer/id #uuid "70f0b31c-6389-564c-9b1b-6f983265e86e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\frac{29}{10},-\\frac{13}{10})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738129} {:answer/id #uuid "9019faff-01f6-52f6-aebe-13cb687cdef5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{45}{13},\\frac{48}{13})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738132} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186738133 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "213c21e1-a661-59f9-abb3-b4704da95320" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{9}{5},-\\frac{8}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738121} {:answer/id #uuid "3453812c-334a-54dd-a9c1-4a3546c519b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{11}{5},-\\frac{7}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738125} {:answer/id #uuid "8a7d9b3c-14f0-52cf-8f40-ba3f6ee887f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(7,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738131} {:answer/id #uuid "c2d9ef84-4d77-52f2-b0d2-71cfb24bfeea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{13}{5},-\\frac{6}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738139} {:answer/id #uuid "d1a911a8-a82c-5f00-a384-6b9b109089e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{1}{5},-\\frac{12}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738140}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186738139} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ac4f421-423b-5cc5-a2ce-6c9fc1a6f47e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738123}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "a2fa40c6-398f-539c-9ed8-bf0c99b1a140" :question/problem "![](images/e5/e5a51635a55ba1839877f9043587dc8d27b86e2da77c9185d6d83d50bfa55896.png)\n\nFind the point on the line $2y-x=-5$ that is closest to the point $(1,2)$." :question/worked-solution "The closest point is where the given line meets the perpendicular line through $(1,2)$.\n\nFirst, rewrite the given line in slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2y-x&=-5 \\\\ 2y&=x-5 \\\\ y&=\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe given line has slope $\\frac{1}{2}$, so the perpendicular slope is $-2$, its negative reciprocal. Using point-slope form,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-y_1&=m(x-x_1) \\\\ y-(2)&=-2\\left(x-(1)\\right) \\\\ y&=-2x+2+(2) \\\\ y&=-2x+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ y &=-2x+4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nby setting the expressions for $y$ equal and collecting terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{5}{2}&=-2x+4 \\\\ \\left(\\frac{1}{2}-(-2)\\right)x&=4-\\left(-\\frac{5}{2}\\right) \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}x&=\\frac{13}{2} \\\\ x&=\\frac{13}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute into the given line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y&=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\frac{13}{5}\\right)+\\left(-\\frac{5}{2}\\right) \\\\ y&=\\frac{13}{10}+\\left(-\\frac{5}{2}\\right) \\\\ y&=-\\frac{6}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point on the line $2y-x=-5$ closest to $(1,2)$ is $(\\frac{13}{5},-\\frac{6}{5})$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186738134 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a7361d1-2a7a-55c9-92b2-2efa5e9b503b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{143}{25},\\frac{101}{25})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738122} {:answer/id #uuid "2e3c06a1-e495-5fcf-975e-072e68c5cfd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\frac{41}{25},-\\frac{37}{25})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738124} {:answer/id #uuid "5c612e15-d8d5-56a1-98fa-682da32d346d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{11}{25},\\frac{2}{25})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738127} {:answer/id #uuid "b9765e22-3f0d-54bb-afe5-09d194f636f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{3}{25},-\\frac{4}{25})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738137} {:answer/id #uuid "fb201786-3dcf-53f0-a785-61986d083df9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{67}{25},\\frac{44}{25})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738147}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186738122} :answer-field/id #uuid "8874db71-3ff8-5fda-a902-61361a881a27" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738130}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "ae27bcaa-52c7-5e51-9976-38303d9febfd" :question/problem "![](images/fa/fac2379455a0588e7408f2db4a2504963a546b70f92d1a1ac7472a6780714554.png)\n\nFind the point on the line $4y-3x=-1$ that is closest to the point $(5,5)$." :question/worked-solution "The closest point is where the given line meets the perpendicular line through $(5,5)$.\n\nFirst, rewrite the given line in slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4y-3x&=-1 \\\\ 4y&=3x-1 \\\\ y&=\\frac{3}{4}x-\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe given line has slope $\\frac{3}{4}$, so the perpendicular slope is $-\\frac{4}{3}$, its negative reciprocal. Using point-slope form,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-y_1&=m(x-x_1) \\\\ y-(5)&=-\\frac{4}{3}\\left(x-(5)\\right) \\\\ y&=-\\frac{4}{3}x+\\frac{20}{3}+(5) \\\\ y&=-\\frac{4}{3}x+\\frac{35}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=\\frac{3}{4}x-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ y &=-\\frac{4}{3}x+\\frac{35}{3}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nby setting the expressions for $y$ equal and collecting terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}x-\\frac{1}{4}&=-\\frac{4}{3}x+\\frac{35}{3} \\\\ \\left(\\frac{3}{4}-\\left(-\\frac{4}{3}\\right)\\right)x&=\\frac{35}{3}-\\left(-\\frac{1}{4}\\right) \\\\ \\frac{25}{12}x&=\\frac{143}{12} \\\\ x&=\\frac{143}{25}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute into the given line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y&=\\frac{3}{4}\\left(\\frac{143}{25}\\right)+\\left(-\\frac{1}{4}\\right) \\\\ y&=\\frac{429}{100}+\\left(-\\frac{1}{4}\\right) \\\\ y&=\\frac{101}{25}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point on the line $4y-3x=-1$ closest to $(5,5)$ is $(\\frac{143}{25},\\frac{101}{25})$."} {:answer/id #uuid "ae4e8e02-6073-5d38-a023-db597fb25384" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{19}{13},\\frac{9}{13})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738135} {:answer/id #uuid "b3368850-1a74-53a6-aa33-87859ed82560" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{37}{10},\\frac{9}{10})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738136} {:answer/id #uuid "b9765e22-3f0d-54bb-afe5-09d194f636f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{3}{25},-\\frac{4}{25})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738137} {:answer/id #uuid "bb6bdb16-c692-529c-8e4c-9f585ebbe9ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\frac{41}{13},-\\frac{81}{13})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738138} {:answer/id #uuid "c2d9ef84-4d77-52f2-b0d2-71cfb24bfeea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{13}{5},-\\frac{6}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738139} {:answer/id #uuid "d1a911a8-a82c-5f00-a384-6b9b109089e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{1}{5},-\\frac{12}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738140} {:answer/id #uuid "d27eff77-6b07-5f4b-95c6-a16244a1800f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{21}{13},\\frac{12}{13})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738141} {:answer/id #uuid "da86b2eb-fc54-5589-a183-187db00016b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{26}{5},\\frac{7}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738142} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186738145 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "017e0edf-1be4-5390-8759-43a3bfcda9ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{8}{5},\\frac{1}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738120} {:answer/id #uuid "70f0b31c-6389-564c-9b1b-6f983265e86e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\frac{29}{10},-\\frac{13}{10})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738129} {:answer/id #uuid "b3368850-1a74-53a6-aa33-87859ed82560" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{37}{10},\\frac{9}{10})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738136} {:answer/id #uuid "da86b2eb-fc54-5589-a183-187db00016b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{26}{5},\\frac{7}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738142} {:answer/id #uuid "f90fdeb5-e1df-5256-af12-defe09021d60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{7}{10},-\\frac{1}{10})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738146}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186738120} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec8fb25e-e3e4-5351-aa77-3650f32f256b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738143}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "f0f501d1-4e83-5bef-889c-ea8823fc37c6" :question/problem "![](images/89/89bf50ad31f50bc3522da3ced908554437efcc6d3f00d57668cf3839092432e2.png)\n\nFind the point on the line $3y-x=-1$ that is closest to the point $(1,2)$." :question/worked-solution "The closest point is where the given line meets the perpendicular line through $(1,2)$.\n\nFirst, rewrite the given line in slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3y-x&=-1 \\\\ 3y&=x-1 \\\\ y&=\\frac{1}{3}x-\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe given line has slope $\\frac{1}{3}$, so the perpendicular slope is $-3$, its negative reciprocal. Using point-slope form,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-y_1&=m(x-x_1) \\\\ y-(2)&=-3\\left(x-(1)\\right) \\\\ y&=-3x+3+(2) \\\\ y&=-3x+5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=\\frac{1}{3}x-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ y &=-3x+5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nby setting the expressions for $y$ equal and collecting terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}x-\\frac{1}{3}&=-3x+5 \\\\ \\left(\\frac{1}{3}-(-3)\\right)x&=5-\\left(-\\frac{1}{3}\\right) \\\\ \\frac{10}{3}x&=\\frac{16}{3} \\\\ x&=\\frac{8}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute into the given line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y&=\\frac{1}{3}\\left(\\frac{8}{5}\\right)+\\left(-\\frac{1}{3}\\right) \\\\ y&=\\frac{8}{15}+\\left(-\\frac{1}{3}\\right) \\\\ y&=\\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point on the line $3y-x=-1$ closest to $(1,2)$ is $(\\frac{8}{5},\\frac{1}{5})$."} {:answer/id #uuid "f90fdeb5-e1df-5256-af12-defe09021d60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{7}{10},-\\frac{1}{10})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738146} {:answer/id #uuid "fb201786-3dcf-53f0-a785-61986d083df9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{67}{25},\\frac{44}{25})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738147} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186738566 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "109e4f70-ebfa-57f5-be65-a5c28377f303" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(\\operatorname{sech}(-5)-\\operatorname{sech}(-1)\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738564} {:answer/id #uuid "36640630-6e87-5475-8bc2-3bf819169cdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\tanh(-5)-\\tanh(-1)\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738567} {:answer/id #uuid "90fd872f-d841-59e5-b009-c35dfdc77977" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(\\operatorname{csch}(-5)-\\operatorname{csch}(-1)\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738575} {:answer/id #uuid "97919f1e-f5bf-508f-9372-b6c2ebeb1e25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\operatorname{sech}(-5)-\\operatorname{sech}(-1)\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738578} {:answer/id #uuid "ef9dbc4c-7fd4-56f3-954f-82fef3a928b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}\\left(\\tanh(-5)-\\tanh(-1)\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738587}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186738567} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f1cad00-15d2-59f8-bcc7-ba8b8f3bf48b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738565}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "35335fb8-cc75-5fd5-972c-516f76495a34" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral.\n\n$$\n\\int_{3}^{9}\\operatorname{sech}^{2}(-\\frac{2x}{3}+1)\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=-\\frac{2x}{3}+1$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=-\\frac{2}{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}x$, so $\\mathrm{d}x=-\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}u$.\n\nRecall that $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}u}\\left(\\tanh(u)\\right)=\\operatorname{sech}^{2}(u)$. The transformed limits, in their original order, are:\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|}\\hline x & 3 & 9 \\\\ \\hline u & -1 & -5 \\\\ \\hline\\end{array}\n$$\n\nLet $I$ denote the given integral. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=-\\frac{3}{2}\\int_{-1}^{-5}\\operatorname{sech}^{2}(u)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\n&=-\\frac{3}{2}\\left[\\tanh(u)\\right]_{-1}^{-5} \\\\\n&=-\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\tanh(-5)-\\tanh(-1)\\right).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe interval contains no singularity. Subtract the lower endpoint contribution from the upper; a definite integral has no arbitrary constant."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186738569 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4bd55190-0224-5764-ab21-944086bfb397" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(\\operatorname{csch}(-4)-\\operatorname{csch}(-2)\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738570} {:answer/id #uuid "b5d322cc-76e1-5fa3-8311-980926b209bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\left(\\operatorname{csch}(-4)-\\operatorname{csch}(-2)\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738580} {:answer/id #uuid "d05a7741-65c9-5452-9532-ec18559bfe1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{csch}(-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738584} {:answer/id #uuid "e3db1a6c-3455-5389-942c-d1920585a2af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\left(\\operatorname{csch}(-3)-\\operatorname{csch}(-1)\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738585} {:answer/id #uuid "e48b82d7-b169-5484-950c-041111bb5351" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\left(\\tanh(-4)-\\tanh(-2)\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738586}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186738580} :answer-field/id #uuid "992a851e-858c-599f-8c47-c155890f36ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738579}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "392f2a79-8610-5048-a6e8-5c474a9a4d6b" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral.\n\n$$\n\\int_{2}^{6}\\operatorname{csch}(-\\frac{x}{2}-1)\\coth(-\\frac{x}{2}-1)\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=-\\frac{x}{2}-1$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x$, so $\\mathrm{d}x=-2\\,\\mathrm{d}u$.\n\nRecall that $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}u}\\left(-\\operatorname{csch}(u)\\right)=\\operatorname{csch}(u)\\coth(u)$. The transformed limits, in their original order, are:\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|}\\hline x & 2 & 6 \\\\ \\hline u & -2 & -4 \\\\ \\hline\\end{array}\n$$\n\nLet $I$ denote the given integral. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=-2\\int_{-2}^{-4}\\operatorname{csch}(u)\\coth(u)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\n&=-2\\left[-\\operatorname{csch}(u)\\right]_{-2}^{-4} \\\\\n&=2\\left(\\operatorname{csch}(-4)-\\operatorname{csch}(-2)\\right).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe interval contains no singularity. Subtract the lower endpoint contribution from the upper; a definite integral has no arbitrary constant."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186738583 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "033675b1-0d24-5d8f-bb62-7e5e7a47b615" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sech}(3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738563} {:answer/id #uuid "76d6b221-c8ed-562b-ad92-6fbabf365e03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\left(\\operatorname{sech}(1)-\\operatorname{sech}(3)\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738573} {:answer/id #uuid "b7d5976f-64e7-5e69-8c81-24661ae650e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\tanh(1)-\\tanh(3)\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738581} {:answer/id #uuid "f717f46b-9d07-5fe6-a003-15c81310fdb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\operatorname{sech}(1)-\\operatorname{sech}(3)\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738589} {:answer/id #uuid "ff72b396-f648-5b1d-899c-3423b4a6c3e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\left(\\coth(1)-\\coth(3)\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738590}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186738589} :answer-field/id #uuid "7666018a-8701-50a1-8290-bf5c4b62d6aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738572}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "cd410ed1-a87c-54c3-8763-99da7342a725" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral.\n\n$$\n\\int_{-3}^{0}\\operatorname{sech}(-\\frac{2x}{3}+1)\\tanh(-\\frac{2x}{3}+1)\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=-\\frac{2x}{3}+1$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=-\\frac{2}{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}x$, so $\\mathrm{d}x=-\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}u$.\n\nRecall that $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}u}\\left(-\\operatorname{sech}(u)\\right)=\\operatorname{sech}(u)\\tanh(u)$. The transformed limits, in their original order, are:\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|}\\hline x & -3 & 0 \\\\ \\hline u & 3 & 1 \\\\ \\hline\\end{array}\n$$\n\nLet $I$ denote the given integral. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=-\\frac{3}{2}\\int_{3}^{1}\\operatorname{sech}(u)\\tanh(u)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\n&=-\\frac{3}{2}\\left[-\\operatorname{sech}(u)\\right]_{3}^{1} \\\\\n&=\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\operatorname{sech}(1)-\\operatorname{sech}(3)\\right).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe interval contains no singularity. Subtract the lower endpoint contribution from the upper; a definite integral has no arbitrary constant."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186738588 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "389c21c0-d3ed-5380-a9ad-1119a90323e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\left(\\operatorname{csch}(1)-\\operatorname{csch}(4)\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738568} {:answer/id #uuid "82815055-2b31-5722-a23d-82b8746cb800" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\coth(1)-\\coth(4)\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738574} {:answer/id #uuid "957f4bd0-33dd-5944-a07a-4ddc79a2c7af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\left(\\coth(1)+\\coth(4)\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738576} {:answer/id #uuid "95c73600-8827-52b5-ad72-8eda2ef615b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\left(\\coth(1)-\\coth(4)\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738577} {:answer/id #uuid "cba9f1af-ad5b-5adc-a73f-ffc56f47c3ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\coth(1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738582}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186738577} :answer-field/id #uuid "759a1b21-9332-53ea-ace1-4e9f0c3b54ed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738571}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "f21889df-ba37-5df5-b68b-7d352672d98a" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral.\n\n$$\n\\int_{-2}^{0}\\operatorname{csch}^{2}(-\\frac{3x}{2}+1)\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=-\\frac{3x}{2}+1$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=-\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x$, so $\\mathrm{d}x=-\\frac{2}{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}u$.\n\nRecall that $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}u}\\left(-\\coth(u)\\right)=\\operatorname{csch}^{2}(u)$. The transformed limits, in their original order, are:\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|}\\hline x & -2 & 0 \\\\ \\hline u & 4 & 1 \\\\ \\hline\\end{array}\n$$\n\nLet $I$ denote the given integral. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=-\\frac{2}{3}\\int_{4}^{1}\\operatorname{csch}^{2}(u)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\n&=-\\frac{2}{3}\\left[-\\coth(u)\\right]_{4}^{1} \\\\\n&=\\frac{2}{3}\\left(\\coth(1)-\\coth(4)\\right).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe interval contains no singularity. Subtract the lower endpoint contribution from the upper; a definite integral has no arbitrary constant."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186738603 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60bc5e78-63b5-5817-ba58-6477868cadb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3\\ln\\left(\\frac{16}{15}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738595} {:answer/id #uuid "66f8e09f-2a97-5f9c-8a88-de5680ca2cac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6\\ln\\left(\\frac{16}{15}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738597} {:answer/id #uuid "72a11c14-884b-5f5c-ae69-87b8398d3c0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3\\ln\\left(\\frac{10}{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738600} {:answer/id #uuid "894e7e96-a5ab-51d2-beac-7f5a1c8c96a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3\\ln\\left(\\frac{8}{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738602} {:answer/id #uuid "b6464a39-a655-5489-99d6-29cb8a28b1b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\ln\\left(\\frac{10}{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738611}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186738602} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab852121-a8be-51b0-bdea-2306b2dd430d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738608}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "8a64810a-4dfd-5a75-9305-24aaa99923c8" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral\n\n$$\n\\int_{\\ln\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{\\ln\\left(3\\right)}\\frac{-3\\cosh\\left(x\\right)}{\\sinh\\left(x\\right)+2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\sinh\\left(x\\right)+2$. Then $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\cosh\\left(x\\right)$, so $-3\\cosh\\left(x\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x=-3\\,\\mathrm{d}u$.\n\nUse $\\sinh t=(e^t-e^{-t})/2$ to evaluate the transformed limits:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu(\\ln\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right))&=\\frac{\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{1}-\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{-1}}{2}+2=\\frac{5}{4} \\\\[4pt]u(\\ln\\left(3\\right))&=\\frac{(3)^{1}-(3)^{-1}}{2}+2=\\frac{10}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe denominator is monotone and positive between these endpoints, so $u>0$. Thus\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\int_{\\ln\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{\\ln\\left(3\\right)}\\frac{-3\\cosh\\left(x\\right)}{\\sinh\\left(x\\right)+2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\[4pt]&=-3\\int_{\\frac{5}{4}}^{\\frac{10}{3}}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\[4pt]&=-3\\left[\\ln u\\right]_{\\frac{5}{4}}^{\\frac{10}{3}} \\\\[4pt]&=-3\\left(\\ln\\left(\\frac{10}{3}\\right)-\\ln\\left(\\frac{5}{4}\\right)\\right) \\\\[4pt]&=-3\\ln\\left(\\frac{8}{3}\\right).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe final step uses the logarithm quotient rule on positive arguments."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186738604 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "949dfc97-0e29-529a-a787-9ee2cd4b537b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\ln\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738605} {:answer/id #uuid "99acc242-b881-57a4-91ca-40da2d259ac0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\ln\\left(\\frac{16}{75}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738606} {:answer/id #uuid "abf1cad9-60b0-5d6f-a7bb-7f92cf3478f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\ln\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738609} {:answer/id #uuid "ad63acc5-26a0-5837-9d7f-8c83c0bbcff0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\ln\\left(\\frac{25}{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738610} {:answer/id #uuid "f326fe56-2683-5d5e-b319-7eee1f2c6c5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\ln\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738617}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186738617} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1e4b3c9-5b40-5120-9e69-a40595b11828" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186738613}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "930539b7-88d6-5a16-a5de-43406b1e41e1" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral\n\n$$\n\\int_{\\ln\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{\\ln\\left(3\\right)}\\frac{\\cosh\\left(x\\right)}{\\sinh\\left(x\\right)+7}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\sinh\\left(x\\right)+7$. Then $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\cosh\\left(x\\right)$, so $\\cosh\\left(x\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x=1\\,\\mathrm{d}u$.\n\nUse $\\sinh t=(e^t-e^{-t})/2$ to evaluate the transformed limits:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu(\\ln\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right))&=\\frac{\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{1}-\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{-1}}{2}+7=\\frac{25}{4} \\\\[4pt]u(\\ln\\left(3\\right))&=\\frac{(3)^{1}-(3)^{-1}}{2}+7=\\frac{25}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe denominator is monotone and positive between these endpoints, so $u>0$. Thus\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\int_{\\ln\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{\\ln\\left(3\\right)}\\frac{\\cosh\\left(x\\right)}{\\sinh\\left(x\\right)+7}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\[4pt]&=\\int_{\\frac{25}{4}}^{\\frac{25}{3}}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\[4pt]&=\\left[\\ln u\\right]_{\\frac{25}{4}}^{\\frac{25}{3}} \\\\[4pt]&=\\left(\\ln\\left(\\frac{25}{3}\\right)-\\ln\\left(\\frac{25}{4}\\right)\\right) \\\\[4pt]&=\\ln\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe final step uses the logarithm quotient rule on positive arguments."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186739331 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0146086-f786-5af0-8327-b6515ab9eb6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{23}{4}\\ln\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)+\\frac{3}{4}\\ln\\left(3\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186739335}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186739335} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f5b1609-5610-535a-8de7-72fce1c9422f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186739333}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4a32402e-8894-5345-b8ef-fb821ba0612e" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{2}^{4}\\frac{2 - 5 x}{(x - 5)(x - 1)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The poles $x=5$ and $x=1$ lie outside $[2,4]$. Set up partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2 - 5 x}{(x - 5)(x - 1)}=\\frac{A}{x - 5}+\\frac{B}{x - 1}\n$$\n\nClear the denominators:\n\n$$\n2 - 5 x=A(x - 1)+B(x - 5)\n$$\n\nSubstitute the zeros of the factors to determine the coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=5:\\quad -23 &= 4A,\\qquad A=- \\frac{23}{4} \\\\ x=1:\\quad -3 &= -4B,\\qquad B=\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus\n\n$$\n\\frac{2 - 5 x}{(x - 5)(x - 1)}=-\\frac{23}{4(x - 5)}+\\frac{3}{4(x - 1)}\n$$\n\nFor each linear factor, use $\\int\\frac{1}{kx+t}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{1}{k}\\ln|kx+t|+C$. The reciprocal slopes are $1$ and $1$, respectively.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x)&=-\\frac{23}{4}(1\\ln\\left|x - 5\\right|)+\\frac{3}{4}(1\\ln\\left|x - 1\\right|) \\\\ &=-\\frac{23}{4}\\ln\\left|x - 5\\right|+\\frac{3}{4}\\ln\\left|x - 1\\right|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the absolute values of the factor values at the endpoints:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(4)&=\\frac{3}{4}\\ln\\left(3\\right) \\\\ F(2)&=-\\frac{23}{4}\\ln\\left(3\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubtract the lower-limit value. For positive arguments, $\\ln U-\\ln V=\\ln(U/V)$, so write $I$ for the given integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I&=F(4)-F(2) \\\\ &=(\\frac{3}{4}\\ln\\left(3\\right)) \\\\ &\\quad-(-\\frac{23}{4}\\ln\\left(3\\right))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the quotient law to each pair of logarithms gives\n\n$$\n-\\frac{23}{4}\\ln\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)+\\frac{3}{4}\\ln\\left(3\\right).\n$$\n\n"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186739332 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "238a4599-a8c4-5ca0-ad7b-7f72689a3641" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{12}{5}\\ln\\left(4\\right)-\\frac{2}{5}\\ln\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186739328}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186739328} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e194ad5-d4f7-5130-96e0-6ac2bb86ec8f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186739334}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6b34e75f-7ad3-5399-a3bd-ddfab7c4cce3" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{-3}^{0}\\frac{2 x - 4}{(x + 4)(x - 1)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The poles $x=-4$ and $x=1$ lie outside $[-3,0]$. Set up partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2 x - 4}{(x + 4)(x - 1)}=\\frac{A}{x + 4}+\\frac{B}{x - 1}\n$$\n\nClear the denominators:\n\n$$\n2 x - 4=A(x - 1)+B(x + 4)\n$$\n\nSubstitute the zeros of the factors to determine the coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=-4:\\quad -12 &= -5A,\\qquad A=\\frac{12}{5} \\\\ x=1:\\quad -2 &= 5B,\\qquad B=- \\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus\n\n$$\n\\frac{2 x - 4}{(x + 4)(x - 1)}=\\frac{12}{5(x + 4)}-\\frac{2}{5(x - 1)}\n$$\n\nFor each linear factor, use $\\int\\frac{1}{kx+t}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{1}{k}\\ln|kx+t|+C$. The reciprocal slopes are $1$ and $1$, respectively.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x)&=\\frac{12}{5}(1\\ln\\left|x + 4\\right|)-\\frac{2}{5}(1\\ln\\left|x - 1\\right|) \\\\ &=\\frac{12}{5}\\ln\\left|x + 4\\right|-\\frac{2}{5}\\ln\\left|x - 1\\right|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the absolute values of the factor values at the endpoints:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(0)&=\\frac{12}{5}\\ln\\left(4\\right) \\\\ F(-3)&=-\\frac{2}{5}\\ln\\left(4\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubtract the lower-limit value. For positive arguments, $\\ln U-\\ln V=\\ln(U/V)$, so write $I$ for the given integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I&=F(0)-F(-3) \\\\ &=(\\frac{12}{5}\\ln\\left(4\\right)) \\\\ &\\quad-(-\\frac{2}{5}\\ln\\left(4\\right))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the quotient law to each pair of logarithms gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{12}{5}\\ln\\left(4\\right)-\\frac{2}{5}\\ln\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right).\n$$\n\n"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186739338 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27065f53-d005-52fb-8deb-efc8a1bc6648" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{5}\\ln\\left(\\frac{6}{7}\\right)+\\frac{1}{5}\\ln\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186739329}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186739329} :answer-field/id #uuid "daa4dfde-101e-5aaf-9098-d8f62df0fa11" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186739339}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "bb23b6ee-84d2-55ca-8fec-726773712194" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{-2}^{-1}\\frac{4 x - 1}{(x - 5)(x)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The poles $x=5$ and $x=0$ lie outside $[-2,-1]$. Set up partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4 x - 1}{(x - 5)(x)}=\\frac{A}{x - 5}+\\frac{B}{x}\n$$\n\nClear the denominators:\n\n$$\n4 x - 1=A(x)+B(x - 5)\n$$\n\nSubstitute the zeros of the factors to determine the coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=5:\\quad 19 &= 5A,\\qquad A=\\frac{19}{5} \\\\ x=0:\\quad -1 &= -5B,\\qquad B=\\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus\n\n$$\n\\frac{4 x - 1}{(x - 5)(x)}=\\frac{19}{5(x - 5)}+\\frac{1}{5(x)}\n$$\n\nFor each linear factor, use $\\int\\frac{1}{kx+t}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{1}{k}\\ln|kx+t|+C$. The reciprocal slopes are $1$ and $1$, respectively.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x)&=\\frac{19}{5}(1\\ln\\left|x - 5\\right|)+\\frac{1}{5}(1\\ln\\left|x\\right|) \\\\ &=\\frac{19}{5}\\ln\\left|x - 5\\right|+\\frac{1}{5}\\ln\\left|x\\right|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the absolute values of the factor values at the endpoints:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(-1)&=\\frac{19}{5}\\ln\\left(6\\right) \\\\ F(-2)&=\\frac{19}{5}\\ln\\left(7\\right)+\\frac{1}{5}\\ln\\left(2\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubtract the lower-limit value. For positive arguments, $\\ln U-\\ln V=\\ln(U/V)$, so write $I$ for the given integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I&=F(-1)-F(-2) \\\\ &=(\\frac{19}{5}\\ln\\left(6\\right)) \\\\ &\\quad-(\\frac{19}{5}\\ln\\left(7\\right)+\\frac{1}{5}\\ln\\left(2\\right))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the quotient law to each pair of logarithms gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{19}{5}\\ln\\left(\\frac{6}{7}\\right)+\\frac{1}{5}\\ln\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right).\n$$\n\n"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186739341 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b86ad604-b456-5ea5-9610-5e68b32521a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{5}\\ln\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)+\\frac{17}{5}\\ln\\left(\\frac{5}{8}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186739337}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186739337} :answer-field/id #uuid "30ae2100-07c7-5bdd-8e95-858ff71a6a78" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186739330}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "fec9f9dc-db36-5c1d-ad3f-2982d7ca48a7" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{-2}^{1}\\frac{5 x + 4}{(x + 4)(x - 6)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The poles $x=-4$ and $x=6$ lie outside $[-2,1]$. Set up partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5 x + 4}{(x + 4)(x - 6)}=\\frac{A}{x + 4}+\\frac{B}{x - 6}\n$$\n\nClear the denominators:\n\n$$\n5 x + 4=A(x - 6)+B(x + 4)\n$$\n\nSubstitute the zeros of the factors to determine the coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=-4:\\quad -16 &= -10A,\\qquad A=\\frac{8}{5} \\\\ x=6:\\quad 34 &= 10B,\\qquad B=\\frac{17}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus\n\n$$\n\\frac{5 x + 4}{(x + 4)(x - 6)}=\\frac{8}{5(x + 4)}+\\frac{17}{5(x - 6)}\n$$\n\nFor each linear factor, use $\\int\\frac{1}{kx+t}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{1}{k}\\ln|kx+t|+C$. The reciprocal slopes are $1$ and $1$, respectively.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x)&=\\frac{8}{5}(1\\ln\\left|x + 4\\right|)+\\frac{17}{5}(1\\ln\\left|x - 6\\right|) \\\\ &=\\frac{8}{5}\\ln\\left|x + 4\\right|+\\frac{17}{5}\\ln\\left|x - 6\\right|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the absolute values of the factor values at the endpoints:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1)&=\\frac{8}{5}\\ln\\left(5\\right)+\\frac{17}{5}\\ln\\left(5\\right) \\\\ F(-2)&=\\frac{8}{5}\\ln\\left(2\\right)+\\frac{17}{5}\\ln\\left(8\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubtract the lower-limit value. For positive arguments, $\\ln U-\\ln V=\\ln(U/V)$, so write $I$ for the given integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I&=F(1)-F(-2) \\\\ &=(\\frac{8}{5}\\ln\\left(5\\right)+\\frac{17}{5}\\ln\\left(5\\right)) \\\\ &\\quad-(\\frac{8}{5}\\ln\\left(2\\right)+\\frac{17}{5}\\ln\\left(8\\right))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the quotient law to each pair of logarithms gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{8}{5}\\ln\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)+\\frac{17}{5}\\ln\\left(\\frac{5}{8}\\right).\n$$\n\n"} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f52c3a2-903a-54c7-9a8f-23501f50036d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740027} {:answer/id #uuid "e88b54d8-7b4f-5295-be97-57d6a4b1a43e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740049}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186740049} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba4ade89-0766-5857-9b0d-bb5f09d1d9de" :answer-field/key "The function is negative throughout each interval $(-\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi,n\\pi)$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740041} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df1806aa-7a20-5789-84f5-60dd3886c5c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740202} {:answer/id #uuid "ec22f4e2-9a44-5974-be28-7457d59769fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740203}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186740203} :answer-field/id #uuid "03e4239d-25df-5f86-bc3e-682dad624a83" :answer-field/key "The function is increasing throughout the interval $(\\frac{3\\pi}{2},2\\pi)$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740145} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186740169 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89d6b481-d201-54ad-b330-483e8e3809bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740181} {:answer/id #uuid "8c79839f-ebed-52f5-bb5a-22aa8a8a2ed2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740182}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186740181} :answer-field/id #uuid "1284e2bd-88ee-55aa-9798-07c0ba58ab17" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740149} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61ee3567-310d-52eb-990f-212f8a0eeab9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740172} {:answer/id #uuid "b2c42bad-5a1a-5467-85fe-e010b5864291" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740192}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186740172} :answer-field/id #uuid "50b1b102-eb45-5d31-8a97-2cdd6a2be79f" :answer-field/key "The function has a global maximum value of $-1$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740168} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b8f977e-11d7-576f-b7e5-ddfd1ef1664e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740186} {:answer/id #uuid "ed112964-90d5-5693-b523-4ec1d3d214e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740204}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186740204} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a5ce1e5-e391-56ff-a1fa-dfa497664973" :answer-field/key "The range of the function is $(-\\infty,-1]\\cup[1,\\infty)$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740185} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b7db129-87e3-51c0-bdc8-5502704c8f98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740151} {:answer/id #uuid "ab722299-ffeb-5920-9e89-71540f8f44e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740190}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186740190} :answer-field/id #uuid "d99840da-d44e-54d6-be78-49f719344f1a" :answer-field/key "The function is increasing throughout the interval $(\\frac{\\pi}{2},\\pi)$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740200}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "59f527ef-4d88-596b-ba76-14b9471f2bfc" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\csc x$?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The graph of $y=\\csc x$ is shown below.\n\n![Graph of the untransformed cosecant function. ](images/a9/a92d46319d381f0a8cab7823021b3b7e9b5c030ad964586b8e72129a2cd5abe7.png)\n\nCheck each statement.\n\n**The function has a global maximum value of $-1$.**\n\nThe range $(-\\infty,-1]\\cup[1,\\infty)$ is unbounded above and below. The vertices of individual branches do not give a global minimum or maximum.\n\nThis statement is **false**.\n\n**The range of the function is $(-\\infty,-1]\\cup[1,\\infty)$.**\n\nWhere defined, $0<|\\sin x|\\leq1$. Its reciprocals fill $(-\\infty,-1]\\cup[1,\\infty)$. Both $-1$ and $1$ are attained, and both rays are unbounded.\n\nThis statement is **true**.\n\n**The function is increasing throughout the interval $(\\frac{\\pi}{2},\\pi)$.**\n\nBetween the asymptotes $x=0$ and $x=\\pi$, the branch is positive. It is decreasing on $(0,\\frac{\\pi}{2})$ and increasing on $(\\frac{\\pi}{2},\\pi)$. At the midpoint $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$, its value is $1$. This follows by taking reciprocals along the positive sine arch; translation by $2\\pi$ preserves the behavior.\n\nThis statement is **true**.\n\nSelect the following statements:\n\n- The range of the function is $(-\\infty,-1]\\cup[1,\\infty)$.\n- The function is increasing throughout the interval $(\\frac{\\pi}{2},\\pi)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186740184 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df1806aa-7a20-5789-84f5-60dd3886c5c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740202} {:answer/id #uuid "ec22f4e2-9a44-5974-be28-7457d59769fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740203}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186740203} :answer-field/id #uuid "03e4239d-25df-5f86-bc3e-682dad624a83" :answer-field/key "The function is increasing throughout the interval $(\\frac{3\\pi}{2},2\\pi)$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740145} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27f23c69-a64f-50f0-b312-6ad1e783e4f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740157} {:answer/id #uuid "38bf1b7f-906c-5ccd-882a-4e48de77f450" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740162}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186740162} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4b960ec-27b0-52c2-8d89-f8fbb5733856" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740188} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20c66948-93bd-5daa-b5bd-3ee16d789b38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740153} {:answer/id #uuid "41a61473-a263-5065-83fd-0dc22e5a802a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740166}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186740153} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2da503a-6409-5ab9-817e-68c739f17d20" :answer-field/key "The point $(-\\frac{3\\pi}{2},1)$ is on the graph." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740193} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f343385-50e3-5577-918a-0c29f48071a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740171} {:answer/id #uuid "8499fd0c-2b11-5edc-ab5a-b09b48739744" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740179}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186740171} :answer-field/id #uuid "c337101b-58e0-5736-bb0b-714661601773" :answer-field/key "The function has no zeros." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740197}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "927f0e96-c1aa-57c7-a766-678090fa7b17" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\csc x$?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The graph of $y=\\csc x$ is shown below.\n\n![Graph of the untransformed cosecant function. ](images/a9/a92d46319d381f0a8cab7823021b3b7e9b5c030ad964586b8e72129a2cd5abe7.png)\n\nCheck each statement.\n\n**The function has no zeros.**\n\nA reciprocal with numerator $1$ cannot be zero. At a zero of sine, cosecant is undefined, rather than zero. Thus cosecant has no zeros.\n\nThis statement is **true**.\n\n**The point $(-\\frac{3\\pi}{2},1)$ is on the graph.**\n\nUsing the period $2\\pi$ and $\\csc x=1/\\sin x$,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-\\frac{3\\pi}{2} &=\\frac{\\pi}{2}-2\\pi \\\\ \\sin\\left(-\\frac{3\\pi}{2}\\right) &=1 \\\\ \\csc\\left(-\\frac{3\\pi}{2}\\right) &=\\frac{1}{1}=1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is **true**.\n\n**The function is increasing throughout the interval $(\\frac{3\\pi}{2},2\\pi)$.**\n\nBetween the asymptotes $x=\\pi$ and $x=2\\pi$, the branch is negative. It is increasing on $(\\pi,\\frac{3\\pi}{2})$ and decreasing on $(\\frac{3\\pi}{2},2\\pi)$. At the midpoint $x=\\frac{3\\pi}{2}$, its value is $-1$. This follows by taking reciprocals along the negative sine arch; translation by $2\\pi$ preserves the behavior.\n\nThis statement is **false**.\n\nSelect the following statements:\n\n- The function has no zeros.\n- The point $(-\\frac{3\\pi}{2},1)$ is on the graph."} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20c66948-93bd-5daa-b5bd-3ee16d789b38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740153} {:answer/id #uuid "41a61473-a263-5065-83fd-0dc22e5a802a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740166}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186740153} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2da503a-6409-5ab9-817e-68c739f17d20" :answer-field/key "The point $(-\\frac{3\\pi}{2},1)$ is on the graph." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740193} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b7db129-87e3-51c0-bdc8-5502704c8f98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740151} {:answer/id #uuid "ab722299-ffeb-5920-9e89-71540f8f44e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740190}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186740190} :answer-field/id #uuid "d99840da-d44e-54d6-be78-49f719344f1a" :answer-field/key "The function is increasing throughout the interval $(\\frac{\\pi}{2},\\pi)$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740200} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186740206 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "225e9a7a-c4fa-569f-b526-c8307c004a03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740155} {:answer/id #uuid "6a4377d9-87dc-5a53-a886-7aba86ff3aae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740174}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186740155} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a1a780f-57d4-51c7-9f6d-205ae91f1118" :answer-field/key "The range of the function is $[-1,1]$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740150} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04be97dd-0980-53bf-a051-cf3bd3a9051f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740146} {:answer/id #uuid "5a386509-eafb-51b9-b555-e9edf37de13c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740170}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186740146} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d78631d-ef15-5e98-9d57-1e708c1bdd7b" :answer-field/key "The function is increasing and then decreasing on the interval $(\\pi,2\\pi)$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740159} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49bcbddd-8ef1-502b-85d4-ef6822289ae8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740167} {:answer/id #uuid "76ecdc21-6a10-5450-9784-4cd69f16d7e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740177}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186740177} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fc16eac-0da7-5a95-8a55-7695ab8182de" :answer-field/key "The function has a global minimum value of $1$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740164} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "060cbc44-5c50-5277-8810-7d58e891c957" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740147} {:answer/id #uuid "32fe83af-ff76-58df-8c30-8a629a0eeee6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740160}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186740160} :answer-field/id #uuid "f79f618e-4dd8-5a65-9acc-01c359dc7d3c" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740207}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f73c232e-3640-5ff8-9522-d73f351eccef" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\csc x$?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The graph of $y=\\csc x$ is shown below.\n\n![Graph of the untransformed cosecant function. ](images/a9/a92d46319d381f0a8cab7823021b3b7e9b5c030ad964586b8e72129a2cd5abe7.png)\n\nCheck each statement.\n\n**The function is increasing and then decreasing on the interval $(\\pi,2\\pi)$.**\n\nBetween the asymptotes $x=\\pi$ and $x=2\\pi$, the branch is negative. It is increasing on $(\\pi,\\frac{3\\pi}{2})$ and decreasing on $(\\frac{3\\pi}{2},2\\pi)$. At the midpoint $x=\\frac{3\\pi}{2}$, its value is $-1$. This follows by taking reciprocals along the negative sine arch; translation by $2\\pi$ preserves the behavior.\n\nThis statement is **true**.\n\n**The range of the function is $[-1,1]$.**\n\nWhere defined, $0<|\\sin x|\\leq1$. Its reciprocals fill $(-\\infty,-1]\\cup[1,\\infty)$. Both $-1$ and $1$ are attained, and both rays are unbounded.\n\nThis statement is **false**.\n\n**The function has a global minimum value of $1$.**\n\nThe range $(-\\infty,-1]\\cup[1,\\infty)$ is unbounded above and below. The vertices of individual branches do not give a global minimum or maximum.\n\nThis statement is **false**.\n\nSelect the following statement:\n\n- The function is increasing and then decreasing on the interval $(\\pi,2\\pi)$."} {:answer/id #uuid "0f71db3d-9de4-59ef-b363-683b434325df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\frac{1}{2},4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740384} {:answer/id #uuid "5037de70-b716-5848-acc0-8830b0098454" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\frac{1}{2},-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740386} {:answer/id #uuid "5d0c7193-6890-5637-af32-12aa480dbc7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\frac{1}{2},-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740389} {:answer/id #uuid "7dbe91f5-686f-52be-9e29-5faa085e9554" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\frac{3}{2},-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740394} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186740399 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f71db3d-9de4-59ef-b363-683b434325df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\frac{1}{2},4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740384} {:answer/id #uuid "5037de70-b716-5848-acc0-8830b0098454" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\frac{1}{2},-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740386} {:answer/id #uuid "5d0c7193-6890-5637-af32-12aa480dbc7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\frac{1}{2},-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740389} {:answer/id #uuid "6504c0e1-641d-549f-b46a-26b1eb254ba4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-3,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740390} {:answer/id #uuid "7dbe91f5-686f-52be-9e29-5faa085e9554" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\frac{3}{2},-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740394}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186740386} :answer-field/id #uuid "5742120c-8ac0-542e-a368-8f03f5643ab5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740388}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e1cb6d40-1680-5c98-b884-ba1e1208c7cd" :question/problem "The point $(-2,3)$ lies on the curve $y=f(x).$ Which of the following points **must** lie on $y=-f(2x-1)+1?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1: Transform the point**\n\nWrite the argument as $2(x-\\frac{1}{2})$. First compress the graph horizontally by a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{2}$, then shift it $\\frac{1}{2}$ unit to the right. Reflect the result across the $x$-axis, then shift it $1$ unit up. The point moves as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(-2,3)&\\longmapsto(-1,3)\\\\\n &\\longmapsto\\left(-\\frac{1}{2},3\\right)\\\\\n &\\longmapsto\\left(-\\frac{1}{2},-3\\right)\\\\\n &\\longmapsto\\left(-\\frac{1}{2},-2\\right).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2: Evaluate the transformed function**\n\nThe given point tells us that $f(-2)=3$. To use this known value in the transformed function, solve\n\n$$\n2x-1=-2\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad 2x=-1\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nAt this horizontal coordinate,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny&=-f\\left(2\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)-1\\right)+1\\\\\n &=-f(-2)+1\\\\\n &=-3+1\\\\\n &=-2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\left(-\\frac{1}{2},-2\\right)$ must lie on the transformed curve."} {:answer/id #uuid "f79234de-77c8-5ad7-93aa-3229342dea9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-2,\\frac{10}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740443} {:answer/id #uuid "a939f57b-6038-5ebe-bc6a-e3ed357efd90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{1}{2},3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740526} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186740716 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "321c3a4d-843e-5c13-a7e4-1455c760986b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/3b/3b3f78234689b7a8c9bb9b1b5806b2d8de8b8723f819d11e1a858162a5acc872.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740724} {:answer/id #uuid "3458a312-c34a-5da6-857d-bd4fb83a9e10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/0c/0c6f0a3af6b3008c8935977ce7ce5adc3561402027ea5dea8be6ffe81c00fecc.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740726} {:answer/id #uuid "9abb19cf-76ff-5dc9-8d43-51e01bf76a79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/ad/adff1314bf67ad458491da23c6afd98f9f24d0aeef5ed0b7650b14fb202fd454.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740730} {:answer/id #uuid "b15df807-6bcd-5c98-a4ff-baed9c20adc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/97/97c92de32c832fbdf3d1cbf6f8c78545f63cc97e6d95abeafe006ba5404dd591.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740732} {:answer/id #uuid "b4ce7673-e36e-5fca-b289-411042016f3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/d6/d66b99f60b054c2aa31f05006ea6b29191ccaaab895d63da333b5b3067510dd3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740733}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186740726} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc21bbf4-0208-5946-94b4-0da5f4c317ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740734}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "087406d6-b172-5771-b5e4-0908197a7f01" :question/problem "Which of the following is the graph of $y=\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^x-\\frac{1}{2}$?" :question/worked-solution "First, consider the graph of $y=\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^x:$\n\n![](images/1e/1ea7634d782d52e7146e3c42cf88052a91adc9d1cea564db697a6dda070036fa.png)\n\nThe term $-\\frac{1}{2}$ outside the exponential shifts every point $\\frac{1}{2}$ units down. The $y$-intercept moves from $(0,1)$ to $(0,\\frac{1}{2}),$ because $\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^0+\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)=1+\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)=\\frac{1}{2}.$ The horizontal asymptote moves from $y=0$ to $y=-\\frac{1}{2}.$ The curve is still increasing, since the base is greater than $1.$\n\n![](images/58/58c7399794cef762e42310742100c7e55ee863e9a0f62cb296da67e40b91b7d2.png)\n\nChoose the increasing curve with horizontal asymptote $y=-\\frac{1}{2}$ and $y$-intercept $(0,\\frac{1}{2}).$ The orange curve shows the original graph; the blue curve shows the translation."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186740723 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ed5fb23-3443-586f-9db9-ed3e7ffbedc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/ca/ca55e103719b5b95c20ba3626de50a51f822d0ebbff2ad9b3be6b7123285a686.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740719} {:answer/id #uuid "1b55d808-e51f-5511-95bf-68155306b032" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/a9/a9af680304aca62e3600e00133ce8fb42c6636017376a0820d10abd17fca0449.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740721} {:answer/id #uuid "67cddc74-a883-5606-ade9-f78cf1936bc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/48/48c56473b18abc39f6e2b2788d9f1669fc5b063d57367a86858c49a1472b929a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740728} {:answer/id #uuid "aa2520a2-4ebf-506c-ac0a-84c03b32d6ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/73/737272ca88c205b35e35024d47f995bd59a7d7936fb49d1a0bc9b374be9e396f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740731} {:answer/id #uuid "ec9a3e0c-67ed-5e78-897d-fed631fb0900" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/a9/a9dc51addee7ca94b8febfe9b4bc4b389109f5b6f7d2798381d45a66ee10a166.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740735}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186740721} :answer-field/id #uuid "772ac40c-07e0-5f39-b387-09ecaa543bcc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740729}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "3126c589-37e3-53bc-8ea7-47303b571f6c" :question/problem "Which of the following is the graph of $y=\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right)^x-\\frac{5}{3}$?" :question/worked-solution "First, consider the graph of $y=\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right)^x:$\n\n![](images/1e/1ea7634d782d52e7146e3c42cf88052a91adc9d1cea564db697a6dda070036fa.png)\n\nThe term $-\\frac{5}{3}$ outside the exponential shifts every point $\\frac{5}{3}$ units down. The $y$-intercept moves from $(0,1)$ to $(0,-\\frac{2}{3}),$ because $\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right)^0+\\left(-\\frac{5}{3}\\right)=1+\\left(-\\frac{5}{3}\\right)=-\\frac{2}{3}.$ The horizontal asymptote moves from $y=0$ to $y=-\\frac{5}{3}.$ The curve is still increasing, since the base is greater than $1.$\n\n![](images/0a/0a32ad82673e20efac8dc092f802d8583653382508130e5b374a22d003d853f9.png)\n\nChoose the increasing curve with horizontal asymptote $y=-\\frac{5}{3}$ and $y$-intercept $(0,-\\frac{2}{3}).$ The orange curve shows the original graph; the blue curve shows the translation."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186740836 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10e1d1f0-69a9-58f3-9c61-feab58e8fe31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(4,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740837} {:answer/id #uuid "46fbe3a5-dcf8-54b7-9323-e57ab8641765" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-1,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740843} {:answer/id #uuid "66961056-18dd-5072-b156-c614fb22170e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-1,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740847} {:answer/id #uuid "6fce709f-cd5a-5b42-b44e-40a253a34307" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(4,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740848} {:answer/id #uuid "b6544d99-f147-55a6-a8cf-d16341c6c1f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(4,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740855}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186740847} :answer-field/id #uuid "23b856e7-92a1-577c-8beb-4c5a9a9d5229" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740840}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "0a242fe7-fa2e-5265-a03d-c9ef053bee01" :question/problem "The point $(3,-5)$ lies on the curve $y=f\\left(x\\right)$. Which of the following points **must** lie on $y=-f\\left(1-2x\\right)-1$?" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1: Transform the point**\n\nStarting from the original graph, reflect across the $y$-axis, then scale horizontally by $\\frac{1}{2}$, then translate $\\frac{1}{2}$ units right, then reflect across the $x$-axis, then translate $1$ unit down. The corresponding points are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3,-5)&\\longmapsto (-\\frac{3}{2},-5)\\\\ &\\longmapsto (-1,-5)\\\\ &\\longmapsto (-1,5)\\\\ &\\longmapsto (-1,4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2: Substitute into the equation**\n\nThe given point tells us that $f\\left(3\\right)=-5$. To reproduce this known input in the transformed curve, solve\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-2x&=3\\\\ -2x&=2\\\\ x&=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt this horizontal coordinate,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y&=-f\\left(-2\\cdot \\left(-1\\right)+1\\right)-1\\\\ &=-f\\left(3\\right)-1\\\\ &=-\\left(-5\\right)-1\\\\ &=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $(-1,4)$ must lie on the transformed curve."} {:answer/id #uuid "43d64529-0640-56ee-aa46-33600075d688" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\frac{1}{2},1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740841} {:answer/id #uuid "4695bb72-607e-5677-a342-07a2355570bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\frac{1}{2},3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740842} {:answer/id #uuid "56bf9cc7-a411-5f11-af70-42b523af5968" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{5}{2},-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740845} {:answer/id #uuid "89072967-eff0-5b9f-8b98-f99a265a8d97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{5}{2},-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740851} {:answer/id #uuid "a50b6246-0f38-5f6c-96bb-42ff728f301d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\frac{3}{2},6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740853} {:answer/id #uuid "a6e61ee8-3bd8-5e63-8ba5-e299947ae0e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{1}{2},1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740854} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186740859 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56bf9cc7-a411-5f11-af70-42b523af5968" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{5}{2},-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740845} {:answer/id #uuid "7c8e7a07-b532-56a3-9fca-ac4a4ad733d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(1,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740849} {:answer/id #uuid "89072967-eff0-5b9f-8b98-f99a265a8d97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{5}{2},-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740851} {:answer/id #uuid "9b462e90-1db3-5904-acc5-7f58edfc96e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(1,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740852} {:answer/id #uuid "d3818cde-b230-5dda-9fbf-db59afc352a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{5}{2},1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740861}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186740845} :answer-field/id #uuid "23117a71-7189-5a5b-a91c-b409ed9defbd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740839}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "cc9a4cf3-9d01-5911-a22d-cb9209d9c5a4" :question/problem "The point $(-2,-1)$ lies on the curve $y=f\\left(x\\right)$. Which of the following points **must** lie on $y=f\\left(3-2x\\right)-2$?" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1: Transform the point**\n\nStarting from the original graph, reflect across the $y$-axis, then scale horizontally by $\\frac{1}{2}$, then translate $\\frac{3}{2}$ units right, then translate $2$ units down. The corresponding points are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2,-1)&\\longmapsto (1,-1)\\\\ &\\longmapsto (\\frac{5}{2},-1)\\\\ &\\longmapsto (\\frac{5}{2},-3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2: Substitute into the equation**\n\nThe given point tells us that $f\\left(-2\\right)=-1$. To reproduce this known input in the transformed curve, solve\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3-2x&=-2\\\\ -2x&=-5\\\\ x&=\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt this horizontal coordinate,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y&=f\\left(-2\\cdot \\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)+3\\right)-2\\\\ &=f\\left(-2\\right)-2\\\\ &=\\left(-1\\right)-2\\\\ &=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $(\\frac{5}{2},-3)$ must lie on the transformed curve."} {:answer/id #uuid "cea704c6-e5ec-52bd-b099-b2e73b8c247e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\frac{3}{2},-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740860} {:answer/id #uuid "d3818cde-b230-5dda-9fbf-db59afc352a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{5}{2},1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740861} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186740862 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43d64529-0640-56ee-aa46-33600075d688" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\frac{1}{2},1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740841} {:answer/id #uuid "4695bb72-607e-5677-a342-07a2355570bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\frac{1}{2},3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740842} {:answer/id #uuid "64488003-7aa4-53a7-a3bf-f145a6211534" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-2,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740846} {:answer/id #uuid "a6e61ee8-3bd8-5e63-8ba5-e299947ae0e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{1}{2},1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740854} {:answer/id #uuid "c0c2306f-d4b6-5370-829c-cfa2186854f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-2,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740857}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186740841} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd0e00e6-adcf-57b0-8cd2-d168641fc4a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740856}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "f3aad8f3-3cf2-506b-aea5-7c5b6ab93073" :question/problem "The point $(-1,2)$ lies on the curve $y=f\\left(x\\right)$. Which of the following points **must** lie on $y=f\\left(-2x-2\\right)-1$?" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1: Transform the point**\n\nStarting from the original graph, reflect across the $y$-axis, then scale horizontally by $\\frac{1}{2}$, then translate $1$ unit left, then translate $1$ unit down. The corresponding points are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1,2)&\\longmapsto (\\frac{1}{2},2)\\\\ &\\longmapsto (-\\frac{1}{2},2)\\\\ &\\longmapsto (-\\frac{1}{2},1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2: Substitute into the equation**\n\nThe given point tells us that $f\\left(-1\\right)=2$. To reproduce this known input in the transformed curve, solve\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x-2&=-1\\\\ -2x&=1\\\\ x&=-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt this horizontal coordinate,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y&=f\\left(-2\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)-2\\right)-1\\\\ &=f\\left(-1\\right)-1\\\\ &=\\left(2\\right)-1\\\\ &=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $(-\\frac{1}{2},1)$ must lie on the transformed curve."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186740863 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5292ea2b-8576-5ff0-8a68-c46d417afac9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(0,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740844} {:answer/id #uuid "7da9bf54-7b56-522c-8077-c818a42bf851" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(0,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740850} {:answer/id #uuid "a50b6246-0f38-5f6c-96bb-42ff728f301d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\frac{3}{2},6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740853} {:answer/id #uuid "cac040ba-c3a5-569a-b332-dd81c13934b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(5,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740858} {:answer/id #uuid "cea704c6-e5ec-52bd-b099-b2e73b8c247e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\frac{3}{2},-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740860}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186740850} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c092765-3f85-5e8d-afdf-0e2ecc6e2dc6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740838}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "fcddfbee-dbe9-574e-b429-5505f5de2044" :question/problem "The point $(3,4)$ lies on the curve $y=f\\left(x\\right)$. Which of the following points **must** lie on $y=-f\\left(3-2x\\right)+2$?" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1: Transform the point**\n\nStarting from the original graph, reflect across the $y$-axis, then scale horizontally by $\\frac{1}{2}$, then translate $\\frac{3}{2}$ units right, then reflect across the $x$-axis, then translate $2$ units up. The corresponding points are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3,4)&\\longmapsto (-\\frac{3}{2},4)\\\\ &\\longmapsto (0,4)\\\\ &\\longmapsto (0,-4)\\\\ &\\longmapsto (0,-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2: Substitute into the equation**\n\nThe given point tells us that $f\\left(3\\right)=4$. To reproduce this known input in the transformed curve, solve\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3-2x&=3\\\\ -2x&=0\\\\ x&=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt this horizontal coordinate,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y&=-f\\left(-2\\cdot \\left(0\\right)+3\\right)+2\\\\ &=-f\\left(3\\right)+2\\\\ &=-\\left(4\\right)+2\\\\ &=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $(0,-2)$ must lie on the transformed curve."} {:answer/id #uuid "6c4f7eaf-667b-5527-ac66-86ac2874e885" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\frac{4}{3},9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740968} {:answer/id #uuid "bdbcea8d-551b-53b0-add9-dbc96a6db7c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{2}{3},3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740976} {:answer/id #uuid "d85793a4-d021-52e5-a858-273672cba3fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\frac{4}{3},-\\frac{9}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740978} {:answer/id #uuid "d942d504-2748-5989-bc12-020c9895a8dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\frac{4}{3},-18)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740980} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186740986 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c4f7eaf-667b-5527-ac66-86ac2874e885" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\frac{4}{3},9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740968} {:answer/id #uuid "bdbcea8d-551b-53b0-add9-dbc96a6db7c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{2}{3},3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740976} {:answer/id #uuid "d85793a4-d021-52e5-a858-273672cba3fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\frac{4}{3},-\\frac{9}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740978} {:answer/id #uuid "d942d504-2748-5989-bc12-020c9895a8dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\frac{4}{3},-18)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740980} {:answer/id #uuid "fc12ef3c-13c8-5c10-90d4-930053342893" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\frac{4}{3},18)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740989}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186740980} :answer-field/id #uuid "92008069-751b-5edf-b59a-ba9bf77abaa1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740969}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ed4222f2-13f7-5eb6-a4c7-25d4c66e2e37" :question/problem "![](images/80/8000655c1943c60282d8844a2ae965b6415e21962c44309cd68806f04744b806.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the global minimum and maximum of the function $y=f(x)$. What is the global minimum point of $y=-2f(3x)$?" :question/worked-solution "The negative outside factor reflects the graph across the $x$-axis, interchanging maxima and minima. We therefore use the original global **maximum** point, $(-4,9)$.\n\nThe input of $f$ must equal the original horizontal coordinate. Solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x&=-4 \\\\ 3x&=-4 \\\\ x&=-\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the outside factor and then the vertical translation to the original vertical coordinate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y&=-2\\cdot(9) \\\\ &=-18 \\\\ &=-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe horizontal transformation preserves the extremum type. Thus the global minimum point is $(-\\frac{4}{3},-18)$."} {:answer/id #uuid "fc12ef3c-13c8-5c10-90d4-930053342893" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\frac{4}{3},18)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740989} {:answer/id #uuid "75050383-8b7f-58bd-86e6-5d68bf6c5dc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{1}{3},-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186741001} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186741002 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a13c506-f5a3-5907-836e-76611fdbc0c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-1,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740993} {:answer/id #uuid "7377bdad-cfb9-5fc8-9ebd-86e74ca4d5bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(0,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186741000} {:answer/id #uuid "75050383-8b7f-58bd-86e6-5d68bf6c5dc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{1}{3},-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186741001} {:answer/id #uuid "7c9b8b33-2387-5d12-9d6c-4e3496f51f7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{1}{3},0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186741004} {:answer/id #uuid "b4394c2f-be0a-5485-b395-46195f08b7d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-1,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186741012}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186741001} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c5e8ef3-9e1a-54a8-96ed-4f5d39289a6a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186740995}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "78ae39c2-fdcd-592e-9dd0-857b80a3cdf4" :question/problem "![](images/1e/1eb29eb3eb3627e24a23d7315295a1d889308d67895f9b798dbf9dd71ba226df.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the local minimum and maximum of the function $y=f(x)$. What is the local maximum point of $y=-f(3x-2)-1$?" :question/worked-solution "The negative outside factor reflects the graph across the $x$-axis, interchanging maxima and minima. We therefore use the original local **minimum** point, $(-1,1)$.\n\nThe input of $f$ must equal the original horizontal coordinate. Solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-2&=-1 \\\\ 3x&=1 \\\\ x&=\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the outside factor and then the vertical translation to the original vertical coordinate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y&=-1\\cdot(1)-1 \\\\ &=-1-1 \\\\ &=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe horizontal transformation preserves the extremum type. Thus the local maximum point is $(\\frac{1}{3},-2)$."} {:answer/id #uuid "7c9b8b33-2387-5d12-9d6c-4e3496f51f7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\\frac{1}{3},0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186741004} {:answer/id #uuid "9d77fbd6-b854-56d2-82a5-698d729f91ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\frac{5}{3},-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186741007} {:answer/id #uuid "a6b8540a-8c2d-53e1-b503-4ff1f6e2d968" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\frac{2}{3},-5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186741010} {:answer/id #uuid "ec4f6a57-3e99-5a6a-861e-2aea4392b53d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\frac{2}{3},-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186741018} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186741497 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2bbfb6c5-5cd3-576b-ae0b-da71cdf2b39f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$18$ cars per day" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186741469} {:answer/id #uuid "480aff34-b86a-589b-a5c3-d2462d76ee61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$68$ cars per day" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186741471} {:answer/id #uuid "a245f9de-2ca5-5510-b58a-c19d2b0905ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$2570$ cars per day" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186741483} {:answer/id #uuid "bed57b40-df4f-5207-a97e-c8cb83aca2ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$-30$ cars per day" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186741486} {:answer/id #uuid "e57b5c77-ba97-57b1-a2a7-3282d2daa53e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$-17$ cars per day" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186741494}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186741469} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1b3494e-5975-568f-b096-bf04e7fa41b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186741495}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "fa2d121a-aec0-5e77-a970-7565dc48804c" :question/problem "The rate $O$ of the orders a car factory receives can be modeled as $O(t)=130t{e}^{-0.2t}$ cars per day. The rate at which cars are completed can be modeled as $C(t)=30+15\\sin(\\frac{2\\pi }{10}t)$ cars per day. In both cases, $t$ is the time, in days, since the launch of the new model. \n\nWhat is the rate of change in the number of cars under construction $20$ days after the model's launch? Assume that an ordered car goes into construction as soon as the factory receives its order. Round your answer to the nearest integer." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The rate of change of the number of cars under construction at time $t$ is equal to the order rate minus the completion rate, that is,\n\n$$\nO(t)-C(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $t=20,$ the rate of change in the number of cars under construction after $20$ days is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}O(t)-C(t) & =130(20){e}^{-0.2(20)}-(30+15\\sin(\\frac{2\\pi }{10}(20))) \\\\  & =130(20){e}^{-4}-30-15\\sin(4 \\pi) \\\\  & =130(20){e}^{-4}-30 \\\\  & ≈18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change in the number of cars in construction after $20$ days is $18$ cars per day. The quantity is increasing."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186741879 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "997583a6-00bd-5083-b4ba-24fbaac7d277" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{(e^2-2)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186741877}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186741877} :answer-field/id #uuid "96c988d1-d875-5d19-b719-8972ef62ced0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186741876}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "aa757f8f-ef42-5646-bf76-fa167882b5f1" :question/problem "If a curve $C$ is given by $y=\\frac{x+\\ln x}{x-\\ln x}$, calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=e^2$.\n\nThe slope at $x=e^2$ is {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The slope is the value of $y'(x)$ at $x=e^2$. Let $u(x)=x+\\ln x$ and $v(x)=x-\\ln x$. Their derivatives are\n\n$$\nu'(x)=1+\\frac{1}{x},\\qquad v'(x)=1-\\frac{1}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the quotient rule and keeping the subtraction around the entire second product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny'(x)&=\\frac{u'(x)v(x)-u(x)v'(x)}{[v(x)]^2}\\\\\n&=\\frac{(1+\\frac{1}{x})(x-\\ln x)-(x+\\ln x)(1-\\frac{1}{x})}{(x-\\ln x)^2}\\\\\n&=\\frac{x-\\ln x+1-\\frac{\\ln x}{x}-(x+\\ln x-1-\\frac{\\ln x}{x})}{(x-\\ln x)^2}\\\\\n&=\\frac{2-2\\ln x}{(x-\\ln x)^2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $x=e^2$, we have $\\ln(e^2)=2$ and the original denominator is $e^2-2\\ne 0$. Thus\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny'(e^2)&=\\frac{2-2(2)}{(e^2-2)^2}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{2}{(e^2-2)^2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope is $-\\frac{2}{(e^2-2)^2}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186742766 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "deff0fd6-6caa-5ae3-b8bf-ee9ba13dc5ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sin x}{2}+x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186742772}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186742772} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e7bd4ee-d858-58e5-bb37-98b173c2d660" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186742751}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "be88eac4-63c9-55fa-8de9-f2d787d0a58a" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $y=\\frac{\\cos x}{2}+\\frac{x^{2}}{2}$.\n\n$\\frac{dy}{dx}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Use $\\frac{d}{dx}(\\sin x)=\\cos x$ and $\\frac{d}{dx}(\\cos x)=-\\sin x$, together with the sum, constant multiple, and power rules.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= \\frac{d}{dx}\\left(\\frac{\\cos x}{2}+\\frac{x^{2}}{2}\\right) \\\\ &=(\\frac{1}{2}(-\\sin x))+(\\frac{1}{2}(2)x) \\\\ &=-\\frac{\\sin x}{2}+x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186742770 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "006d1bc0-9620-5657-be7f-9be190fc7e8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sin x+x^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186742746} {:answer/id #uuid "968377f7-3861-59f3-b167-fd76fe0c9e26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\sin x+x^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186742761} {:answer/id #uuid "b39b75dc-1392-59c6-bace-4dd192d29697" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\sin x+x^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186742765} {:answer/id #uuid "c403193f-7238-53fc-b304-d9e9de2b4329" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\cos x+\\frac{x^{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186742767} {:answer/id #uuid "ddf838e8-1daf-5750-9077-08a7d61d6108" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sin x+x^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186742771}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186742765} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff8b5b0a-a9b5-504a-b8c9-dd8c6df713e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186742776}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d68af547-d88d-509c-8b76-4e14986993af" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $y=\\cos x+\\frac{x^{3}}{3}$." :question/worked-solution "Use $\\frac{d}{dx}(\\sin x)=\\cos x$ and $\\frac{d}{dx}(\\cos x)=-\\sin x$, together with the sum, constant multiple, and power rules.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= \\frac{d}{dx}\\left(\\cos x+\\frac{x^{3}}{3}\\right) \\\\ &=(1(-\\sin x))+(\\frac{1}{3}(3)x^{2}) \\\\ &=-\\sin x+x^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186742780 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50dca24c-2687-56b4-9d8e-47b286fcca51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\cos x}{2}+2\\sin x+x^{2}-\\frac{3}{x^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186742784}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186742784} :answer-field/id #uuid "003e2430-5e8b-58ba-80c0-7f6a93282c65" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186742778}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "33c21077-32cd-53c0-87cb-dd943d166134" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $y=\\frac{\\sin x}{2}-2\\cos x+\\frac{x^{3}}{3}+\\frac{1}{x^{3}}$.\n\n$\\frac{dy}{dx}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Use $\\frac{d}{dx}(\\sin x)=\\cos x$ and $\\frac{d}{dx}(\\cos x)=-\\sin x$, together with the sum, constant multiple, and power rules.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= \\frac{d}{dx}\\left(\\frac{\\sin x}{2}-2\\cos x+\\frac{x^{3}}{3}+\\frac{1}{x^{3}}\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(\\frac{\\sin x}{2}-2\\cos x+\\frac{x^{3}}{3}+x^{-3}\\right) \\\\ &=(\\frac{1}{2}(\\cos x))+(-2(-\\sin x)) \\\\ &\\quad{}+(\\frac{1}{3}(3)x^{2})+(1(-3)x^{-4}) \\\\ &=\\frac{\\cos x}{2}+2\\sin x+x^{2}-\\frac{3}{x^{4}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function and derivative have domain $x\\ne0$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186742782 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b99c5aa-a5a8-5586-b9ff-4d48a2f8bb60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\cos x}{2}-2\\sin x+x+\\frac{2}{x^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186742787}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186742787} :answer-field/id #uuid "15f28df3-ae61-53a4-a80c-4743e00e7fb7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186742779}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "48bc2d6a-2956-555f-b5f3-39b125aa4b4d" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $y=-\\frac{\\sin x}{2}+2\\cos x+\\frac{x^{2}}{2}-\\frac{1}{x^{2}}$.\n\n$\\frac{dy}{dx}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Use $\\frac{d}{dx}(\\sin x)=\\cos x$ and $\\frac{d}{dx}(\\cos x)=-\\sin x$, together with the sum, constant multiple, and power rules.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= \\frac{d}{dx}\\left(-\\frac{\\sin x}{2}+2\\cos x+\\frac{x^{2}}{2}-\\frac{1}{x^{2}}\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(-\\frac{\\sin x}{2}+2\\cos x+\\frac{x^{2}}{2}-x^{-2}\\right) \\\\ &=(\\frac{-1}{2}(\\cos x))+(2(-\\sin x)) \\\\ &\\quad{}+(\\frac{1}{2}(2)x)+(-1(-2)x^{-3}) \\\\ &=-\\frac{\\cos x}{2}-2\\sin x+x+\\frac{2}{x^{3}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function and derivative have domain $x\\ne0$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186742786 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6aaa5f76-12e9-5c66-9817-6f3794da0983" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sin x}{3}+2\\cos x+x^{2}-\\frac{1}{x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186742785}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186742785} :answer-field/id #uuid "47040106-0759-50bc-bd66-b9a5ff0ff4c5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186742781}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "6aae0c1d-fd21-51ca-9fd2-521f7d5e22ab" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $y=\\frac{\\cos x}{3}+2\\sin x+\\frac{x^{3}}{3}+\\frac{1}{x}$.\n\n$\\frac{dy}{dx}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Use $\\frac{d}{dx}(\\sin x)=\\cos x$ and $\\frac{d}{dx}(\\cos x)=-\\sin x$, together with the sum, constant multiple, and power rules.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= \\frac{d}{dx}\\left(\\frac{\\cos x}{3}+2\\sin x+\\frac{x^{3}}{3}+\\frac{1}{x}\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(\\frac{\\cos x}{3}+2\\sin x+\\frac{x^{3}}{3}+x^{-1}\\right) \\\\ &=(\\frac{1}{3}(-\\sin x))+(2(\\cos x)) \\\\ &\\quad{}+(\\frac{1}{3}(3)x^{2})+(1(-1)x^{-2}) \\\\ &=-\\frac{\\sin x}{3}+2\\cos x+x^{2}-\\frac{1}{x^{2}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function and derivative have domain $x\\ne0$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186742788 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2ab20f4-c0c1-5f46-8b31-f630dac75aa7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sin x}{2}+\\cos x-x^{3}+\\frac{2}{x^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186742789}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186742789} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a28b7c5-f1e1-5e73-bd20-2f1dcaa9a229" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186742783}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "d48e4883-f3b4-5326-a296-e3ff5b5d635e" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $y=-\\frac{\\cos x}{2}+\\sin x-\\frac{x^{4}}{4}-\\frac{1}{x^{2}}$.\n\n$\\frac{dy}{dx}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Use $\\frac{d}{dx}(\\sin x)=\\cos x$ and $\\frac{d}{dx}(\\cos x)=-\\sin x$, together with the sum, constant multiple, and power rules.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= \\frac{d}{dx}\\left(-\\frac{\\cos x}{2}+\\sin x-\\frac{x^{4}}{4}-\\frac{1}{x^{2}}\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(-\\frac{\\cos x}{2}+\\sin x-\\frac{x^{4}}{4}-x^{-2}\\right) \\\\ &=(\\frac{-1}{2}(-\\sin x))+(1(\\cos x)) \\\\ &\\quad{}+(\\frac{-1}{4}(4)x^{3})+(-1(-2)x^{-3}) \\\\ &=\\frac{\\sin x}{2}+\\cos x-x^{3}+\\frac{2}{x^{3}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function and derivative have domain $x\\ne0$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186743002 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6debbac0-8b3e-5d33-a731-6fea63f81519" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743007} {:answer/id #uuid "9e62916c-f5d1-586c-ab3f-aedaa924c243" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743014}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186743007} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a3a9865-53ab-5262-8908-1e4142a25713" :answer-field/key "$x\\in (-\\infty,-2]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743005} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1bc397a-aa5d-5f98-899d-79403b74b4f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743020} {:answer/id #uuid "ed3f40fc-773a-532e-b4f0-bcc4ab807ed3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743029}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186743020} :answer-field/id #uuid "83901d7f-c506-518c-85ea-7b80db8555d3" :answer-field/key "$x\\in (-3,\\infty)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743011} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f659f65-ff07-5ced-9a87-6c43f269bfb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743006} {:answer/id #uuid "bba98656-d357-5a29-8581-70ca4eebe9fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743018}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186743006} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3f55fdb-aa5e-565f-b4d4-57c386cdcb11" :answer-field/key "$x\\in [-1,3)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743027}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1d430519-9dec-5b74-9f67-7a61375ec901" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=|x+2|-1,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Start with $y=|x|$, translate the graph $2$ units left, and then $1$ unit down. The vertex is $(-2,-1)$.\n\n![The full V-shaped graph and the three domain restrictions; dashed horizontal lines illustrate the horizontal line test.](images/b4/b4a64bd5c4ddbc16c194eb91048f141f98dc7c6a85c7083a6d53693403d33ca0.png)\n\nA function is invertible on an interval if and only if it is one-to-one there. On each side of the vertex this graph is strictly monotone and passes the horizontal line test.\n\n- On $x\\in(-3,\\infty)$, the graph contains both sides of the vertex. For example, $f(-\\frac{5}{2})=f(-\\frac{3}{2})=-\\frac{1}{2}$. Both inputs belong to this interval, so it is not invertible there.\n- On $x\\in(-\\infty,-2]$, the graph is strictly decreasing. Including the vertex as an endpoint does not produce a repeated output, so it is invertible there.\n- On $x\\in[-1,3)$, the graph is strictly increasing, since this interval is to the right of the vertex. It is invertible there as well.\n\nSelect $x\\in(-\\infty,-2]$ and $x\\in[-1,3)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186743012 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7078238f-1188-5753-b2c2-dec1ef0924e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743008} {:answer/id #uuid "c0e30c99-991d-5846-8104-f674e5febad1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743019}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186743008} :answer-field/id #uuid "99904baa-6f25-53ab-a04a-e67c606b373a" :answer-field/key "$x\\in [-2,-1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743013} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "165867dd-db73-5c32-b4a4-a15cee675a97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743000} {:answer/id #uuid "d87359d2-34cc-570c-b6d4-6ffdc9a210dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743024}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186743024} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad3cbfbc-6bc5-51c9-9e59-3f5e72855717" :answer-field/key "$x\\in (-\\infty,-1]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743016} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc7bd434-d8c2-557a-bf80-79a63c97ac0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743022} {:answer/id #uuid "db40b838-1987-54d6-8471-4cf489040fd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743026}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186743026} :answer-field/id #uuid "da48a625-0672-52e8-84f0-0853226d1379" :answer-field/key "$x\\in [-\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{1}{2})$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743025}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "959f82bc-e648-5f1a-b1b4-398f4487ef7f" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=-(x+\\frac{3}{2})^{2}+\\frac{1}{2},$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Start with $y=x^2$, reflect it across the $x$-axis, translate it $\\frac{3}{2}$ units left, and then $\\frac{1}{2}$ unit up. The vertex is $(-\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{1}{2})$.\n\n![The full reflected parabola and the three domain restrictions; open and filled dots mark excluded and included endpoints.](images/24/24d92fb4c9fbebc0704901508b41cb3dd1887cfd9a6484f91735454de25a02be.png)\n\nA function is invertible on an interval if and only if it is one-to-one there. The parabola is strictly increasing to the left of its vertex and strictly decreasing to the right. Each branch passes the horizontal line test, including the vertex if it is an endpoint.\n\n- On $x\\in[-2,-1)$, there are points on both sides of $-\\frac{3}{2}$. In particular, $-\\frac{7}{4}$ and $-\\frac{5}{4}$ are both in this interval, and\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}\n  f(-\\frac{7}{4})&=\\frac{1}{2}-(-\\frac{1}{4})^2=\\frac{7}{16},\\\\\n  f(-\\frac{5}{4})&=\\frac{1}{2}-(\\frac{1}{4})^2=\\frac{7}{16}.\n  \\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\n  These distinct inputs have the same output, so $f$ is not invertible on this interval. Excluding the endpoint $-1$ does not remove these repeated outputs.\n- On $x\\in[-\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{1}{2})$, the graph lies entirely on the decreasing branch, starting at the vertex. Thus $f$ is invertible on this interval.\n- On $x\\in(-\\infty,-1]$, the same distinct inputs $-\\frac{7}{4}$ and $-\\frac{5}{4}$ are present and have equal outputs. Thus $f$ is not invertible on this interval either.\n\nSelect $x\\in[-\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{1}{2})$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186743137 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0748e23a-eaca-5e9f-9f9b-84d6c44a8764" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743136} {:answer/id #uuid "fae781f3-a1b8-5c88-8bf3-996d14a559a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743213}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186743136} :answer-field/id #uuid "09c4d826-32a4-5b51-9eeb-98f1c11f9085" :answer-field/key "Graph II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743138} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a8cb877-b04e-5e7d-8eaf-ad2665edc57c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743146} {:answer/id #uuid "e919677e-3f3e-5dea-bff4-a0204bcca993" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743204}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186743204} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fc1b418-4999-5f07-ab5d-b3ad2425d5ad" :answer-field/key "Graph IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743140} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b0692c36-d7c5-5580-9d4c-a68446b16d30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743185} {:answer/id #uuid "b1885b21-86fa-5e00-9286-55682e57a9ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743186}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186743186} :answer-field/id #uuid "a22fa617-6040-5dbf-b977-d234d580ad24" :answer-field/key "Graph I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743181} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ac8511a-a18e-5573-8365-ebc3f82f21c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743159} {:answer/id #uuid "e80480c0-e716-5acb-af1f-9c5a712449cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743203}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186743159} :answer-field/id #uuid "a58a91d9-8429-5ec4-a725-9b2130c9c483" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743184} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "323362eb-55d5-53cf-9a09-a5831ea87de8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743147} {:answer/id #uuid "eff65137-b2a2-592a-a9ae-1d11c87c354b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743208}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186743147} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9951569-62ad-59a8-ae28-635b173cb661" :answer-field/key "Graph III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743196}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "07b79ccf-7443-56ee-9430-b88bdfe0be34" :question/problem "Which of the graphs below correspond to an invertible function?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n![](images/e7/e7343fee221d37ba5c99bedbf3488cc8edfabdf7e1874aa346d561ef2ed7693f.png)\n\nEach graph shows its entire domain." :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible if and only if it is one-to-one. Apply the horizontal line test to the entire graph: every horizontal line must meet it at most once. Filled endpoints belong to the graph; open endpoints do not.\n\n![](images/b5/b55836dfa8c590199e5bc537ec751c03891ecd961d3174aedb8968c150b7ce84.png)\n\n- **Graph I:** Each piece is strictly monotone. From left to right, the output ranges are $[0,2]$, $[-2,1]$. The horizontal line $y=\\frac{1}{2}$ meets pieces $1$ and $2$ at different inputs. The function is not invertible.\n\n- **Graph II:** Each piece is strictly monotone. From left to right, the output ranges are $[- \\frac{5}{2},\\frac{1}{2})$, $(- \\frac{1}{2},\\frac{5}{2}]$. The horizontal line $y=0$ meets pieces $1$ and $2$ at different inputs. The function is not invertible.\n\n- **Graph III:** Each piece is strictly monotone. From left to right, the output ranges are $(- \\frac{5}{2},- \\frac{1}{2}]$, $[\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{5}{2}]$. These ranges are disjoint, including endpoint membership. Thus no output is repeated across pieces, and the function is invertible.\n\n- **Graph IV:** Each piece is strictly monotone. From left to right, the output ranges are $[- \\frac{3}{2},\\frac{1}{2}]$, $[- \\frac{1}{2},\\frac{3}{2}]$. The horizontal line $y=0$ meets pieces $1$ and $2$ at different inputs. The function is not invertible.\n\nSelect **Graph III**."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186743188 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "387fa7ac-5131-53bc-bc9e-a655ad771871" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743148} {:answer/id #uuid "51a26dd9-7521-5025-a5f2-97f7c97e458b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743154}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186743154} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d062ca4-4dc8-5b30-bde9-2207574eb422" :answer-field/key "Graph III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743139} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c97fca61-16b7-53b1-a7d4-eb56e9fd1241" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743195} {:answer/id #uuid "d8bd564e-a171-5e31-b388-12b1b4395058" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743198}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186743195} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a2fdd0f-91bb-51a8-b666-6f9a8b4a19d9" :answer-field/key "Graph IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743173} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c109eed-d92a-544d-9645-66125e134853" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743160} {:answer/id #uuid "b5a9c043-cf3f-528f-9c27-717e9fa3d4eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743187}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186743160} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b4a0199-8017-58c0-b6ae-9947dbcfeeaa" :answer-field/key "Graph II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/r