below correspond to an invertible function?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n![](images/70/70ce25430e92695d3d73d55c63ce25ac974ed2afd7547ee298288f5cdcb20522.png)\n\nEach graph shows its entire domain." :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible if and only if it is one-to-one. Apply the horizontal line test to the entire graph: every horizontal line must meet it at most once. Filled endpoints belong to the graph; open endpoints do not.\n\n![](images/e8/e8f5d35acbcf8a41b177a3c30ed73060967d538223517171591a33cef3c4b7a4.png)\n\n- **Graph I:** Each piece is strictly monotone. From left to right, the output ranges are $[-3,-1]$, $[0,3]$. These ranges are disjoint, including endpoint membership. Thus no output is repeated across pieces, and the function is invertible.\n\n- **Graph II:** Each piece is strictly monotone. From left to right, the output ranges are $[0,2]$, $(-2,1)$. The horizontal line $y=\\frac{1}{2}$ meets pieces $1$ and $2$ at different inputs. The function is not invertible.\n\n- **Graph III:** Each piece is strictly monotone. From left to right, the output ranges are $[- \\frac{7}{2},- \\frac{1}{2}]$, $[\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{7}{2}]$. These ranges are disjoint, including endpoint membership. Thus no output is repeated across pieces, and the function is invertible.\n\n- **Graph IV:** Each piece is strictly monotone. From left to right, the output ranges are $[-3,-1]$, $[0,3]$. These ranges are disjoint, including endpoint membership. Thus no output is repeated across pieces, and the function is invertible.\n\nSelect **Graph I, Graph III, Graph IV**."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186743193 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d34b627-2e6b-5543-936f-a1bef8a72034" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743151} {:answer/id #uuid "583fc9cf-ce0a-52f0-b73c-4c1b0bbe86cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743156}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186743156} :answer-field/id #uuid "56bece4b-3f87-5fd7-b891-2ddca4b1866f" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743155} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "608f8eba-5eea-5329-8425-d84279830797" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743162} {:answer/id #uuid "de6b6e8b-1bce-5b89-9f57-fa55d19269ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743200}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186743162} :answer-field/id #uuid "bad9eedc-55ff-513b-aa87-f9477ffed2cd" :answer-field/key "Graph IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743190} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "807efa6d-32a8-5e24-9381-4e0f339fb4ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743175} {:answer/id #uuid "f9753b85-c436-55b8-b76e-34581087c98b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743212}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186743212} :answer-field/id #uuid "bfc51501-1c87-5072-8c99-eaaad3261750" :answer-field/key "Graph III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743192} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fb45348-99cd-568b-b526-4596ed591800" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743144} {:answer/id #uuid "fd12dfe4-260c-5a0a-9952-becd2fba2c76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743215}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186743144} :answer-field/id #uuid "caf2d6ad-420c-5362-bfb2-7c43dc56c888" :answer-field/key "Graph II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743197} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fd66c45-ca74-5f0d-90ae-51b01e3352f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743152} {:answer/id #uuid "73c09fbc-bdd4-5408-b3d0-d8c27528ce7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743169}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186743169} :answer-field/id #uuid "f088956b-e8ee-5b83-821d-e2772c0a9573" :answer-field/key "Graph I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743210}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c4e44a6d-227e-5ac9-907c-686c44e9ba42" :question/problem "Which of the graphs below correspond to an invertible function?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n![](images/aa/aa2d92034d57d122ab3aa6705dd708cb4f5e79ceaa80690df5e02248da9aa84f.png)\n\nEach graph shows its entire domain." :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible if and only if it is one-to-one. Apply the horizontal line test to the entire graph: every horizontal line must meet it at most once. Filled endpoints belong to the graph; open endpoints do not.\n\n![](images/4a/4a321c9318a43c0d7715478feac4c8281135cd6ba0b24095e41af5aa3099e9f8.png)\n\n- **Graph I:** Each piece is strictly monotone. From left to right, the output ranges are $[-1,2)$, $(-2,0]$. The horizontal line $y=- \\frac{1}{2}$ meets pieces $1$ and $2$ at different inputs. The function is not invertible.\n\n- **Graph II:** Each piece is strictly monotone. From left to right, the output ranges are $[0,2]$, $[-2,1]$. The horizontal line $y=\\frac{1}{2}$ meets pieces $1$ and $2$ at different inputs. The function is not invertible.\n\n- **Graph III:** Each piece is strictly monotone. From left to right, the output ranges are $[- \\frac{5}{2},- \\frac{1}{2}]$, $[\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{5}{2}]$. These ranges are disjoint, including endpoint membership. Thus no output is repeated across pieces, and the function is invertible.\n\n- **Graph IV:** Each piece is strictly monotone. From left to right, the output ranges are $[-1,2]$, $(-2,0]$. The horizontal line $y=- \\frac{1}{2}$ meets pieces $1$ and $2$ at different inputs. The function is not invertible.\n\nSelect **Graph III**."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186743472 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b09c55f-ad62-5aea-ac68-95991fc22b6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743455} {:answer/id #uuid "975a9d2d-322c-53eb-9f30-94a335d48485" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743476}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186743476} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcca8f70-780e-54c1-bd07-c0fd85f293a0" :answer-field/key "$x\\in [-1,1]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743489} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77687b7c-5db5-55c3-8918-245b041da353" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743469} {:answer/id #uuid "86245fa8-304f-51d4-b384-02b1fe0d5d58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743471}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186743469} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3454b62-dd71-594b-8f9d-c24b05702fd1" :answer-field/key "$x\\in (-3,4]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743496} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5f6221a-b2a9-5632-b6a9-3f6bc55fa7a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743497} {:answer/id #uuid "eb70c397-ecfe-5de4-94c3-bb5c5b3c32e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743498}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186743497} :answer-field/id #uuid "f94df8cc-f8d3-5caf-9d08-48904ecf9807" :answer-field/key "$x\\in [0,1]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743499}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8737d07d-4a09-59bd-b216-70c0b9eb3406" :question/problem "![](images/ea/eab48f55878fef239e1dc5cc834362717f6234a52a0f5fcd2b9cb488564a003e.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ shown above invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a domain exactly when it is one-to-one there. Apply the horizontal line test to the entire proposed domain.\n\n- On $x\\in [-1,1]$: **Invertible.** Each nonconstant graph piece is one-to-one. Its restricted output ranges are $[0,1]$, $\\{1\\}$. Any shared output at a joined vertex belongs to the same input; no output belongs to two distinct inputs.\n\n![](images/28/2823654a0160b9f30464b26058aba3551e70e2f6caf2596e1f1600b0ef8c1a44.png)\n\n- On $x\\in (-3,4]$: **Not invertible.** The horizontal line $y=0$ meets this restriction at two distinct inputs: $f(-1)=f\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)=0$.\n\n![](images/7b/7b695776d34f8f45c85edda10ed93342e44661f2b56e87172549b5ff9acbdd95.png)\n\n- On $x\\in [0,1]$: **Invertible.** Each nonconstant graph piece is one-to-one. Its restricted output ranges are $[\\frac{1}{2},1]$, $\\{1\\}$. Any shared output at a joined vertex belongs to the same input; no output belongs to two distinct inputs.\n\n![](images/12/12c6434d38296c4ebf0a3ed6af8a73df1bd9f823753ee206a63fce1ce6a365f1.png)\n\nSelect $x\\in [-1,1]$, $x\\in [0,1]$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186743482 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17eee25e-a14d-5423-a67b-b785b67dd699" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743454} {:answer/id #uuid "ada76951-de8c-540b-8877-bf1c7a2d8b7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743485}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186743485} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c009f8a-1a01-51cf-9c69-9b9f14a3c32a" :answer-field/key "$x\\in (-3,3)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743457} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0aa78d03-b94e-500c-959c-fbdb90bbc55e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743451} {:answer/id #uuid "9989e24c-20a0-5a56-9009-8f8c4785d102" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743477}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186743477} :answer-field/id #uuid "54ed28fb-4c21-5e8f-9ab7-261c75378630" :answer-field/key "$x\\in (-2,-1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743464} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5744a4f8-92cd-58b4-a81a-eb28b99757ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743465} {:answer/id #uuid "cc4c518f-dadf-5ca7-9daa-50e62314ec28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743490}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186743490} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2859088-3077-5587-8325-b1ef01abecd0" :answer-field/key "$x\\in (-2,3]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186743493}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a27c37c5-2d19-59e9-b19a-97fd1aa959e8" :question/problem "![](images/0e/0e63d41a9cfeeef5a4463565e8c94585273a7cd90d55f52a30c98f75ad45b902.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ shown above invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a domain exactly when it is one-to-one there. Apply the horizontal line test to the entire proposed domain.\n\n- On $x\\in (-2,3]$: **Not invertible.** The horizontal line $y=\\frac{8}{3}$ meets this restriction at two distinct inputs: $f(-1)=f(2)=\\frac{8}{3}$.\n\n![](images/92/92212fc8b8fa4577d0e906a78c17f9edd79106f0de4d600d2f33929491af3c41.png)\n\n- On $x\\in (-2,-1)$: **Invertible.** Each nonconstant graph piece is one-to-one. Its restricted output range is $(\\frac{4}{3},\\frac{8}{3})$. Any shared output at a joined vertex belongs to the same input; no output belongs to two distinct inputs.\n\n![](images/a1/a18bc17f336845ce4a8ea72706beeb0e44417f85e148c79ec2e01291e393018a.png)\n\n- On $x\\in (-3,3)$: **Not invertible.** The horizontal line $y=\\frac{5}{2}$ meets this restriction at two distinct inputs: $f\\left(-\\frac{9}{8}\\right)=f\\left(\\frac{21}{10}\\right)=\\frac{5}{2}$.\n\n![](images/39/399e64dcb0067ab3c49a0850a1dadd90d591e743e034b8ec9f397d17904900e6.png)\n\nSelect $x\\in (-2,-1)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186744587 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1641f8d1-9569-5c0f-9a59-9dc1f6028fb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x-\\frac{7}{4})^{2}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186744589} {:answer/id #uuid "1dc1632a-b86a-5e2c-97a3-34eef5872886" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x-\\frac{7}{2})^{2}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186744591} {:answer/id #uuid "748c4af7-1fa5-5a59-8b0a-411162ee3cf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x-\\frac{49}{4})^{2}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186744598} {:answer/id #uuid "87b0f964-5cb4-5d3a-9186-5bf800dec2b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x-7)^{2}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186744601} {:answer/id #uuid "f2bc36a3-a824-59e4-956b-fa035273e23c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x+\\frac{7}{2})^{2}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186744605}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186744591} :answer-field/id #uuid "a80f5b74-5b45-5e8f-aa5e-286cbb64c34d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186744603}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "0f8e00ab-8f70-5ee7-881e-550912dafdf3" :question/problem "Rewrite the expression $(x^{2}-7x+\\frac{49}{4})-3$ as the difference between a perfect square and a constant." :question/worked-solution "Recall the perfect-square identity:\n\n$$\nx^{2}-2ax+a^{2}=(x-a)^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe expression in parentheses factors as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^{2}-7x+\\frac{49}{4} &= x^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{7}{2}\\cdot x+\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right)^{2} \\\\\n&= (x-\\frac{7}{2})^{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKeep the outside constant unchanged. Therefore,\n\n$$\n(x^{2}-7x+\\frac{49}{4})-3=(x-\\frac{7}{2})^{2}-3.\n$$"} {:answer/id #uuid "1641f8d1-9569-5c0f-9a59-9dc1f6028fb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x-\\frac{7}{4})^{2}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186744589} {:answer/id #uuid "1dc1632a-b86a-5e2c-97a3-34eef5872886" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x-\\frac{7}{2})^{2}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186744591} {:answer/id #uuid "748c4af7-1fa5-5a59-8b0a-411162ee3cf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x-\\frac{49}{4})^{2}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186744598} {:answer/id #uuid "f2bc36a3-a824-59e4-956b-fa035273e23c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x+\\frac{7}{2})^{2}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186744605} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186744608 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e2bd096-a14e-503d-b6d5-503450aa8356" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186744612} {:answer/id #uuid "3a5e71c6-446d-50a7-9d12-e90064ccc5f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186744615} {:answer/id #uuid "595177cf-a197-58cd-ae55-900626e27bc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186744620} {:answer/id #uuid "ae4d6163-bac2-5abd-b7a8-7485c2e52c1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186744626} {:answer/id #uuid "b885ecac-8cd0-5a5b-99b1-fb382b4e0c36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186744627}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186744612} :answer-field/id #uuid "51dd973f-ec71-588f-9b2d-c1e04c92d69a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186744618}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "0439636c-5f8c-5d5a-85d8-31a0709fad65" :question/problem "What is the slope of the tangent to the curve $y=6\\sqrt[4]{x^{3}}-3\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}+\\frac{5}{2}x$ at the point $(1,\\frac{11}{2})$?" :question/worked-solution "The slope of the tangent is the derivative evaluated at the point's $x$-coordinate. Rewrite the radicals and reciprocal radicals as powers, then apply the power rule to each term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny&=6x^{3/4}-3x^{-1/2}+\\frac{5}{2}x,\\\\\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=6\\cdot\\frac{3}{4}x^{-1/4}-3\\cdot\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)x^{-3/2}+\\frac{5}{2}\\\\\n&=\\frac{9}{2}x^{-1/4}+\\frac{3}{2}x^{-3/2}+\\frac{5}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $x=1$, evaluate the powers and add the exact contributions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm&=\\frac{9}{2}\\left(1\\right)^{-1/4}+\\frac{3}{2}\\left(1\\right)^{-3/2}+\\frac{5}{2}\\\\\n&=\\frac{9}{2}+\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{5}{2}\\\\\n&=\\frac{17}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope is $\\frac{17}{2}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186744611 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ef1bc6a-7fcc-5f62-adc8-9000aa75bfda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{83}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186744622} {:answer/id #uuid "98f695d8-3a9a-54da-9e09-9c4bdbf7c118" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "166" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186744623} {:answer/id #uuid "c28ea25f-85f4-596c-8fb1-c22aaeb70f07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{83}{128}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186744628} {:answer/id #uuid "e0d562c9-bb5f-54cc-a1fc-16ceef2781db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{89}{128}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186744631} {:answer/id #uuid "fcc2cc76-e122-51e5-8aa2-a35d20df3e8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{563}{128}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186744634}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186744628} :answer-field/id #uuid "f28a44b1-431b-59c6-b843-eab80a55b63e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186744632}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "1b59bb0e-0a49-5239-9f6c-ada9b6eedc68" :question/problem "What is the slope of the tangent to the curve $y=-5\\sqrt[4]{x^{3}}-3\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}+\\frac{5}{2}x$ at the point $(16,-\\frac{3}{4})$?" :question/worked-solution "The slope of the tangent is the derivative evaluated at the point's $x$-coordinate. Rewrite the radicals and reciprocal radicals as powers, then apply the power rule to each term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny&=-5x^{3/4}-3x^{-1/2}+\\frac{5}{2}x,\\\\\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=-5\\cdot\\frac{3}{4}x^{-1/4}-3\\cdot\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)x^{-3/2}+\\frac{5}{2}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{15}{4}x^{-1/4}+\\frac{3}{2}x^{-3/2}+\\frac{5}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $x=16$, evaluate the powers and add the exact contributions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm&=-\\frac{15}{4}\\left(16\\right)^{-1/4}+\\frac{3}{2}\\left(16\\right)^{-3/2}+\\frac{5}{2}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{15}{8}+\\frac{3}{128}+\\frac{5}{2}\\\\\n&=\\frac{83}{128}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope is $\\frac{83}{128}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186744617 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "016032d8-1454-52d7-9f53-c967179ffd5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{131}{128}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186744607} {:answer/id #uuid "347e2267-9ab0-54dc-84fe-de7ba2b98bec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{419}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186744614} {:answer/id #uuid "7bc889e8-6759-5022-9196-ce09e8dbd850" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{157}{128}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186744621} {:answer/id #uuid "cdd38ec7-5dba-5dde-8f30-ef8b46f17249" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{253}{64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186744629} {:answer/id #uuid "e06667d0-b3e8-5a9e-b18d-93f7069e525d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{419}{128}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186744630}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186744630} :answer-field/id #uuid "22f16961-1b0d-5e0b-b730-22ef763ca290" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186744613}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "3f6708f7-6817-5bf5-a3e4-dcaa117f120b" :question/problem "What is the slope of the tangent to the curve $y=-6\\sqrt[4]{x^{3}}+3\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}-x$ at the point $(16,-\\frac{253}{4})$?" :question/worked-solution "The slope of the tangent is the derivative evaluated at the point's $x$-coordinate. Rewrite the radicals and reciprocal radicals as powers, then apply the power rule to each term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny&=-6x^{3/4}+3x^{-1/2}-x,\\\\\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=-6\\cdot\\frac{3}{4}x^{-1/4}+3\\cdot\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)x^{-3/2}-1\\\\\n&=-\\frac{9}{2}x^{-1/4}-\\frac{3}{2}x^{-3/2}-1.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $x=16$, evaluate the powers and add the exact contributions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm&=-\\frac{9}{2}\\left(16\\right)^{-1/4}-\\frac{3}{2}\\left(16\\right)^{-3/2}-1\\\\\n&=-\\frac{9}{4}-\\frac{3}{128}-1\\\\\n&=-\\frac{419}{128}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope is $-\\frac{419}{128}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186744624 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13ddc968-1300-54fe-9cb4-707b3437e6e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{241}{64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186744610} {:answer/id #uuid "3bc70705-91f3-521a-81bb-b999e881a95a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "196" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186744616} {:answer/id #uuid "58940217-1d1c-5b2d-8505-fd39605b1e3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{49}{64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186744619} {:answer/id #uuid "ac53ffac-c832-57e9-b630-d6d74111daf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{45}{64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186744625} {:answer/id #uuid "f56033ce-537c-544d-87ee-6eed1dae363e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{49}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186744633}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186744619} :answer-field/id #uuid "0bac3f68-a975-5d88-b974-ec22b518ae3d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186744609}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "995a28a7-580d-5aa0-bd14-59d5e761ea4a" :question/problem "What is the slope of the tangent to the curve $y=6\\sqrt[4]{x^{3}}-2\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{3}{2}x$ at the point $(16,\\frac{47}{2})$?" :question/worked-solution "The slope of the tangent is the derivative evaluated at the point's $x$-coordinate. Rewrite the radicals and reciprocal radicals as powers, then apply the power rule to each term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny&=6x^{3/4}-2x^{-1/2}-\\frac{3}{2}x,\\\\\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=6\\cdot\\frac{3}{4}x^{-1/4}-2\\cdot\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)x^{-3/2}-\\frac{3}{2}\\\\\n&=\\frac{9}{2}x^{-1/4}+x^{-3/2}-\\frac{3}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $x=16$, evaluate the powers and add the exact contributions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm&=\\frac{9}{2}\\left(16\\right)^{-1/4}+\\left(16\\right)^{-3/2}-\\frac{3}{2}\\\\\n&=\\frac{9}{4}+\\frac{1}{64}-\\frac{3}{2}\\\\\n&=\\frac{49}{64}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope is $\\frac{49}{64}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186744880 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d0bddad1-7da6-5c1c-a402-fb436af