y {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "d4273ffc-336f-5c40-9a77-84d0e443206b" :question/problem "Rewrite the following expression as the difference between a perfect square and a constant.\n\n$(x^{2}-7x+\\frac{49}{4})-9=(${{field-1}}$)^{2}-$ {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall the perfect-square identity:\n\n$$\nx^{2}-2ax+a^{2}=(x-a)^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe expression in parentheses factors as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^{2}-7x+\\frac{49}{4} &= x^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{7}{2}\\cdot x+\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right)^{2} \\\\\n&= (x-\\frac{7}{2})^{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKeep the outside constant unchanged. Therefore,\n\n$$\n(x^{2}-7x+\\frac{49}{4})-9=(x-\\frac{7}{2})^{2}-9.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186744898 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cdf72a43-2106-50ae-bb0f-c1bf6724905b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x-\\frac{13}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186744891}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186744891} :answer-field/id #uuid "66714905-23fb-540e-82d1-6cf9838b0241" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186744882} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9793a54-df38-54fd-8867-6a5932434823" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186744888}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186744888} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd248c3c-7a87-5418-b457-7f05ac3d3390" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186744899}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e2c68a8a-b652-5def-ba40-5aa175521802" :question/problem "Rewrite the following expression as the sum of a perfect square and a constant.\n\n$(x^{2}-13x+\\frac{169}{4})+4=(${{field-1}}$)^{2}+$ {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall the perfect-square identity:\n\n$$\nx^{2}-2ax+a^{2}=(x-a)^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe expression in parentheses factors as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^{2}-13x+\\frac{169}{4} &= x^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{13}{2}\\cdot x+\\left(\\frac{13}{2}\\right)^{2} \\\\\n&= (x-\\frac{13}{2})^{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKeep the outside constant unchanged. Therefore,\n\n$$\n(x^{2}-13x+\\frac{169}{4})+4=(x-\\frac{13}{2})^{2}+4.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186745171 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3fcb85f0-743a-503e-a264-7d1610bbfd44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745163} {:answer/id #uuid "40bd89c7-d0f8-5299-8661-4471e9c567cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745164} {:answer/id #uuid "af3cd05c-f2a5-5151-8a8d-23d4b1e2a1de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x^{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745166} {:answer/id #uuid "d092a438-99ad-5803-a598-c8373bb0e1a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745169}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186745164} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1af37fc-2e76-5e39-8a3b-d444e09a3bfb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745167} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32bc807e-3d3b-56f4-adaa-f992bcc06603" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x^{5}} + \\frac{4 x}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745161} {:answer/id #uuid "3e2458c9-78c2-54e6-b674-3c9bb5d4f731" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x^{4}} + x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745162} {:answer/id #uuid "622050d6-7ef5-534c-b953-24ffad416a0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x^{5}} + x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745165} {:answer/id #uuid "d08116da-6afd-5f89-a85e-f8720c36635b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x^{4}} + \\frac{4 x}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745168}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186745168} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1b84b24-76b1-59f0-aaad-d4b514797ee0" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745170}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "dd09c693-5983-57c6-bf07-3561959baedc" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n$\\frac{dy}{dx} + \\frac{4}{x}y = 4, x > 0$.\n\nSelect the correct options below:\n\nAn integrating factor for this equation is $I(x) =$ {{field-1}}.\n\nThe general solution is given by $y(x) =$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{4}{x}$ and $Q(x)=4.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (4/x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4})} \\\\  & ={x}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={x}^{4}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{4}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{4}{x}y) & ={x}^{4}\\cdot 4 \\\\ {x}^{4}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4{x}^{3}y & =4{x}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x))$ and carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{d}{dx}(y{x}^{4})\\,dx & =\\int 4{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{4} & =\\frac{4{x}^{5}}{5}+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{4x}{5}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186745583 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "185993f9-5f41-554d-8ef2-8671f6e47639" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{6 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745568} {:answer/id #uuid "30f39df2-4f3c-564e-8715-55df63ae186e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{3 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745571} {:answer/id #uuid "933dc969-d468-5c81-ab07-082a633a7c34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{- 3 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745579} {:answer/id #uuid "d598f3c6-4e9b-5474-9b20-4a72cccf8276" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{\\frac{3 x}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745588}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186745571} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d69c0d2-7281-5542-9128-c92524ae2083" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745578} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25bef243-80c6-5aee-91c5-37077146ac9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2 - 2 e^{- 3 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745570} {:answer/id #uuid "5460460e-f183-59a4-b200-60929b6398c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 4 e^{- 3 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745574} {:answer/id #uuid "60cfefb9-764f-5937-80fc-a7c97511ddd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2 - 2 e^{- \\frac{3 x}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745576} {:answer/id #uuid "8c3c13e9-2d09-5b2f-8f26-f77f827a8804" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 - 6 e^{- 3 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745577} {:answer/id #uuid "be8c49bd-2211-552e-ab32-26edc634c540" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 - 6 e^{- \\frac{3 x}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745584}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186745577} :answer-field/id #uuid "effeed87-db09-57a1-a922-4d03a08b8f9e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745590}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "bd66b8b5-bcce-5407-86d3-29c2531a668c" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\left(3\\right)y=6,\\quad y(0)=-4\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\nAn integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\nThe solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=3$ and $Q(x)=6.$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =e^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =e^{\\int 3\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =e^{3 x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)=e^{3 x}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}e^{3 x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+3y) & =e^{3 x}\\cdot 6 \\\\ e^{3 x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+3 e^{3 x}y & =6 e^{3 x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ye^{3 x}) & =6 e^{3 x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ye^{3 x})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 6 e^{3 x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ ye^{3 x} & =6\\left(\\frac{1}{3} e^{3 x}\\right)+C \\\\ ye^{3 x} & =2 e^{3 x}+C \\\\ y & =\\left(C + 2 e^{3 x}\\right) e^{- 3 x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=-4$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =\\frac{(2 e^{3 (0)})+C}{(e^{3 (0)})} \\\\ -4 & =\\frac{2+C}{1} \\\\ C & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=2 - 6 e^{- 3 x}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186745589 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1924ed73-759c-543e-9c44-e0e4e2b9095d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{- 4 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745569} {:answer/id #uuid "3cff3d24-e429-5c18-bff4-db352665d359" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{- 6 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745573} {:answer/id #uuid "c5105182-0bd7-5e74-a856-15b45284b7a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{- x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745586} {:answer/id #uuid "cea78b72-92a8-5eba-96ca-df475ac4aa1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{2 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745587}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186745587} :answer-field/id #uuid "5793ceb7-e2d5-5fb7-bfc4-0c1f53a95956" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745575} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01e511db-5495-5eae-afd7-6b7482e58937" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6 e^{2 x} - 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745567} {:answer/id #uuid "328839e1-bec6-51ae-8328-834f1896b9da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 2 e^{2 x} + 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745572} {:answer/id #uuid "9a5f074a-1b9a-5dc9-9b71-5e8462b871ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4 + 6 e^{- 2 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745580} {:answer/id #uuid "a824c390-4c2f-5dbf-b297-3a4de8857635" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 e^{- 2 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745581} {:answer/id #uuid "bedd19ad-3d27-57fc-8960-551a2bbe196a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4 - 2 e^{- 2 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745585}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186745585} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc2f1abc-2762-59de-b9df-c2879e7e760e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745582}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d7200314-8517-5cc6-b709-81ec8c578041" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\left(2\\right)y=8,\\quad y(0)=2\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\nAn integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\nThe solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=2$ and $Q(x)=8.$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =e^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =e^{\\int 2\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =e^{2 x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)=e^{2 x}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}e^{2 x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y) & =e^{2 x}\\cdot 8 \\\\ e^{2 x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2 e^{2 x}y & =8 e^{2 x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ye^{2 x}) & =8 e^{2 x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ye^{2 x})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 8 e^{2 x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ ye^{2 x} & =8\\left(\\frac{1}{2} e^{2 x}\\right)+C \\\\ ye^{2 x} & =4 e^{2 x}+C \\\\ y & =\\left(C + 4 e^{2 x}\\right) e^{- 2 x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=2$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =\\frac{(4 e^{2 (0)})+C}{(e^{2 (0)})} \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{4+C}{1} \\\\ C & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=4 - 2 e^{- 2 x}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186745600 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f31e9ddd-a90c-5cf1-a3c9-b1d88cc43dbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{70}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745603}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186745603} :answer-field/id #uuid "f933ad5f-f928-5b28-a101-65dc289f70c7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745604}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "bdd44f6b-eafd-543d-a1df-d18a28d5483e" :question/problem "Given that the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\mathbf{u}=\\langle a,5\\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{v}=\\langle -7,\\frac{3}{2}\\rangle$ equals zero, what is the value of $a$?\n\n$a=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Place the vectors in the columns of a matrix:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}a & -7 \\\\ 5 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nCompute its determinant:\n\n$$\n\\det(M)=a\\cdot\\frac{3}{2}-(-7)\\cdot5=\\frac{3a}{2}+35.\n$$\n\nSince the area is $|\\det(M)|$, zero area means the determinant is zero. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3a}{2}+35&=0 \\\\ \\frac{3a}{2}&=-35 \\\\ a&=-35\\cdot\\frac{2}{3}=-\\frac{70}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCheck: multiplying $\\mathbf{u}=\\langle -\\frac{70}{3},5\\rangle$ by $\\frac{3}{10}$ gives $\\mathbf{v}=\\langle -7,\\frac{3}{2}\\rangle$. The vectors are parallel, as required."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186745682 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32bf6865-7f55-5399-81b2-6712a4b37719" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-7-6z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745683} {:answer/id #uuid "6c288493-603c-59a9-abd0-586fd8e0839d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1+y+6z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745685} {:answer/id #uuid "800e3b74-bd23-59ff-9d25-35cbf486f955" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4-y-7z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745686} {:answer/id #uuid "837084de-a1cc-5e72-bd46-d7947ec43421" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5-7y+3z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745687} {:answer/id #uuid "d89af7ea-b0a1-5245-ad52-3f5ed8b317ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2-2y-2z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745688}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186745688} :answer-field/id #uuid "4cef9aee-6714-519a-b8de-9abfa2a61935" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745684}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "08e1ff1d-31d5-5a1b-993c-31dda7bd6f06" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x-4y-4z &=-4 \\\\ -x-2y-2z &=-2 \\\\ -x-2y-2z &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & -4 & -4 & -4 \\\\ -1 & -2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -2 & -2 & -2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nR_1:=(-\\frac{1}{2})R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -2 & -2 & -2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_2:=R_2+(1)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -2 & -2 & -2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_3:=R_3+(1)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+2z &=2 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z &=0 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z &=0\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final two equations, we can remove these equations from the system.\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$, and we have two free variables, $y$ and $z$. That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y$ and $z$.\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2-2y-2z \\\\ y &=y \\\\ z &=z\\end{aligned}\\right.,\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ and $z$ (the free variables) are arbitrary numbers.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2-2y-2z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in(-\\infty,\\infty).\n$$\n\n"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186745717 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "008f6588-feae-5baf-837f-b53538d485d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{5}{3}-\\frac{5}{3}y+\\frac{2}{3}z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745711} {:answer/id #uuid "014955ff-22c2-545b-8a99-b9ef90a62d35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{2}{3}y+\\frac{4}{3}z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745712} {:answer/id #uuid "76a2c8ff-4f94-595e-ab3f-f4ec44594974" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}y+\\frac{5}{3}z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745724} {:answer/id #uuid "cd9a0c2a-24dc-5664-9937-1d6daf5b0f06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}y-\\frac{7}{3}z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745732} {:answer/id #uuid "fff8e4cd-c49c-5cfe-b930-e9ff122b364d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{4}{3}y-\\frac{4}{3}z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745738}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186745732} :answer-field/id #uuid "6654f339-c98d-527d-8b16-554866a7b0a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745721}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "3b4cd886-94a4-5d05-bd79-6a2c5f186836" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x-2y-7z &=-1 \\\\ -3x-2y-7z &=-1 \\\\ 6x+4y+14z &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-3 & -2 & -7 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -7 & -1 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 14 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nR_1:=(-\\frac{1}{3})R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & \\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{7}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -3 & -2 & -7 & -1 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 14 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_2:=R_2+(3)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & \\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{7}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 14 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_3:=R_3+(-6)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & \\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{7}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+\\frac{2}{3}y+\\frac{7}{3}z &=\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0x+0y+0z &=0 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z &=0\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final two equations, we can remove these equations from the system.\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$, and we have two free variables, $y$ and $z$. That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y$ and $z$.\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}y-\\frac{7}{3}z \\\\ y &=y \\\\ z &=z\\end{aligned}\\right.,\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ and $z$ (the free variables) are arbitrary numbers.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}y-\\frac{7}{3}z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in(-\\infty,\\infty).\n$$\n\n"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186745718 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52fc04c7-8ae6-561f-9f09-06817f16c040" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{5}{2}y+\\frac{5}{2}z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745719} {:answer/id #uuid "84027e57-29cc-5c52-b3af-b30d73d08584" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}y+\\frac{3}{2}z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745726} {:answer/id #uuid "afb74399-7630-5e90-ac50-b8be718c792b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{5}{2}y-\\frac{1}{2}z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745729} {:answer/id #uuid "c2179ded-2413-5ea8-bca1-0063f7cadaf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{7}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}y-\\frac{7}{2}z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745731} {:answer/id #uuid "f7128a80-6900-5530-9a6f-50a65af30fd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{5}{2}+\\frac{7}{2}y-\\frac{3}{2}z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745736}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186745719} :answer-field/id #uuid "66411a97-fe17-5d8f-98d3-065a0a1a1011" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745720}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "4de08e1d-7568-5759-b38f-792320e8860e" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-4x-10y+10z &=-10 \\\\ 6x+15y-15z &=15 \\\\ -6x-15y+15z &=-15\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-4 & -10 & 10 & -10 \\\\ 6 & 15 & -15 & 15 \\\\ -6 & -15 & 15 & -15\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nR_1:=(-\\frac{1}{4})R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & \\frac{5}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} & \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 6 & 15 & -15 & 15 \\\\ -6 & -15 & 15 & -15\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_2:=R_2+(-6)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & \\frac{5}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} & \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -6 & -15 & 15 & -15\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_3:=R_3+(6)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & \\frac{5}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} & \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+\\frac{5}{2}y-\\frac{5}{2}z &=\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0x+0y+0z &=0 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z &=0\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final two equations, we can remove these equations from the system.\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$, and we have two free variables, $y$ and $z$. That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y$ and $z$.\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{5}{2}y+\\frac{5}{2}z \\\\ y &=y \\\\ z &=z\\end{aligned}\\right.,\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ and $z$ (the free variables) are arbitrary numbers.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{5}{2}y+\\frac{5}{2}z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in(-\\infty,\\infty).\n$$\n\n"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186745728 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06be88d9-5b33-5604-9e67-23fc29a8c929" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{5}{2}+\\frac{5}{2}y-\\frac{3}{2}z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745713} {:answer/id #uuid "084d7018-c45c-543d-9f39-5087272217f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{3}{2}y+\\frac{7}{2}z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745714} {:answer/id #uuid "2b3f5738-17f2-57d1-9bfb-b3ececf7e340" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{7}{2}y-\\frac{1}{2}z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745716} {:answer/id #uuid "6c008fc6-5a95-596a-bf32-21a75c1a625d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{7}{2}-\\frac{5}{2}y-\\frac{7}{2}z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745723} {:answer/id #uuid "9235765d-2471-5e40-ade7-347ed059795f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{7}{2}-\\frac{7}{2}y+\\frac{5}{2}z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745727}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186745713} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1c2db59-9093-554c-832d-f53cad077d7f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745734}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "9b6e9d65-9228-5135-a3a8-eac27c6ca3e1" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-6x+15y-9z &=-15 \\\\ -4x+10y-6z &=-10 \\\\ -2x+5y-3z &=-5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-6 & 15 & -9 & -15 \\\\ -4 & 10 & -6 & -10 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -3 & -5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nR_1:=(-\\frac{1}{6})R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -\\frac{5}{2} & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ -4 & 10 & -6 & -10 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -3 & -5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_2:=R_2+(4)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -\\frac{5}{2} & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -3 & -5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_3:=R_3+(2)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -\\frac{5}{2} & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-\\frac{5}{2}y+\\frac{3}{2}z &=\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0x+0y+0z &=0 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z &=0\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final two equations, we can remove these equations from the system.\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$, and we have two free variables, $y$ and $z$. That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y$ and $z$.\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=\\frac{5}{2}+\\frac{5}{2}y-\\frac{3}{2}z \\\\ y &=y \\\\ z &=z\\end{aligned}\\right.,\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ and $z$ (the free variables) are arbitrary numbers.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{5}{2}+\\frac{5}{2}y-\\frac{3}{2}z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in(-\\infty,\\infty).\n$$\n\n"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186745730 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10fdcda7-103c-574e-8b2a-a05f19dd7f32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}y-\\frac{7}{2}z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745715} {:answer/id #uuid "66ea643a-3a46-5636-8e4f-e24da5530667" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{7}{2}y-\\frac{1}{2}z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745722} {:answer/id #uuid "81ce8f0b-c6ff-5dbc-8bc8-82b1c2de7a43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{5}{2}y-\\frac{3}{2}z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745725} {:answer/id #uuid "de574bef-ba0e-5513-be9e-694b715607d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{7}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}y+\\frac{7}{2}z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745733} {:answer/id #uuid "f9c6e8e5-def0-51c7-917d-55d6b2c4a721" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{7}{2}-\\frac{7}{2}y+\\frac{5}{2}z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745737}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186745737} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee751920-2a1f-518d-9323-3ad5fd531f1d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186745735}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "b4fe7b9f-3fc5-5a67-9100-069b246ab956" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}6x+21y-15z &=-21 \\\\ 6x+21y-15z &=-21 \\\\ 4x+14y-10z &=-14\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}6 & 21 & -15 & -21 \\\\ 6 & 21 & -15 & -21 \\\\ 4 & 14 & -10 & -14\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nR_1:=(\\frac{1}{6})R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} & -\\frac{7}{2} \\\\ 6 & 21 & -15 & -21 \\\\ 4 & 14 & -10 & -14\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_2:=R_2+(-6)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} & -\\frac{7}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 14 & -10 & -14\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_3:=R_3+(-4)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} & -\\frac{7}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+\\frac{7}{2}y-\\frac{5}{2}z &=-\\frac{7}{2} \\\\ 0x+0y+0z &=0 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z &=0\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final two equations, we can remove these equations from the system.\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$, and we have two free variables, $y$ and $z$. That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y$ and $z$.\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-\\frac{7}{2}-\\frac{7}{2}y+\\frac{5}{2}z \\\\ y &=y \\\\ z &=z\\end{aligned}\\right.,\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ and $z$ (the free variables) are arbitrary numbers.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{7}{2}-\\frac{7}{2}y+\\frac{5}{2}z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in(-\\infty,\\infty).\n$$\n\n"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186746066 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c715496-d730-57ed-bf45-5d947811e1aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "16 \\ln|x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746063} {:answer/id #uuid "419184c9-886f-5cd4-994c-ea55e022b0cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 22 \\ln|x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746064} {:answer/id #uuid "86fd58a8-aa14-5c4f-80eb-af2dac708009" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "22 \\ln|x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746065} {:answer/id #uuid "f9380710-6602-5e2f-bb77-7110e1d3916c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 16 \\ln|x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746068} {:answer/id #uuid "fc957c01-40a5-5807-92f9-09626d90a42b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "19 \\ln|x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746069}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186746063} :answer-field/id #uuid "dcfe86f2-dccc-56a9-aaf0-8b876515928d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746067}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "bcc33fe4-cedb-525d-beb9-07b5fc4c8671" :question/problem "Find the integral of $19\\frac{\\sqrt{x^{1}}}{\\sqrt{x^{3}}}-3x^{-1}$ with respect to $x$." :question/worked-solution "Simplifying the exponents and applying the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int (19\\frac{\\sqrt{x^{1}}}{\\sqrt{x^{3}}}-3x^{-1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ &=19\\int \\frac{1}{x^{3/2-1/2}}\\,\\text{d}x - 3\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ &=19\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x - 3\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ &=16\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ &=16 \\ln|x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186746076 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7799179a-8d5e-51f3-8608-9f023142cb8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9 x - 12 \\ln|x| + \\frac{4}{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746071} {:answer/id #uuid "7f852fa3-6359-52c4-8063-c53cb9475edf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 9 x - 12 \\ln|x| + \\frac{4}{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746072} {:answer/id #uuid "97b852b4-40db-5822-8da6-39931081551f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9 x - 12 \\ln|x| - \\frac{4}{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746073} {:answer/id #uuid "c04fb58b-962e-5534-a5c1-9c6003436e68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 9 x - 12 \\ln|x| - \\frac{4}{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746074} {:answer/id #uuid "fc53836f-57e1-5e4a-8693-76b1b5a5fe19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "18 x - 24 \\ln|x| - \\frac{8}{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746077}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186746073} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8031e73-1570-5ae7-99f3-f287f527e09b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746075}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f411bdb7-37c4-5fb0-b44a-2f4f23897a8e" :question/problem "Find the integral of $\\left(3 - \\frac{2}{x}\\right)^2$ with respect to $x$." :question/worked-solution "Expanding the binomial and applying the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int \\left(3 - \\frac{2}{x}\\right)^2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ &=\\int (9 - \\frac{12}{x} + \\frac{4}{x^{2}})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ &=\\int 9\\,\\text{d}x - \\int \\frac{12}{x}\\,\\text{d}x + \\int \\frac{4}{x^2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ &=9\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x - 12\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x + 4\\int x^{-2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ &=9x - 12\\ln|x| + 4\\frac{x^{-2+1}}{-2+1}+C \\\\ &=9 x - 12 \\ln|x| - \\frac{4}{x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:answer/id #uuid "21155090-f5a4-5a04-bb38-a83b9c411ea1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x+\\frac{5}{2})^{2}+(y-\\frac{3}{2})^{2}=\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746142} {:answer/id #uuid "25206834-7aba-5fbf-869f-03050859872e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x+\\frac{3}{2})^{2}+(y+\\frac{5}{2})^{2}=\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746143} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186746144 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21155090-f5a4-5a04-bb38-a83b9c411ea1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x+\\frac{5}{2})^{2}+(y-\\frac{3}{2})^{2}=\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746142} {:answer/id #uuid "25206834-7aba-5fbf-869f-03050859872e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x+\\frac{3}{2})^{2}+(y+\\frac{5}{2})^{2}=\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746143} {:answer/id #uuid "867b0a5d-067a-57bb-b733-6b42ba6d1879" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x-\\frac{3}{2})^{2}+(y+\\frac{5}{2})^{2}=\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746152} {:answer/id #uuid "9a95c6b5-82e9-5ea5-94d7-a81c506c6ed6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x-\\frac{3}{2})^{2}+(y+\\frac{5}{2})^{2}=\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746153} {:answer/id #uuid "c8db3645-9831-5a05-a9af-d5e51e9dddab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x-\\frac{3}{2})^{2}+(y-\\frac{5}{2})^{2}=\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746158}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186746153} :answer-field/id #uuid "32b2b9d9-216f-59b3-9172-150e943b19a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746146}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "2922a2d5-4225-59f9-97b1-94da4d593cc6" :question/problem "![](images/6e/6ec40d37f7c8a8948fa5b26eb210021b8033d4b2babef38250d326a7d9318ca8.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the circle given above?" :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows center $C(\\frac{3}{2},- \\frac{5}{2})$ and radius $r=\\frac{3}{2}$. A circle with center $(a,b)$ and radius $r$ has equation\n\n$$\n(x-a)^2+(y-b)^2=r^2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the center and radius gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-\\frac{3}{2})^2+(y-\\left(- \\frac{5}{2}\\right))^2&=\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^2 \\\\ (x-\\frac{3}{2})^{2}+(y+\\frac{5}{2})^{2}&=\\frac{9}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubtract each center coordinate inside its squared term, and square the radius on the right."} {:answer/id #uuid "867b0a5d-067a-57bb-b733-6b42ba6d1879" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x-\\frac{3}{2})^{2}+(y+\\frac{5}{2})^{2}=\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746152} {:answer/id #uuid "9a95c6b5-82e9-5ea5-94d7-a81c506c6ed6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x-\\frac{3}{2})^{2}+(y+\\frac{5}{2})^{2}=\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746153} {:answer/id #uuid "c8db3645-9831-5a05-a9af-d5e51e9dddab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x-\\frac{3}{2})^{2}+(y-\\frac{5}{2})^{2}=\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746158} {:answer/id #uuid "148ff696-eaea-5a67-aace-fd6a4066f427" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x-\\frac{1}{2})^{2}+(y+\\frac{3}{2})^{2}=\\frac{17}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746296} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186746301 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "148ff696-eaea-5a67-aace-fd6a4066f427" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x-\\frac{1}{2})^{2}+(y+\\frac{3}{2})^{2}=\\frac{17}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746296} {:answer/id #uuid "661a4388-9886-55cb-bccf-5184bda23bbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x+\\frac{1}{2})^{2}+(y-\\frac{3}{2})^{2}=\\frac{17}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746302} {:answer/id #uuid "9094c267-7fd5-56e5-bb04-edca61d0289a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x-\\frac{1}{2})^{2}+(y+\\frac{3}{2})^{2}=\\frac{\\sqrt{34}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746307} {:answer/id #uuid "9888cc6f-3d62-5b7c-97aa-aad922acf0e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x+\\frac{1}{2})^{2}+(y+\\frac{3}{2})^{2}=\\frac{17}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746308} {:answer/id #uuid "e2a06781-bf82-59f0-8111-200739a70af3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x+\\frac{1}{2})^{2}+(y-\\frac{3}{2})^{2}=\\frac{\\sqrt{34}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746314}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186746302} :answer-field/id #uuid "d759b899-42ef-55a5-ae64-539c53e16ac0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746311}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "656a3186-7e91-5698-9009-105bd419ba01" :question/problem "![](images/56/5637c02732a27246d21c5630287c99098eccf4717ac4d94a0aa3029e5d002123.png)\n\nThe circle above is centered at $C(- \\frac{1}{2},\\frac{3}{2})$ and the point $X(1,-1)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^2+(y-b)^2=r^2.\n$$\n\nThe radius is the distance from $C$ to $X$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CX &=\\sqrt{(1-\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right))^2+(-1-\\frac{3}{2})^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^2+\\left(- \\frac{5}{2}\\right)^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{\\frac{17}{2}} \\\\ &=\\frac{\\sqrt{34}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute the center and the squared radius:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right))^2+(y-\\frac{3}{2})^2 &=\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{34}}{2}\\right)^2 \\\\ (x+\\frac{1}{2})^{2}+(y-\\frac{3}{2})^{2} &=\\frac{17}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:answer/id #uuid "661a4388-9886-55cb-bccf-5184bda23bbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x+\\frac{1}{2})^{2}+(y-\\frac{3}{2})^{2}=\\frac{17}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746302} {:answer/id #uuid "9094c267-7fd5-56e5-bb04-edca61d0289a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x-\\frac{1}{2})^{2}+(y+\\frac{3}{2})^{2}=\\frac{\\sqrt{34}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746307} {:answer/id #uuid "9888cc6f-3d62-5b7c-97aa-aad922acf0e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x+\\frac{1}{2})^{2}+(y+\\frac{3}{2})^{2}=\\frac{17}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746308} {:answer/id #uuid "e2a06781-bf82-59f0-8111-200739a70af3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x+\\frac{1}{2})^{2}+(y-\\frac{3}{2})^{2}=\\frac{\\sqrt{34}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746314} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186746374 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ca35bd7-385e-54f7-98d5-dfcdbec895c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746370} {:answer/id #uuid "6baf9fb0-b38e-5c74-96f9-46af35a711cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746371} {:answer/id #uuid "702ace46-1f13-5b69-a59d-f0ec20e58d47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746373} {:answer/id #uuid "a18cb5ce-d240-5366-be1d-95c7eae42c41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746375} {:answer/id #uuid "c0cbd2b6-b985-59eb-9f0b-2e942980d863" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746376}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186746373} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e691575-612c-5080-80ac-384c2bd5e42a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746372}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8cda404e-08cd-570d-a9ba-2a05b8c5b6cd" :question/problem "![](images/09/09a6c888fc799c6f8e061b5a5e26cd41e72c3ada3562f74552bb1f176938ce7c.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overline{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(2,0)$ and $(2,-4)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^2+(y-b)^2=r^2.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(2,0)$ and $Y(2,-4),$ we find that the length of the diameter is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{(2-2)^2+(0-(-4))^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(0)^2+(4)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{XY}{2}=\\frac{4}{2}=2.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, to find the center we use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{x_1+x_2}{2},\\frac{y_1+y_2}{2})=(\\frac{2+2}{2},\\frac{0+(-4)}{2})=(2,-2)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=2$ and center $(a,b)=(2,-2),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^2+(y-b)^2 & =r^2 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(y-(-2))^{2} & =(2)^2 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186746507 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15b62a0f-ae49-5fc4-9bdc-8e0293499531" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{2e}{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746506}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186746506} :answer-field/id #uuid "36facd63-2c83-5942-851a-5cc826296388" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746509}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "2504a178-a3b6-50db-97b2-8a8614ba3437" :question/problem "Given that $y=\\frac{-2e\\ln x}{5}$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Rewrite the constant denominator as a constant factor:\n\n$$\n\\frac{-2e\\ln x}{5}=-\\frac{2e}{5}\\ln x\n$$\n\nThe derivative of the natural logarithm is the reciprocal function:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\ln x)=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nApply the constant multiple rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{2e}{5}\\ln x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2e}{5}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\ln x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2e}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2e}{5x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186746508 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d00a04b6-cf2d-5220-ac02-9c4540f54d7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{10e}{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746515}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186746515} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd66e82e-d19c-5f02-b4d8-51a7ad04eeb1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746518}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "2850bf9b-a9e7-53e4-885f-d8144588fd88" :question/problem "Given that $y=\\frac{-10e\\ln x}{3}$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Rewrite the constant denominator as a constant factor:\n\n$$\n\\frac{-10e\\ln x}{3}=-\\frac{10e}{3}\\ln x\n$$\n\nThe derivative of the natural logarithm is the reciprocal function:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\ln x)=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nApply the constant multiple rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{10e}{3}\\ln x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{10e}{3}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\ln x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{10e}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{10e}{3x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186746510 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ada576b-5f15-5c65-bee0-2b83dacc5fb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4e}{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746504}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186746504} :answer-field/id #uuid "10a3f7ae-b7a0-5d97-88ab-bd9003764677" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746505}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "53d1d957-2cf6-58d4-ad8d-6a53eeb682ac" :question/problem "Give