27} {:answer/id #uuid "ca5ef06f-1ba9-507a-b957-67c58106344f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748331}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186748331} :answer-field/id #uuid "f237acb7-6045-560e-8466-8203a3e4c3df" :answer-field/key "$y=1 + \\frac{\\pi}{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748362} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b98761c-9c7f-558c-9c43-d528d467da4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748226} {:answer/id #uuid "84deefac-6bc4-5706-9ccf-c57bb40b9668" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748277}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186748277} :answer-field/id #uuid "fed39b0d-a6e9-5537-920a-d6dbe1ac1915" :answer-field/key "$y=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748369}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "86972ed0-fdb5-5c6a-a3da-dc7cbd5ab885" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\frac{dy}{dt}= \\\\ 2 \\sin{\\left(y - 1 \\right)}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following are equilibrium solutions? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "An equilibrium is a constant function $y(t)=c$. Set $dy/dt=0$ and test the resulting equation.\n\nTest whether $f(c)=0$, where\n\n$$\nf(c) = 2 \\sin{\\left(c - 1 \\right)}\n$$\n\n- For $c=- \\frac{\\pi}{2} + 1$: Use $\\sin{\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)}=-1$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}f(- \\frac{\\pi}{2} + 1)= \\\\ 2 \\sin{\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)} \\\\ =-2\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nThis is nonzero, so it is not an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $c=1$: Use $\\sin{\\left(0 \\right)}=0$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) &=2 \\sin{\\left(0 \\right)} \\\\ &=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is zero, so it is an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $c=1 + \\frac{\\pi}{2}$: Use $\\sin{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)}=1$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}f(1 + \\frac{\\pi}{2})= \\\\ 2 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)} \\\\ =2\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nThis is nonzero, so it is not an equilibrium solution.\n\nSelect $y=1$."}]
